window.NS_CONV_GUIDES = {
  "overview": "# Nintendo Switch v1 (Erista) \u2192 Clamshell Cyberdeck (`ns-conv`)\n\nA complete, reversible hardware conversion that transforms an unpatched first-generation **Nintendo Switch v1 (2017 Erista, `HAC-001`)** into a **translucent lilac clamshell cyberdeck** integrating a **Drop \u00d7 OLKB MIT Planck 40% ortholinear keyboard**, a **compact 38 mm USB HID trackball**, and an **internal slim UN 38.3 USB-C PD power bank**.\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Interactive 3D WebGL CAD Studio & All-in-One Documentation Portal:**\n> Open **[`docs/index.html`](docs/index.html)** (or visit the deployed GitHub Pages site) to spin the 3D cyberdeck, animate the clamshell lid (`0\u00b0\u2013125\u00b0`), explode all 7 OpenSCAD STL meshes, switch between all 6 premade SLA factory colors, and browse/search all 10 engineering guides in one interactive app!\n\n![Open Clamshell Cyberdeck Render](docs/renders/assembly_open_iso.png)\n\n| Exploded Assembly View | Closed Clamshell View (`0\u00b0`) |\n| :---: | :---: |\n| ![Exploded View](docs/renders/assembly_exploded.png) | ![Closed View](docs/renders/assembly_closed.png) |\n\n---\n\n## System Architecture Overview\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    subgraph LID[\"Upper Lid Assembly (Translucent Lilac SLA)\"]\n        SW_CORE[\"Switch v1 Core Assembly<br/>(LCD + Digitizer + Magnesium Midframe +<br/>Mainboard + Fan + 4310mAh Int. Battery)\"]\n        RCM_BTN[\"Recessed RCM Momentary Trigger<br/>(Right Rail Pin 10 \u2192 GND)\"]\n        RCM_BTN --> SW_CORE\n    end\n\n    subgraph HINGE[\"Torque-Balanced Dual Axis\"]\n        F_HINGE[\"2\u00d7 Friction Torque Hinges<br/>(~0.40 N\u00b7m combined, 100\u2013120\u00b0 hold)\"]\n        USBC_FPC[\"Flexible Coaxial USB-C 3.1 Ribbon<br/>(Strained-relieved through hinge channel)\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph BASE[\"Base Deck Assembly (Translucent Lilac SLA)\"]\n        HUB[\"Internal Compact USB-C PD Hub<br/>(PD 3.0 15V Pass-Through + 3\u00d7 USB 2.0/3.0 HID)\"]\n        PLANCK[\"Drop \u00d7 MIT Planck Keyboard<br/>(Recessed PCB + Plate, QMK 6KRO)\"]\n        TBALL[\"Integrated Trackball<br/>(Ploopy Nano 2 QMK / 38mm Ball)\"]\n        PBANK[\"Slim UN 38.3 USB-C PD Power Bank<br/>(15V/2.6A+ PD Output, Fused & Thermally Isolated)\"]\n        EXT_USBC[\"Rear Panel USB-C PD Input/Data Port<br/>(Payload Injection & Charging)\"]\n\n        PLANCK -->|USB 2.0 HID| HUB\n        TBALL -->|USB 2.0 HID| HUB\n        PBANK -->|15V USB-PD + Inline 5A Fuse| HUB\n        EXT_USBC <-->|Charging / RCM Injection| PBANK\n        EXT_USBC -.->|Direct Switch Mode / OTG| HUB\n    end\n\n    SW_CORE <-->|Bottom USB-C Port via Low-Profile 90\u00b0 Plug| USBC_FPC\n    USBC_FPC <--> HUB\n```\n\n### Core Design Principles\n\n1. **Zero-Destruction Reversibility:** The Switch's factory-bonded LCD, capacitive digitizer, die-cast magnesium midframe, thermal heatpipe/fan, and internal 4310 mAh battery remain intact as a single structural module inside the upper lid. No PCB traces are cut, and the risky LCD/digitizer adhesive separation is completely avoided.\n2. **No High-Speed MIPI DSI Extension Across the Hinge:** Prior art shows that passively extending the Switch's 53-pin MIPI DSI LCD ribbon across a hinge causes severe signal reflection and black-screen failures. Keeping the mainboard and display together in the lid means **only a single USB-C cable** crosses the hinge into the base.\n3. **Horizon OS Safety First & Mainline Chimera Linux 6.18 (`chimera-l4s`):** Stock `sysNAND` remains 100% unmodified for online play. Custom firmware (**Kefir `v927` AIO**) and Linux (**[`../chimera-l4s`](../chimera-l4s) \u2014 Chimera Linux `aarch64` with Linux `6.18.0-enigma-r20-erista+`** + optional **Switchroot L4T Ubuntu** rescue path) run strictly from the external microSD card (`emmc=0`, `LABEL=SWR-CHI` + `emuNAND` with `exosphere`/`dns.mitm` telemetry blanking).\n4. **Translucent Lilac Industrial 3D Printing:** All enclosure components are designed in parametric OpenSCAD (`cad/`) for **SLA Translucent Resin with custom Pantone Lilac dyeing** and clear UV-protective urethane coating via **PCBWay (`UTR-8100 Transparent`)** or **JLC3DP (`8001 Translucent`)**.\n\n---\n\n## Build Phase Status & Deliverables\n\nThis project is executed strictly phase-by-phase with user sign-off between phases:\n\n| Phase | Deliverable | Document / Path | GitHub Issue | Status |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **1** | **Research Summary** (Prior art, hardware verification, OS HID behavior, trackball & battery trade-offs) | [`docs/research.md`](docs/research.md) | [#1](https://github.com/JonasNowak/ns-conv/issues/1) | **Complete** |\n| **2** | **Bill of Materials (BOM)** (Every part, tool, consumable, EUR pricing, suppliers & alternatives) | [`docs/bom.md`](docs/bom.md) & [`hardware/BOM.csv`](hardware/BOM.csv) | [#2](https://github.com/JonasNowak/ns-conv/issues/2) | **Complete** |\n| **3** | **Teardown Plan** (Step-by-step Switch v1 & Drop Planck non-destructive disassembly) | [`docs/teardown.md`](docs/teardown.md) | [#3](https://github.com/JonasNowak/ns-conv/issues/3) | **Complete** |\n| **4** | **Electronics & Wiring Plan** (USB-C hub vs harness, PD power-bank topology, fusing, thermals) | [`docs/wiring.md`](docs/wiring.md) & [`hardware/`](hardware/) | [#4](https://github.com/JonasNowak/ns-conv/issues/4) | **Complete** |\n| **5** | **Parametric OpenSCAD CAD Package** (`config.scad`, lid, base, hinge brackets, jigs, STLs) | [`cad/`](cad/) & [`docs/cad-overview.md`](docs/cad-overview.md) | [#5](https://github.com/JonasNowak/ns-conv/issues/5) | **Complete** |\n| **6** | **3D Print Order Specification** (PCBWay / JLC3DP all 6 premade factory SLA color options & test-fit jig) | [`docs/print-spec.md`](docs/print-spec.md) | [#6](https://github.com/JonasNowak/ns-conv/issues/6) | **Complete** |\n| **7** | **Assembly Guide** (Step-by-step mechanical & electrical build, torque sequence, first boot) | [`docs/assembly.md`](docs/assembly.md) | [#7](https://github.com/JonasNowak/ns-conv/issues/7) | **Complete** |\n| **8** | **Software Setup Guide** (`../chimera-l4s` Linux 6.18 Enigma R20 + Kefir `v927` `emuNAND` + SD deployment script) | [`docs/software.md`](docs/software.md) & [`software/`](software/) | [#8](https://github.com/JonasNowak/ns-conv/issues/8) | **Complete** |\n| **9** | **Test & Acceptance Checklist** (Horizon OS, L4T Linux, USB HID, PD charging, thermals, hinges) | [`docs/testing.md`](docs/testing.md) | [#9](https://github.com/JonasNowak/ns-conv/issues/9) | **Complete** |\n| **10** | **Risk Register** (Top 10 technical, safety, and ban risks with mitigations) | [`docs/risks.md`](docs/risks.md) | [#10](https://github.com/JonasNowak/ns-conv/issues/10) | **Complete** |\n\n---\n\n## Exposed External Ports & Wireless Connectivity Summary\n\n- **Wi-Fi & Bluetooth (`BCM4356` 2\u00d72 MIMO 802.11ac 2.4/5 GHz + BT 4.1):** Both factory Switch `U.FL` coaxial cables and flat PCB patch antennas remain plugged into the mainboard and sit inside the **100% RF-transparent non-conductive SLA upper lid (`2.5 mm` wall)**, preserving full dual-band Wi-Fi and wireless Joy-Con / Bluetooth range in both Horizon OS and L4T Ubuntu Linux.\n- **Right-Side Flush I/O Window (`cad/base_bottom.scad`):** Exposes **`1\u00d7 USB-A 3.0 SuperSpeed (5 Gbps)` port** + **`1\u00d7 4K HDMI` output port** directly from the internal 5-in-1 USB-C PD hub (`HUB-01`) for external flash drives, SDR dongles, Ethernet adapters, or an external monitor.\n- **Rear Panel I/O (`cad/base_bottom.scad`):** Exposes **`1\u00d7 USB-C PD Charging Socket (`CAB-03`)`**, the **Recessed Center RCM / Direct Switch USB-C Coupler Pocket**, and the **Master Battery Cutoff Switch (`ELC-02`)**.\n- **Top & Bottom Lid I/O (`cad/lid_rear.scad`):** Exposes the Switch's native **Power button**, **Volume `+/-`**, **`3.5 mm` audio jack**, **Game Card slot**, **Top Heatsink Exhaust**, **Rear Intake Louvers**, **microSDXC slot**, and **Recessed RCM Momentary Pinhole Button (`RCM-01`)**.\n\n---\n\n## Repository Structure\n\n```text\nns-conv/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 README.md                 # Project overview, architecture, and build phase tracker\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 docs/\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 research.md           # Phase 1: Prior art, donor verification & subsystem trade-offs\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 bom.md                # Phase 2: Bill of Materials & EUR budget (AliExpress vs DE)\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 teardown.md           # Phase 3: Non-destructive Switch v1 & Planck teardown\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 wiring.md             # Phase 4: Internal USB-C hub, PD power bank & fusing plan\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 cad-overview.md       # Phase 5: Dimensioned CAD overview & verification checklist\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 print-spec.md         # Phase 6: PCBWay / JLC3DP premade SLA print specification\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 assembly.md           # Phase 7: Mechanical assembly & first power-on guide\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 software.md           # Phase 8: Full software guide (../chimera-l4s Linux 6.18 + Kefir v927)\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 testing.md            # Phase 9: Test & acceptance checklist\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 risks.md              # Phase 10: Top 10 risk register & recovery playbooks\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 renders/              # OpenSCAD PNG renders of all 7 parts + open/closed/exploded views\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 cad/                      # Phase 5: Parametric OpenSCAD sources, Makefile, STLs & 3MFs\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 hardware/                 # BOM.csv, wiring-diagram.mmd, and component datasheets.md\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 software/                 # deploy-chimera-kefir-sd.sh staging script & chimera-l4s integration\n```\n",
  "phase1_research": "# Phase 1: Research Summary \u2014 Nintendo Switch v1 Clamshell Cyberdeck (`ns-conv`)\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\nThis document establishes the engineering baseline, prior-art evaluation, donor verification protocol, and subsystem trade-offs for converting an unpatched **2017 Nintendo Switch v1 (Erista, `HAC-001`)** into a reversible, dual-booting (**Horizon OS + Switchroot L4T Ubuntu**) **clamshell cyberdeck** housed in a custom **translucent lilac SLA-printed enclosure**.\n\n### Key Architectural Decisions Validated by Research\n1. **Mainboard + Display Stay Together in the Lid:** Separating the Switch's 6.2\" LCD from its mainboard requires extending a 53-pin high-speed MIPI DSI ribbon across a hinge\u2014a major failure point in prior art due to signal reflection and mechanical fatigue. Keeping the Switch's factory-bonded LCD, digitizer, die-cast magnesium midframe, mainboard, cooling fan, and 4310 mAh battery as a unified core inside the lid means **only a single flexible USB-C connection crosses the hinge**.\n2. **100% Reversible, Non-Destructive Mod:** Only the Switch's outer plastic rear cover and detachable Left/Right Joy-Con rails are unbolted. The 10 precision M2 threaded bosses along the left and right edges of the Switch's metal midframe (originally holding the Joy-Con rails) serve as structural mounting anchors inside the custom lid shell.\n3. **Planck QMK Must Run in 6KRO Mode for Horizon OS:** Stock Horizon OS natively supports standard USB HID keyboards for text entry and compatible games, **but only via the 6-Key Rollover (6KRO) USB HID descriptor**. Enabling NKRO in QMK causes Horizon OS to ignore the keyboard; L4T Ubuntu supports both 6KRO and NKRO natively.\n4. **Thermoset SLA Resin Fastening Strategy:** Translucent lilac is achieved via **clear SLA resin (`PCBWay UTR-8100 Transparent` or `JLC3DP 8001 Translucent`) + custom Pantone lilac immersion dyeing + UV-resistant clear urethane coat**. Because SLA resin is a *thermoset* (it chars/cracks under a hot soldering iron rather than melting like FDM PLA/ABS), screw bosses must use **captive hex nuts, factory-tapped threads, or bonded/cold-press knurled brass inserts** rather than thermal heat-set inserts.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Donor Hardware Verification (Pre-Disassembly Protocol)\n\nBefore purchasing parts or loosening a single screw on the donor console, the user **must verify** that the Switch is an unpatched **Erista (`HAC-001`)** vulnerable to the `fusee-gelee` coldboot BootROM exploit.\n\n### 2.1 Model & Serial Number Check\n1. **Check the Model Number on the Rear Shell:**\n   - **Valid:** `MOD. HAC-001` (2017\u2013mid-2018 Erista Tegra X1 `T210`).\n   - **Invalid:** `MOD. HAC-001(-01)` (2019+ Mariko Tegra X1+ `T214`\u2014patched BootROM, incompatible with `fusee-gelee`).\n2. **Verify the Serial Number (Sticker on Bottom Edge AND in `System Settings \u2192 System \u2192 Serial Information`):**\n   *Always verify the serial number inside `System Settings` to rule out a swapped plastic backplate.*\n\n| Region Prefix | Unpatched (Guaranteed Vulnerable) | Potentially Patched (Mixed Transition Batch) | Patched (Not Vulnerable to `fusee-gelee`) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **XAW1** (NA) | `XAW10000000000` \u2013 `XAW10074000000` | `XAW10074000000` \u2013 `XAW10120000000` | `> XAW10120000000` |\n| **XAW4** (NA) | `XAW40000000000` \u2013 `XAW40011000000` | `XAW40011000000` \u2013 `XAW40012000000` | `> XAW40012000000` |\n| **XAW7** (NA) | `XAW70000000000` \u2013 `XAW70017800000` | `XAW70017800000` \u2013 `XAW70030000000` | `> XAW70030000000` |\n| **XAJ1** (EU/JP) | `XAJ10000000000` \u2013 `XAJ10020000000` | `XAJ10020000000` \u2013 `XAJ10030000000` | `> XAJ10030000000` |\n| **XAJ4** (EU/JP) | `XAJ40000000000` \u2013 `XAJ40046000000` | `XAJ40046000000` \u2013 `XAJ40060000000` | `> XAJ40060000000` |\n| **XAJ7** (EU/JP) | `XAJ70000000000` \u2013 `XAJ70040000000` | `XAJ70040000000` \u2013 `XAJ70050000000` | `> XAJ70050000000` |\n\n*Cross-reference tool:* [ismyswitchpatched.com](https://ismyswitchpatched.com/) and the [NH Switch Guide Serial Reference](https://nh-server.github.io/switch-guide/user_guide/getting_started/).\n\n### 2.2 Mandatory Live RCM (`fusee-gelee`) Test Before Disassembly\nEven if the serial number falls in the \"Unpatched\" range, a refurbished unit could have a replacement motherboard. Perform this non-invasive test before teardown:\n1. Power the Switch completely **OFF** (hold Power for 3 seconds \u2192 *Power Options* \u2192 *Turn Off*).\n2. Slide a plastic **RCM Jig** into the **Right Joy-Con rail** (bridging Pin 10 `HOME/RCM` to Ground Pin 1/7). *Never use a bent metal paperclip, which can bend Pin 9 (`+5V`) onto Pin 10 and fry the rail controller.*\n3. Hold **Volume Up (`+`)** and press **Power** once. The screen will remain **completely black** (this is normal in Recovery Mode).\n4. Connect the Switch via USB-C to a PC/Mac/Linux host:\n   - **macOS/Linux:** Run `lsusb` or check `ioreg -p IOUSB` for `NVIDIA Corp. APX` (`VID:PID 0955:7321`).\n   - Inject the `hekate` payload using `fusee-nano`, `Rekado` (Android), or `WebFG` / `TegraRcmGUI`.\n5. **Pass Criteria:**\n   - Payload Smash returns `0x7000` bytes transferred and the Switch display lights up into the **Hekate graphical bootloader menu**.\n   - While in this pre-teardown check, test **touchscreen digitizer responsiveness**, **Wi-Fi/Bluetooth**, **microSD card reader**, **fan spin**, and **15V USB-C PD fast charging** in both USB-C connector orientations.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Prior Art Survey: What to Copy vs. What to Avoid\n\nWe surveyed existing Nintendo Switch clamshell/laptop conversions and Planck-based 40% ortholinear cyberdecks to identify proven mechanical patterns and avoid known dead ends.\n\n| Prior Art Project / Category | Architecture Summary | Techniques to COPY | Mistakes to AVOID & Why |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Switch MIPI-Extension Clamshell Mods** *(GBA-SP style / split-board discussions on GBAtemp & Reddit `r/SwitchHacks`)* | Attempts to place the Switch mainboard in the base half and run extended 53-pin LCD MIPI DSI, 34-pin digitizer, and 4-pin backlight ribbons through a hinge to the lid. | None for the display bus. | **AVOID extending the 53-pin MIPI DSI ribbon.** MIPI DSI uses multi-gigabit low-voltage differential signaling without re-timers. Even a 10 cm passive FPC extension introduces severe impedance mismatch, EMI, and black-screen failures. |\n| **Full Front-Housing / OLED Unbonding Swaps** *(eXtremeRate full shell swaps, Retro Remake Super5)* | Heating the front bezel to 80\u00b0C and prying the glued glass digitizer, LCD panel, and LiPo battery out of the stock magnesium midframe. | Reusing OEM M2 screw boss patterns for drop-in alignment. | **AVOID unbonding the LCD/digitizer or prying out the glued LiPo battery.** Prying the digitizer risks cracking the glass or trapping dust on the LCD; prying the glued 4310 mAh battery risks cell puncture and thermal runaway. |\n| **Switch Clamshell / \"Switch SP\" Tablet-in-Lid Builds** *(Bob Wulff / Printables / MakerWorld)* | Houses the intact Switch tablet core in the upper lid and routes a low-profile 90\u00b0 USB-C OTG cable to the base controller/keyboard. | **COPY tablet-in-lid architecture** and low-profile 90\u00b0 right-angle USB-C plug with printed mechanical strain relief. | Avoid bulky consumer docks or unshielded 3D-printed PLA friction hinges that wear loose after ~50 cycles. |\n| **Planck 40% Ortholinear Cyberdecks** *(READY! Model 100, Penkesu Computer, Yarh.io, `r/cyberDeck` Planck builds)* | Recesses a `233 \u00d7 81 mm` Planck plate/PCB assembly into the top deck above a flat battery/hub bay, using constant-torque metal laptop hinges. | **COPY recessed Planck top-plate mounting**, constant-torque metal friction hinges (`Southco E6` / `Sugatsune`), and placing the heavy power bank in the base for a low center of gravity. | Avoid routing rigid round USB cables through hinge knuckles; use flat flexible USB-C ribbon cables with dedicated service loops. |\n\n### Resulting Mechanical Strategy for `ns-conv`\n- **Upper Lid:** Retains the Switch v1 **front bezel + glass digitizer + LCD + die-cast magnesium midframe + mainboard + heatpipe/fan + speakers + stock 4310 mAh battery** as a single untouched factory sub-assembly (`~265 g` once the plastic backplate and metal Joy-Con rails are unscrewed).\n- **Structural Lid Anchoring:** The Switch's magnesium midframe has **5\u00d7 M2 threaded holes on the left edge** and **5\u00d7 M2 threaded holes on the right edge** (originally securing the Joy-Con rails), plus the rear backplate screw bosses. Our translucent lilac SLA lid bolts directly into these 10 metal-threaded side holes via internal aluminum/printed brackets tied directly to the metal friction hinges.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Keyboard Integration: Drop \u00d7 MIT Planck (40% Ortholinear)\n\n### 4.1 Mechanical & PCB Specifications\n- **Footprint (PCB & Switch Plate):** `233.0 mm \u00d7 81.0 mm` (official OLKB / Drop Planck specification; source: [`olkb/olkb_parts`](https://github.com/olkb/olkb_parts)).\n- **Key Matrix:** 4 rows \u00d7 12 columns (47 keys in MIT layout with a central `2u` spacebar on the bottom row; `19.05 mm` standard MX key spacing).\n- **Z-Height Stackup:**\n  - Switch plate top to PCB bottom: `~10.8 mm` (`1.5 mm` plate + `3.5 mm` switch housing to PCB + `1.6 mm` PCB + `~4.2 mm` SMD components/hotswap sockets and USB-C receptacle clearance).\n  - Keycap height above plate: `~8.5 mm` (DSA/XDA) to `~11.5 mm` (OEM/MT3).\n- **Mounting Holes (M2 Standoffs between Plate & PCB \u2192 Case):**\n  - Standard Drop Planck Rev 6 (Lo-Pro / Mid-Pro / Hi-Pro) uses M2 standoffs sandwiched between the switch plate and PCB, with through-holes in the PCB accepting M2 screws from the case floor.\n  - Typical OLKB Rev 6 mounting coordinates (measured from top-left PCB corner, to be verified against the user's exact revision in Phase 3/5):\n    - Left/Right pair: `(21.5 mm, 21.5 mm)`, `(211.5 mm, 21.5 mm)`, `(21.5 mm, 59.5 mm)`, `(211.5 mm, 59.5 mm)` and center `(116.5 mm, 40.5 mm)`.\n  - Additionally, our base enclosure CAD will include a **full perimeter support ledge (`1.5 mm` shelf supporting the edges of the `233 \u00d7 81 mm` switch plate)** plus slotted M2 bottom mounting bosses so both Drop Lo-Pro and Hi-Pro Planck revisions drop in without modification.\n\n### 4.2 USB HID Behavior in Horizon OS vs. Switchroot L4T Ubuntu\n\n| Feature / Scenario | Stock / CFW Horizon OS | Switchroot L4T Ubuntu (Linux) | Engineering Requirement / Workaround |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **USB Enumeration** | Native USB HID Boot/Report Keyboard driver (`hid` sysmodule). | Native Linux kernel `usbhid` / `libinput` driver. | **CRITICAL:** Horizon OS **only supports 6KRO (6-Key Rollover)**. If QMK `NKRO` is active, the keyboard will not respond in Horizon OS! Toggle QMK to 6KRO (`Magic + N` or `NKRO_ENABLE = no`). |\n| **System Text Input** *(Wi-Fi passwords, eShop, naming, chat)* | **100% Supported Natively.** Typing on the Planck immediately fills any Horizon OS on-screen keyboard prompt. | **100% Supported Natively** across all desktop apps, terminal, browsers, and login prompt. | Works out of the box in 6KRO mode. |\n| **In-Game Keyboard Input** | Works natively in games with USB keyboard support (*Minecraft*, *Quake*, *Doom*, *Skyrim* naming, *Factorio*, *Monster Hunter* chat). | Works natively in all Linux games, Steam/Box64 titles, and emulators. | None required for keyboard-aware titles. |\n| **Horizon OS Home Menu Navigation / Controller-Only Games** | **Not supported via standard USB Keyboard HID.** Stock Horizon OS requires a gamepad input or touchscreen to navigate the Home menu. | Full desktop/window navigation via keyboard shortcuts. | **Conflict & Honest Workaround:** In stock Horizon OS, use the capacitive touchscreen or a wirelessly paired Joy-Con/Pro Controller (or on `emuNAND` CFW, install the [`sys-con`](https://github.com/o0Zz/sys-con) sysmodule or flash a secondary QMK/GP2040-CE gamepad descriptor). |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Trackball Selection & Integration Research\n\nBecause Horizon OS and L4T Linux sit in a compact clamshell base alongside a `233 \u00d7 81 mm` Planck keyboard, we evaluated four off-the-shelf USB HID trackball solutions against footprint, height, open-source CAD availability, and dual-OS compatibility.\n\n### 5.1 Candidate Comparison\n\n| Candidate | Dimensions (`L \u00d7 W \u00d7 H`) | Ball \u00d8 | MCU / Sensor / Firmware | Buttons | Pros & Cons for `ns-conv` |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **1. Ploopy Nano 2 (Recommended \u2014 Side or Top-Right Mount)** | `62 \u00d7 54 \u00d7 49 mm` (or `~48 \u00d7 48 \u00d7 36 mm` bare PCB + integrated socket) | `38.0 mm` (1.5\") | RP2040 + PAW-3222 Optical Sensor, **QMK / VIA** (USB-C) | Via Planck QMK keys (or 2 added MX switches) | **Best ergonomics & open-source CAD.** Full 38 mm finger ball; STEP files on GitHub (`ploopyco/nano-trackball`); standard USB HID mouse. Left/Right/Middle click & Drag-Scroll sit right under the thumb on the Planck bottom row. |\n| **2. Perixx PERIPRO-506 / Industrial 14mm USB Trackball Module (Recommended \u2014 Palm-Rest Mount)** | `~45 \u00d7 45 \u00d7 22 mm` module | `14.0 mm` / `16.0 mm` | Integrated USB 2.0 HID optical/laser controller | 2 integrated microswitches (L/R click) | **Best low-profile option (`22 mm` tall).** Fits centered in a narrow front palm rest below the Planck spacebar without adding width to the deck. |\n| **3. ProtoArc EM04 / Perixx PERIMICE-517 (Decased Thumb Trackball)** | `~133 \u00d7 100 \u00d7 45 mm` (stock shell) | `34.0 mm` | Proprietary USB / 2.4GHz / BT PCB | 5 buttons + scroll wheel | Requires destructive decasing of an irregularly shaped consumer PCB; adds `~85 mm` width to the right of the Planck. |\n| **4. Pimoroni Trackball Breakout (`PIM447`)** | `25 \u00d7 22 \u00d7 9.5 mm` | `4.5 mm` | Nuvoton I2C slave (`0x0A`), RGBW LED + click | Push-to-click | **Not standalone USB.** Requires soldering 4 I2C wires to the Planck PCB and compiling custom QMK firmware; tiny 4.5 mm ball fatigues fingers during desktop Linux use. |\n\n### 5.2 Recommendation & Layout Options\nWe recommend **Ploopy Nano 2** as the primary choice (mounted to the right of the Planck keyboard in a dedicated socket, creating a comfortable right-hand finger trackball layout with Left/Right click on the Planck's bottom-right keys or two flanking choc/MX switches), **OR** a **low-profile 14\u201319 mm panel-mount USB HID optical trackball module** if you prefer a narrower symmetrical deck (`~255 mm` total width) with the trackball centered below the spacebar. *(See Open Questions at the end of this document to lock in your preference before CAD.)*\n\n### 5.3 Trackball OS Behavior\n- **Switchroot L4T Ubuntu:** Standard USB HID Mouse descriptor works immediately at boot (cursor, left/right/middle click, and QMK drag-scrolling).\n- **Horizon OS:** Stock Horizon OS has **no mouse pointer in the Home Menu** (pointer actions use the capacitive touchscreen), **but** games that implement Nintendo's `Mouse` HID API (*Quake*, *Doom I/II/64*, *Factorio*, *Game Builder Garage*, *Hypnospace Outlaw*, *Minecraft* Bedrock, *Mario Paint* NSO) natively recognize a standard USB HID trackball!\n\n---\n\n## 6. Additional Battery (Slim USB-C PD Power Bank) & Charging Topology\n\n### 6.1 Switch v1 Power Delivery Requirements\nThe Switch v1 (`HAC-001`) uses a **ROHM `BM92T36` USB-PD controller** paired with a **Texas Instruments `BQ24193` battery charger IC**.\n- For maximum charging speed while playing (up to `~18W` total draw), the power source **must advertise a `15V` USB-PD Fixed PDO (`15V @ 2.6A` or `15V @ 3.0A`)**.\n- Standard 5V/9V banks charge slowly (`~7.5W` max) and allow the internal battery to drain during heavy CPU/GPU workloads in L4T Ubuntu.\n\n### 6.2 Comparison of Candidate Slim UN 38.3 USB-C PD Power Banks\n\nAll candidates below are factory-sealed commercial lithium-polymer packs certified to **UN 38.3**, **CE**, **FCC**, and **UL 2056**:\n\n| Model | Capacity | Dimensions (`L \u00d7 W \u00d7 H`) | Weight | USB-C PD Output (15V PDO) | Pass-Through Support | Fit & Verdict for Base Half |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **1. Baseus Blade HD 100W (`PPBLD100-HD`) \u2014 Recommended Primary** | `20,000 mAh` (`74 Wh`) | **`134 \u00d7 134 \u00d7 18.0 mm`** | `445 g` | `2\u00d7 USB-C` (up to `100W`, includes **`15V/3A`** & `20V/5A`), `2\u00d7 USB-A` | **Yes** (simultaneous 60W in / 30W\u201345W out; briefly renegotiates on plug/unplug) | **Best Z-Height (`18.0 mm`) & Capacity.** Sits completely flat underneath the Planck keyboard tray (`233 \u00d7 81 mm`), adding ~3.5\u00d7 runtime (`~92 Wh` total system energy with Switch's `16 Wh` battery). |\n| **2. Baseus Blade 100W Original (`PPBLD100-S`)** | `20,000 mAh` (`74 Wh`) | `162 \u00d7 143 \u00d7 18.0 mm` | `490 g` | `2\u00d7 USB-C` (`100W`, **`15V/3A`**), `2\u00d7 USB-A` | **Yes** | Equally thin (`18.0 mm`), requires `~20 mm` deeper base enclosure than the Blade HD (`143 mm` vs `134 mm`). |\n| **3. INIU B62 / P50-E1 45W Slim (Lightweight Alternative)** | `10,000 mAh` (`37 Wh`) | `~110 \u00d7 68 \u00d7 18.5 mm` | `~210 g` | `USB-C` (`45W` PD, **`15V/3A`**) | **Yes** | Half the weight and footprint of the Baseus Blade HD (`+1.8\u00d7` runtime extension). Ideal if keeping total cyberdeck weight under `1.1 kg` is prioritized over maximum battery life. |\n| **4. Anker 537 PowerCore 24K 65W (`A1379`)** | `24,000 mAh` (`86.4 Wh`) | `160 \u00d7 85 \u00d7 26.5 mm` | `500 g` | `2\u00d7 USB-C` (`65W` PD, **`15V/3A`**) | **No** (disables USB-C PD output while charging via USB-C1) | Too thick (`26.5 mm` adds 8.5 mm to base height) and lacks USB-C-to-USB-C pass-through. **Eliminated.** |\n\n### 6.3 Charging, Data & Safety Architecture\nTo allow a **single external USB-C port** to charge the cyberdeck while also allowing direct USB-C connection to the Switch (for initial RCM payload injection or Hekate USB Mass Storage access to the microSD card without opening the lid):\n1. **Normal Operating & Pass-Through Mode:**\n   - The **Switch's bottom USB-C port** plugs via a custom-clamped low-profile 90\u00b0 right-angle USB-C ribbon cable into the upstream port of a **compact internal USB-C PD 3.0 Hub** in the base.\n   - The **Planck keyboard** and **Trackball** plug into two of the hub's USB 2.0/3.0 downstream HID ports.\n   - The **Baseus Blade HD (`USB-C2 Out`)** feeds the hub's **USB-C PD Power-In port** through a **panel-accessible High-Current Slide Switch** and an **inline 5A Fast-Acting Blade/Cartridge Fuse**. This lets you turn off power-bank charging when the Switch internal battery is full or stored, preventing continuous trickle-charge wear.\n   - The **Baseus Blade HD (`USB-C1 In/Out`)** connects to a rear panel-mount **External Charging USB-C Port**. Plugging a 65W+ wall charger into the rear port recharges the Baseus Blade HD while simultaneously passing power through to the Switch.\n2. **RCM Payload Injection / USB Device Mode:**\n   - Because `fusee-gelee` RCM payload injection requires the Switch to act as a **USB Device (`APX 0955:7321`)** rather than a USB Host (a USB-C hub places the Switch in Host mode via `CC` pull-down `Rd`), we will evaluate two clean options in Phase 4 (Wiring):\n     - **Option 1 (Internal Switchable USB-C 2:1 Mux / Short Extension Header):** A small rear access port or DPDT/USB-C mux switch that switches the Switch's USB-C port between the Internal Hub (Normal Host Mode) and External Port / Dongle (RCM Device Mode).\n     - **Option 2 (Internal Zero-Solder RCM Dongle Docked in Lid/Base):** An off-the-shelf USB-C payload injector (e.g., RCMLoader One or an RP2040-Tiny flashed with `fusee-nano`) connected on the Switch USB-C line during the first 2 seconds of boot before the hub enumerates.\n3. **Mandatory Thermal & Mechanical Safety Rules:**\n   - **Certification:** Only factory-sealed UN 38.3 certified packs (Baseus Blade HD or INIU 45W).\n   - **Fastener Clearance:** Minimum `3.5 mm` clearance between the power bank casing and any screw tip, standoff, or metal edge; an unbroken `2.0 mm` SLA barrier wall plus `1.5 mm` flame-retardant Poron/silicone foam pads isolate the battery bay from the Planck PCB above it.\n   - **Thermal Isolation:** Because the Switch mainboard resides in the **upper lid** and the power bank resides in the **lower base**, the two heat sources are physically separated across the air gap of the clamshell! Dedicated bottom intake slots and rear exhaust louvers cool the power bank bay passively.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Boot Selection & Console Preservation Without Joy-Cons\n\nSince the Switch is mounted inside the upper lid without removable Joy-Cons attached to the sides, boot navigation and RCM entry must work reliably using only hardware accessible on the deck:\n\n1. **Entering RCM (`fusee-gelee`) Non-Destructively:**\n   - We do **not** use `AutoRCM` (which modifies `BOOT0` on `sysNAND` and prevents normal stock cold-booting without a payload injector).\n   - Instead, a tiny **Right-Rail RCM Flex Adapter (or modified replacement Right Joy-Con rail ribbon)** connects to the Switch's Right Joy-Con ZIF header (or slides into the preserved Right rail inside the lid bezel) and routes **Pin 10 (`RCM`)** and **Pin 1 (`GND`)** to a recessed **momentary tactile \"RCM Boot\" button** on the upper lid edge.\n   - **To boot pure Stock Horizon OS (`sysNAND`):** Simply press **Power** (do not hold the RCM button). The Switch boots 100% untouched stock firmware for safe online play.\n   - **To boot Hekate (`Kefir CFW emuNAND` or `Switchroot L4T Ubuntu`):** Hold **[RCM Button] + [Volume Up]** and press **Power**, then inject `hekate`.\n2. **Navigating the Boot Menu Without Joy-Cons:**\n   - **Hekate Nyx GUI** has **full native capacitive touchscreen support**! Once Hekate boots, the user simply taps **Launch \u2192 Kefir emuNAND** or **More Configs \u2192 Switchroot L4T Ubuntu** directly on the Switch screen.\n   - Even if Nyx GUI is missing (`hekate` text menu fallback), Hekate navigates completely using **`Volume +` (Up)**, **`Volume -` (Down)**, and **`Power` (Select)**\u2014all three buttons remain directly accessible through precision cutouts (with printed actuator caps) on the top edge of our upper lid shell!\n\n---\n\n## 8. Materials & Manufacturing Research: Translucent Lilac 3D Printing\n\n### 8.1 Process & Material Selection (PCBWay vs. JLC3DP)\nNeither SLA nor MJF offers a pre-tinted \"translucent lilac\" raw resin vat. Industrial prototyping bureaus produce translucent colored enclosures by printing in **optically clear SLA photopolymer resin** followed by **heated immersion dyeing** and a **UV-protective clear urethane topcoat**:\n\n| Parameter | **PCBWay (Recommended for Turnkey Lilac Dyeing)** | **JLC3DP (Budget Alternative \u2014 Clear or DIY Dye)** |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Process** | **SLA (Stereolithography)** | **SLA (Stereolithography)** |\n| **Material** | **`UTR-8100 (Transparent)`** or **`UTR-8100 (Translucent)`** | **`8001 Translucent Resin`** |\n| **Color / Dyeing** | Select **Surface Finish \u2192 Dyeing \u2192 Custom Color** and specify **Pantone `2577 C` or `2645 C` (Translucent Lilac / Pastel Purple)** in order notes. | `8001` ships clear/slightly cool-tinted with **Clear Oil Spraying**. *(JLC3DP does not offer custom Pantone translucent purple dyeing in its automated checkout; requires either DIY Rit DyeMore Synthetic *Royal Purple* dip prior to clear-coat, or ordering from PCBWay).* |\n| **Surface Finish** | **Polishing + Dyeing + Clear Glossy or Semi-Matte Acrylic/Urethane Spray** (prevents UV yellowing and yields a frosted or glass-like Game Boy Atomic Purple / Lilac look). | **Sanding + Clear Oil Spraying** (Translucent finish). |\n| **Dimensional Tolerance** | `\u00b10.10 mm` (for features `<100 mm`) or `\u00b10.15%` (`~\u00b10.38 mm` across a `255 mm` shell). | `\u00b10.15 mm` or `\u00b10.20%` (`~\u00b10.50 mm` across a `255 mm` shell). |\n| **Layer Height** | `0.05 mm` (`50 \u00b5m`) high-resolution or `0.10 mm` standard. | `0.10 mm` (`100 \u00b5m`). |\n| **Min. Wall Thickness** | `0.8 mm` unsupported (`2.2\u20132.5 mm` recommended for structural laptop shells to prevent post-cure warp and keep uniform color saturation). | `1.0 mm` minimum (`2.5 mm` recommended for large flat enclosures). |\n\n### 8.2 Designing Parametric OpenSCAD for Translucent SLA Resin\n- **Uniform Wall Thickness (`2.5 mm` nominal):** Because immersion dye penetrates the outer `~0.3\u20130.5 mm` surface layer and light transmits through the bulk cross-section, sudden jumps from `1.5 mm` to `8.0 mm` solid blocks create dark blotches. We will core out thick structural ribs (`1.8 mm` rib thickness = `~70%` of nominal wall) so the translucent lilac tint looks even throughout.\n- **Fastener Strategy for Thermoset Resin:** Standard thermal heat-set inserts designed for FDM thermoplastics **crack SLA thermoset resin** if pressed in with a hot iron. Instead, all screw joints in `cad/` will use:\n  1. **Hex-nut trap pockets (`DIN 934` M2, M2.5, and M3 stainless steel nuts)** for high-torque structural joints (hinges and Switch midframe brackets), which are visible as clean mechanical details through the translucent lilac shell, AND\n  2. **Cold-press / epoxy-bonded knurled brass inserts** (or PCBWay factory-tapped threads) for blind standoffs.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Preliminary Ergonomics, Hinge Torque & Mass Budget\n\n### 9.1 Lid Mass & Hinge Torque Calculation\nTo ensure the upper lid holds any angle between **100\u00b0 and 120\u00b0** without drooping during typing or lifting the base when opening:\n\n1. **Upper Lid Mass ($m_{\\text{lid}}$):**\n   - Switch v1 core without plastic backplate and metal Joy-Con rails: `~265 g`\n   - Custom SLA Upper Lid Shell + Front Bezel Retainer + RCM Button assembly: `~95 g`\n   - Internal Steel Hinge Arms + M2/M3 Fasteners + USB-C right-angle connector: `~30 g`\n   - **Total Lid Mass ($m_{\\text{lid}}$):** $\\approx \\mathbf{390\\text{ g}\\ (0.39\\text{ kg})}$\n2. **Lid Center of Gravity ($L_{\\text{cog}}$):**\n   - Total lid height from hinge axis to top edge: `~118 mm`.\n   - Center of gravity sits near the geometric center of the Switch core: $L_{\\text{cog}} \\approx \\mathbf{58\\text{ mm}\\ (0.058\\text{ m})}$ from the hinge pivot axis.\n3. **Static Gravitational Torque ($\\tau_{g}$):**\n   - At maximum horizontal overhang ($90^\\circ$ from vertical):\n     $$\\tau_{\\max} = m_{\\text{lid}} \\cdot g \\cdot L_{\\text{cog}} = 0.39\\text{ kg} \\times 9.81\\text{ m/s}^2 \\times 0.058\\text{ m} = \\mathbf{0.222\\text{ N}\\cdot\\text{m}}$$\n   - At typical $115^\\circ$ viewing angle ($25^\\circ$ past vertical):\n     $$\\tau_{115^\\circ} = 0.222\\text{ N}\\cdot\\text{m} \\times \\sin(25^\\circ) = \\mathbf{0.094\\text{ N}\\cdot\\text{m}}$$\n4. **Required Constant-Torque Friction Hinge Spec:**\n   - Applying a **$1.8\\times$ dynamic hold safety factor** over $\\tau_{\\max}$ (so tapping the capacitive touchscreen at $110^\\circ$ does not push the lid backward):\n     $$\\tau_{\\text{hinge, total}} = 1.8 \\times 0.222\\text{ N}\\cdot\\text{m} \\approx \\mathbf{0.40\\text{ N}\\cdot\\text{m}}\\quad (\\mathbf{0.20\\text{ N}\\cdot\\text{m}\\text{ per hinge}}\\text{ using 2 hinges})$$\n   - **Selected Off-the-Shelf Hinge Family:** **Southco `E6-10-204-50`** (`0.23 N\u00b7m` symmetric constant torque per hinge, `0.46 N\u00b7m` pair) or **Sugatsune `HG-TA20` / `HG-IT`** compact friction hinges, with an integrated hard mechanical stop built into the SLA hinge knuckles at **$120^\\circ$**.\n\n### 9.2 Center-of-Gravity Anti-Tip Verification & Overall Dimensions\n- **Base Half Mass ($m_{\\text{base}}$):**\n  - Drop \u00d7 MIT Planck PCB + steel plate + 47 switches + keycaps: `~260 g`\n  - Baseus Blade HD 20,000 mAh power bank: `~445 g`\n  - Trackball module + Internal USB-C Hub + cabling + fasteners: `~95 g`\n  - Custom SLA Base Enclosure + Tray + Feet: `~185 g`\n  - **Total Base Mass ($m_{\\text{base}}$):** $\\approx \\mathbf{985\\text{ g}}$\n- **Stability Ratio:** The base (`~985 g`) is **$2.5\\times$ heavier than the lid (`~390 g`)**. Even at the $120^\\circ$ maximum opening stop, the combined center of mass remains `>42 mm` forward of the rear rubber feet\u2014guaranteeing the deck **will never tip backward** on a desk or lap, even when poking the touchscreen.\n- **Estimated Overall Dimensions & Weight:**\n  - **Closed Dimensions (Layout A \u2014 Compact Front/Corner Trackball):** `~255 mm (W) \u00d7 175 mm (D) \u00d7 39 mm (H)`\n  - **Closed Dimensions (Layout B \u2014 Right-Side Ploopy Nano 38mm Trackball):** `~305 mm (W) \u00d7 165 mm (D) \u00d7 39 mm (H)`\n  - **Front Typing Wrist Height:** `~19.5 mm` (recessed Planck switch plate keeps top of keycaps nearly flush with the top deck bezel).\n  - **Total Cyberdeck Weight:** **`~1.37 kg`** (with 20,000 mAh Baseus Blade HD) or **`~1.14 kg`** (with 10,000 mAh INIU 45W slim bank).\n\n---\n\n## 10. Confirmed User Decisions (Locked In for Phase 2\u201310)\n\nThe following design decisions were confirmed by the user at the conclusion of Phase 1:\n\n1. **Trackball Module & Placement \u2014 Option A Confirmed:**\n   - **Ploopy Nano 2** (`38 mm` ball, RP2040 QMK/VIA, USB-C) mounted in a dedicated socket to the right of the Planck keyboard, with Left/Right/Middle click and Drag-Scroll mapped to the Planck's bottom-right keys (plus optional flanking switches). Total deck width: `~305 mm`.\n2. **Internal Power Bank \u2014 Cheaper Option in Germany Confirmed:**\n   - **INIU Carry `P50-E1` / `BI-B62` 45W Slim USB-C PD Power Bank (`10,000 mAh / 37 Wh`, `15V @ 3A` PD, UN 38.3)** at **~\u20ac33.99 on Amazon.de** (vs. \u20ac69.99+ for Baseus Blade HD 100W). *Note: Parametric OpenSCAD (`cad/config.scad`) will default to the INIU 45W Slim and retain a 1-line preset toggle for the `20,000 mAh` INIU P62-E1 65W (`\u20ac44.99`) and Baseus Blade HD (`\u20ac69.99`).*\n3. **Translucent Lilac 3D Printing Service \u2014 100% Premade Turnkey Factory-Dyed Confirmed:**\n   - **PCBWay `SLA UTR-8100 (Transparent)` + Factory Custom Pantone `2577 C` Lilac Immersion Dyeing + Factory UV Clear Coat (`~\u20ac145.00\u2013\u20ac165.00` shipped to Germany incl. IOSS VAT)**. Arrives 100% finished in Translucent Lilac out of the box with **zero home dyeing or spray painting required**.\n4. **Drop \u00d7 MIT Planck Revision \u2014 Confirmed:**\n   - **Drop + OLKB Planck Rev 6.x** (`233.0 \u00d7 81.0 mm`, USB-C receptacle, MX hotswap PCB + switch plate).\n",
  "phase2_bom": "# Phase 2: Bill of Materials (BOM) & EUR Budget (`ns-conv`)\n\nAll prices below are verified in **EUR (incl. 19% German VAT / MwSt. and shipping to Germany)** as of November 2026.\n\nFollowing your feedback, this BOM now reflects:\n1. **Your Spare Joy-Con / RCM Hardware (`\u20ac0.00`):** Since you can spare your Joy-Con rail/RCM hardware, the replacement rail kit is removed\u2014only a `\u20ac0.99` momentary tactile button is needed.\n2. **AliExpress Mass-Sourcing vs. Fast German Retail (Amazon.de / RS):** Every item lists both its **AliExpress Choice price (incl. 19% German IOSS VAT & free 7\u201310 day shipping)** and its **Amazon.de / EU retail price**.\n3. **100% Premade Enclosure (Zero Home Dyeing or Painting):** All 3D-printed parts arrive ready to assemble out of the box\u2014using **PCBWay Turnkey Factory-Dyed Translucent Lilac SLA (`UTR-8100` + `Pantone 2577 C` Translucent Lilac + UV Clear Coat, `~\u20ac145.00`)** or **JLC3DP Premade Un-Dyed Clear (`~\u20ac50.00`) / Opaque Matte (`~\u20ac28.00`) SLA**.\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Machine-readable CSV version: [`hardware/BOM.csv`](../hardware/BOM.csv)\n\n---\n\n## 1. User-Owned Donor Hardware (`\u20ac0.00` Incremental Cost)\n\n| ID | Component | Specification | Qty | Cost (EUR) | Source | Notes |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :---: | :---: | :--- | :--- |\n| `DON-01` | **Nintendo Switch v1 (2017 Erista)** | `MOD. HAC-001` (Tegra X1 `T210`, unpatched BootROM) | 1 | `\u20ac0.00` | User Owned | Original screen, digitizer, magnesium midframe, mainboard, fan, and 4310 mAh battery reused intact in the lid. |\n| `DON-02` | **Drop \u00d7 OLKB MIT Planck Keyboard** | **Planck Rev 6.x** (`233.0 \u00d7 81.0 mm` PCB + switch plate, USB-C, 47 MX switches + keycaps) | 1 | `\u20ac0.00` | User Owned | Outer aluminum case is unbolted and stored; bare PCB + plate + switches + keycaps recess into the base deck. |\n| `DON-03` | **Spare Right Joy-Con Rail / RCM Jig Parts** | OEM/spare Right Joy-Con rail flex & RCM jig (Pin 10 `HOME/RCM` \u2192 Pin 1 `GND`) | 1 | `\u20ac0.00` | User Owned | Used to wire the lid's recessed momentary RCM boot button without buying a replacement rail. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Core Peripherals, Power Bank & Storage\n\n| ID | Component | Specification | Qty | **AliExpress Budget (EUR)** | **Amazon.de / EU Fast (EUR)** | Recommended Links (AliExpress & DE) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :---: | :---: | :---: | :--- |\n| `PER-01` | **38 mm QMK Trackball (`Ploopy Nano 2` Architecture)** | `38.0 mm` snooker/trackball, **RP2040-Zero** MCU + **PMW3360 / PAW3222** optical sensor breakout + 3\u00d7 **MR63ZZ (`3\u00d76\u00d72.5 mm`)** roller bearings running open-source QMK (`ploopyco/nano`) | 1 | **`\u20ac21.50`** *(DIY AliExpress kit: `\u20ac14.00` PMW3360 lens breakout + `\u20ac2.50` RP2040-Zero + `\u20ac3.00` 38mm ball + `\u20ac2.00` 10\u00d7 MR63ZZ)* | **`\u20ac60.00`** *(Pre-built from [ploopy.co](https://ploopy.co/shop/nano-trackball/) incl. DE shipping)* | **AliExpress:** [PMW3360 Breakout](https://www.aliexpress.com/w/wholesale-PMW3360-module.html) + [RP2040-Zero](https://www.aliexpress.com/w/wholesale-RP2040-Zero.html) + [38mm Snooker Ball](https://www.aliexpress.com/w/wholesale-38mm-snooker-ball.html) + [MR63ZZ Bearings](https://www.aliexpress.com/w/wholesale-MR63ZZ.html) *(or ready-made [ProtoArc EM04 Trackball](https://www.aliexpress.com/w/wholesale-ProtoArc-EM04.html) for `\u20ac18.50`)* |\n| `PWR-01` | **Slim 15V USB-C PD Power Bank (UN 38.3 Certified)** | **INIU Carry `P50-E1` / `BI-B62` 45W Slim** (`10,000 mAh / 37 Wh`, **`15V @ 3.0A` PD**, pass-through charging, `~110 \u00d7 68 \u00d7 18.5 mm`, `210 g`, UN 38.3 / CE) | 1 | **`\u20ac25.99`** *(AliExpress INIU/Baseus DE/PL EU Warehouse)* | **`\u20ac33.99`** *(Amazon.de regular; often `\u20ac27.99` w/ voucher)* | **AliExpress (EU Warehouse):** [INIU / Baseus 45W-65W PD Powerbank](https://www.aliexpress.com/w/wholesale-INIU-45W-power-bank.html)<br>**Amazon.de:** [INIU 45W 10,000 mAh](https://www.amazon.de/s?k=INIU+45W+Powerbank+10000mAh) *(20,000 mAh `INIU P62-E1 65W` alt: `\u20ac44.99`)* |\n| `HUB-01` | **Internal USB-C PD 3.0 Hub (`100W PD` + `3\u00d7 USB-A`)** | **UGREEN Revodok 105 / Baseus 5-in-1 USB-C PD Hub** (`100W` PD pass-through input + `3\u00d7 USB-A` data ports + `4K HDMI`, `115 \u00d7 27 \u00d7 12 mm`) | 1 | **`\u20ac6.50`** *(AliExpress Choice Baseus/Essager/UGREEN 100W PD Hub)* | **`\u20ac12.99`** *(Amazon.de UGREEN Revodok 105)* | **AliExpress:** [100W PD 5-in-1 USB-C Hub](https://www.aliexpress.com/w/wholesale-UGREEN-USB-C-Hub-100W-PD.html)<br>**Amazon.de:** [UGREEN Revodok 105](https://www.amazon.de/s?k=UGREEN+Revodok+105+USB+C+Hub) |\n| `STR-01` | **High-Endurance microSDXC (`256 GB`)** *(Skip if owned)* | **Samsung PRO Plus / Lexar Play `256 GB`** (`UHS-I U3 / A2 / V30`, for Kefir `emuNAND` + Switchroot L4T Ubuntu) | 1 | **`\u20ac16.90`** *(AliExpress Choice Original Lexar/Samsung 256GB)* | **`\u20ac22.99`** *(Amazon.de Samsung PRO Plus)* | **Amazon.de (Recommended to avoid counterfeit SDs):** [Samsung PRO Plus 256GB](https://www.amazon.de/s?k=Samsung+PRO+Plus+256GB+microSDXC) |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Internal Cabling, Power Protection & RCM Trigger Hardware\n\n| ID | Component | Specification | Qty | **AliExpress Budget (EUR)** | **Amazon.de / EU Fast (EUR)** | Recommended Links (AliExpress & DE) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :---: | :---: | :---: | :--- |\n| `CAB-01` | **90\u00b0 Right-Angle Flat Flexible USB-C Ribbon (`20 cm`, Lid \u2192 Base)** | **ADT-Link / FPV Ultra-Flat 90\u00b0 USB-C 3.1 Male-to-Female FPC Cable** (`20 cm`, `100W 20V/5A` PD + `10 Gbps` data, routes through hinge channel) | 1 | **`\u20ac3.40`** | **`\u20ac11.99`** | **AliExpress:** [ADT-Link 90\u00b0 Flat USB-C Extension 20cm](https://www.aliexpress.com/w/wholesale-ADT-Link-USB-C-90-degree-flat-20cm.html)<br>**Amazon.de:** [90\u00b0 USB-C Flachkabel 20cm](https://www.amazon.de/s?k=USB+C+90+Grad+Flachkabel+Verl%C3%A4ngerung+100W) |\n| `CAB-02` | **Short Flexible USB-A to USB-C Cables (`2\u00d7 15 cm`, Planck & Trackball \u2192 Hub)** | **Flat Silicone/FPC USB-A to USB-C Data Cables** (`15 cm`, 2 pcs) | 1 *(pair)* | **`\u20ac1.80`** | **`\u20ac7.99`** | **AliExpress:** [Flat Silicone USB-A to USB-C 15cm](https://www.aliexpress.com/w/wholesale-flat-silicone-USB-A-to-USB-C-15cm.html)<br>**Amazon.de:** [USB-A auf USB-C 15cm 2er](https://www.amazon.de/s?k=USB+A+auf+USB+C+Kabel+15cm+2er) |\n| `CAB-03` | **Rear Panel-Mount USB-C PD Socket (`20 cm`)** | **USB-C Female-to-Male Panel-Mount Extension** (`20 cm`, `M2/M3` screw ears, `16 mm` hole pitch, `100W PD`) | 1 | **`\u20ac2.10`** | **`\u20ac8.99`** | **AliExpress:** [USB-C Panel Mount Extension 100W](https://www.aliexpress.com/w/wholesale-USB-C-panel-mount-extension-cable-100W.html)<br>**Amazon.de:** [USB-C Einbaubuchse Panel Mount](https://www.amazon.de/s?k=USB+C+Einbaubuchse+Panel+Mount+100W) |\n| `ELC-01` | **Inline 5A Blade Fuse Holder + 5A Fast Fuses** | **16 AWG Inline Mini/ATO Blade Fuse Holder + `5A` Fast-Acting Fuses** (protects `VBUS` line from Power Bank) | 1 *(kit)* | **`\u20ac1.50`** | **`\u20ac5.99`** | **AliExpress:** [16AWG Inline Blade Fuse Holder 5A](https://www.aliexpress.com/w/wholesale-16AWG-inline-blade-fuse-holder-5A.html)<br>**Amazon.de:** [Flachsicherungshalter 16AWG 5A](https://www.amazon.de/s?k=Flachsicherungshalter+16AWG+5A) |\n| `ELC-02` | **High-Current Power Cutoff Switch (Power Bank \u2192 Hub)** | **USB-C Male-to-Female Power Toggle Switch Cable (`20V/5A`)** or **`KCD1` `10A` Panel Rocker Switch** | 1 | **`\u20ac1.60`** | **`\u20ac7.99`** | **AliExpress:** [USB-C Switch Extension Cable](https://www.aliexpress.com/w/wholesale-USB-C-switch-extension-cable.html)<br>**Amazon.de:** [USB-C Schalter Kabel](https://www.amazon.de/s?k=USB+C+Schalter+Kabel+Power+Switch) |\n| `RCM-01` | **Recessed Lid RCM Momentary Tactile Switch** | **`6\u00d76\u00d75 mm` Through-Hole/SMD Momentary Tactile Pushbutton** (wires to your spare Right Joy-Con rail Pin 10 `RCM` & Pin 1 `GND`) | 1 *(pack)* | **`\u20ac0.99`** | **`\u20ac2.99`** | **AliExpress:** [6x6x5mm Tactile Push Button Pack](https://www.aliexpress.com/w/wholesale-6x6x5mm-tactile-switch.html) |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Custom 3D-Printed Enclosure: 100% Premade Factory Options (Zero Home Dyeing)\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **100% Premade Out-of-the-Box Requirement (No Home Dyeing or Spraying):**\n> - **Primary Recommendation \u2014 PCBWay Turnkey Factory-Dyed Translucent Lilac (`~\u20ac145.00`):** Ordered on [PCBWay (`pcbway.com`)](https://www.pcbway.com/rapid-prototyping/manufacture/?type=2) in **`UTR-8100 Transparent` SLA resin** with **Factory Custom Pantone `2577 C` Translucent Lilac Immersion Dyeing + Factory UV-Resistant Gloss Clear Spraying**. The parts arrive at your door in Germany already polished, dyed translucent lilac, and UV clear-coated. *(Saving `~\u20ac20` by leaving the 2 hidden internal clamps un-dyed is already reflected in the `\u20ac145.00` total; dyeing all 7 parts is `~\u20ac165.00`).*\n> - **Premade Budget Alternatives on JLC3DP (`~\u20ac50.00` Clear / `~\u20ac28.00` Opaque):** If you want a lower-cost 100% premade shell with zero home work, [JLC3DP (`jlc3dp.com`)](https://jlc3dp.com/) delivers **`8001 Translucent` with factory Clear Oil Spray** (crystal-clear ice aesthetic, **`~\u20ac50.00`** shipped) or **`9000R` Matte White / `Imagine Black` Opaque SLA** (**`~\u20ac28.00`** shipped).\n> - **All options use the exact same OpenSCAD `.stl` / `.3mf` files** (identical SLA dimensional tolerances).\n\n| ID | Component | Specification | Qty | **PCBWay Premade Translucent Lilac (EUR)** | **JLC3DP Premade Factory Color Alternatives (EUR)** | Supplier & Ordering Notes |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :---: | :---: | :---: | :--- |\n| `PRT-01` | **Custom 7-Part SLA Enclosure Set + Test-Fit Jig (100% Factory-Finished)** | Upper Lid Shell (`lid_rear`), Lid Front Bezel (`lid_bezel`), Base Lower Shell (`base_bottom`), Base Top Deck (`base_top_deck`), Power Bank Retainer (`battery_retainer`), Cable Clamp (`cable_clamp`) & Test Jig (`test_fit_jig`) | 1 *(set)* | **`\u20ac145.00`** *(PCBWay `UTR-8100 Transparent` + Factory `Pantone 2577 C` Translucent Lilac Dye + Factory UV Clear Coat incl. DE IOSS shipping)* | \u2022 **`\u20ac26.00`** *(Matte White `9000R`)*<br>\u2022 **`\u20ac28.00`** *(Matte Grey `8111X`)*<br>\u2022 **`\u20ac30.00`** *(Matte Black `Imagine Black`)*<br>\u2022 **`\u20ac50.00`** *(Translucent Clear `8001` Polished)*<br>\u2022 **`\u20ac58.00`** *(Factory Painted Red/Silver/Sky Blue)* | **Lilac:** [PCBWay 3D Printing](https://www.pcbway.com/rapid-prototyping/manufacture/?type=2)<br>**Other Colors:** [JLC3DP](https://jlc3dp.com/) \u2014 see full matrix in [`docs/print-spec.md`](print-spec.md) |\n| \u2014 | **Enclosure Subtotal (Zero Home Dyeing)** | | | **`\u20ac145.00`** | **`\u20ac26.00 \u2013 \u20ac58.00`** *(depending on color)* | |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Off-the-Shelf Mechanical Hardware & Fasteners\n\n| ID | Component | Specification | Qty | **AliExpress Budget (EUR)** | **Amazon.de / RS Fast (EUR)** | Recommended Links (AliExpress & DE) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :---: | :---: | :---: | :--- |\n| `MEC-01` | **Adjustable Friction Torque Hinges (`42.9 \u00d7 36.5 \u00d7 12.7 mm`)** | **Southco `E6-10-301-20` / `CL226` Screw-Adjustable Friction Torque Hinges** (`0\u20130.80 N\u00b7m` per hinge; set to `~0.20 N\u00b7m` each for `100\u2013120\u00b0` hold) | 2 *(1 pair)* | **`\u20ac5.90`** *(AliExpress `CL226 / E6-10-301` 43\u00d736mm pair)* | **`\u20ac14.99`** *(Amazon.de pair)* / **`\u20ac27.60`** *(RS Online DE `192-5488`)* | **AliExpress:** [CL226 / E6-10-301 Adjustable Torque Hinge 43x36mm](https://www.aliexpress.com/w/wholesale-E6-10-301-hinge.html)<br>**Amazon.de:** [Positionierscharnier Einstellbar](https://www.amazon.de/s?k=Positionierscharnier+Drehmomentscharnier+einstellbar) |\n| `MEC-02` | **Stainless Steel Screw & Hex Nut Assortment (`M2 / M2.5 / M3`)** | **A2-70 (`SUS304`) Socket/Button Head Screws (`DIN 912` / `ISO 7380`) + `DIN 934` Hex Nuts & Washers** | 1 *(kit)* | **`\u20ac3.60`** | **`\u20ac11.99`** | **AliExpress:** [M2 M2.5 M3 Stainless Screw Nut Set](https://www.aliexpress.com/w/wholesale-M2-M2.5-M3-stainless-screw-nut-assortment.html)<br>**Amazon.de:** [M2 M2.5 M3 Edelstahl Sortiment](https://www.amazon.de/s?k=M2+M2.5+M3+Edelstahl+Schrauben+Sortiment+DIN+912) |\n| `MEC-03` | **Knurled Brass Threaded Inserts (`M2` & `M3` for Blind SLA Bosses)** | **`M2\u00d73\u00d73.2 mm` & `M3\u00d74\u00d74.5 mm` Brass Inserts** (cold-pressed + CA bonded into blind SLA bosses) | 1 *(pack)* | **`\u20ac1.80`** | **`\u20ac7.99`** | **AliExpress:** [M2 M3 Knurled Brass Inserts](https://www.aliexpress.com/w/wholesale-M2-M3-knurled-brass-insert.html)<br>**Amazon.de:** [M2 M3 Gewindeeinsatz Sortiment](https://www.amazon.de/s?k=M2+M3+Einpressmutter+Messing+Gewindeeinsatz) |\n| `MEC-04` | **Silicone Feet, Lid Bezel Bumpers & `1.5 mm` EVA Battery Foam** | **`10\u00d73 mm` Rubber Feet + `6\u00d71.5 mm` Lid Bumpers + `1.5 mm` High-Density EVA Foam Sheet** | 1 *(set)* | **`\u20ac1.60`** | **`\u20ac6.99`** | **AliExpress:** [Silicone Bumper Feet + 1.5mm EVA Foam](https://www.aliexpress.com/w/wholesale-silicone-rubber-feet-bumper-pad.html)<br>**Amazon.de:** [Elastikpuffer + Moosgummi 1.5mm](https://www.amazon.de/s?k=Elastikpuffer+Gummif%C3%BC%C3%9Fe+selbstklebend+EVA+Moosgummi) |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Tools & Consumables (Skip Any Already Owned)\n\n| ID | Component | Specification | Qty | **AliExpress Budget (EUR)** | **Amazon.de / EU Fast (EUR)** | Recommended Links (AliExpress & DE) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :---: | :---: | :---: | :--- |\n| `TOL-01` | **Precision Screwdriver & Spudger Set (`Y00` + `JIS 00` + `H1.5`)** | **`Y00` Tri-Point + `PH00/JIS 00` + `H1.5` Hex + Plastic Spudger & Opening Picks** | 1 *(set)* | **`\u20ac3.90`** *(AliExpress 25-in-1 / Switch Repair Set)* | **`\u20ac19.99`** *(iFixit Moray 32-Bit Kit)* | **AliExpress:** [25-in-1 Precision Screwdriver Set Y00](https://www.aliexpress.com/w/wholesale-precision-screwdriver-set-Y00-switch.html)<br>**Amazon.de:** [iFixit Moray Bit Set](https://www.amazon.de/s?k=iFixit+Moray+Bit+Set+Y00) |\n| `TOL-02` | **Medium Cyanoacrylate Gel + Blue Threadlocker (`243`)** | **CA Gel (`3 g`) for SLA Brass Inserts + `243` Medium Threadlocker (`10 ml`) for Hinge Screws** | 1 *(pair)* | **`\u20ac2.40`** | **`\u20ac8.99`** | **AliExpress:** [Threadlocker 243 + CA Gel](https://www.aliexpress.com/w/wholesale-threadlocker-243.html)<br>**Amazon.de:** [Schraubensicherung Mittelfest + Gel](https://www.amazon.de/s?k=Liqui+Moly+Schraubensicherung+mittelfest) |\n\n---\n\n## 7. Complete Budget Comparison (EUR \u2014 Germany, Zero Home Dyeing)\n\n| Build Configuration | Peripherals & Power (`PER/PWR/HUB`) | Cabling, Fuse & RCM (`CAB/ELC/RCM`) | 3D-Printed SLA Shell (`PRT-01`) | Mechanical & Fasteners (`MEC`) | **Core Build Total (excl. SD & Tools)** | **All-In Total (incl. 256GB SD & Tools)** |\n| :--- | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| **Option 1: AliExpress Hardware + Turnkey PCBWay Factory-Dyed Translucent Lilac SLA** *(100% Premade Lilac Shell)* | `\u20ac53.99` *(or `\u20ac92.49` w/ pre-built Ploopy Nano 2)* | `\u20ac11.39` | `\u20ac145.00` *(PCBWay `UTR-8100` + Factory Pantone `2577 C` Lilac)* | `\u20ac12.90` | **`\u20ac223.28`** *(`\u20ac261.78` w/ pre-built Ploopy Nano 2)* | **`\u20ac246.48`** *(`\u20ac284.98` w/ pre-built Ploopy)* |\n| **Option 2: AliExpress Hardware + JLC3DP Premade Factory Colors (`White \u20ac26` / `Grey \u20ac28` / `Black \u20ac30` / `Clear \u20ac50` / `Painted \u20ac58`)** | `\u20ac53.99` | `\u20ac11.39` | `\u20ac26.00 \u2013 \u20ac58.00` *(depending on color)* | `\u20ac12.90` | **`\u20ac104.28` (`White`) / `\u20ac108.28` (`Black`) / `\u20ac128.28` (`Clear`)** | **`\u20ac127.48` (`White`) / `\u20ac131.48` (`Black`) / `\u20ac151.48` (`Clear`)** |\n| **Option 3: Fast German Retail (Amazon.de / Ploopy / RS) + Turnkey PCBWay Factory-Dyed Translucent Lilac SLA** | `\u20ac106.98` | `\u20ac45.94` | `\u20ac145.00` | `\u20ac54.57` | **`\u20ac352.49`** | **`\u20ac404.46`** |\n",
  "phase3_teardown": "# Phase 3: Non-Destructive Teardown Plan (`docs/teardown.md`)\n\nThis guide provides a step-by-step, shop-floor disassembly procedure for both donor devices:\n1. **Nintendo Switch v1 (`MOD. HAC-001`, 2017 Erista)** \u2014 Partial, 100% reversible teardown that removes only the outer plastic backplate and detachable Left/Right Joy-Con rails while keeping the factory-bonded LCD, digitizer, magnesium midframe, mainboard, thermal assembly, and 4310 mAh battery intact.\n2. **Drop \u00d7 OLKB MIT Planck (Rev 6.x)** \u2014 Extraction of the `233.0 \u00d7 81.0 mm` switch-plate + hotswap PCB assembly from its aluminum case.\n\nEvery step that carries a risk of component damage is flagged with an explicit **`[RISK / IRREVERSIBILITY WARNING]`** callout.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Pre-Disassembly Safety Gate (Mandatory Stop-Work Checks)\n\nBefore loosening a single fastener, complete all five checks below:\n\n1. **RCM (`fusee-gelee`) Verification Complete:** Confirm that your Switch has already passed the live RCM payload injection test (`0x7000` smash bytes into Hekate) documented in [`docs/research.md`](research.md#22-mandatory-live-rcm-fusee-gelee-test-before-disassembly).\n2. **Discharge Internal Battery Below 25%:** If the Switch battery is above 30%, run a game or Linux benchmark until the battery indicator drops below **25%**. *Why: A lithium-polymer pouch cell below 25% state-of-charge stores minimal thermal energy, drastically reducing fire/runaway risk if accidentally stressed.*\n3. **Full Power-Off (NOT Sleep Mode):** Hold the **Power** button for 3 seconds \u2192 select **Power Options** \u2192 **Turn Off**. Wait 15 seconds after the backlight extinguishes.\n4. **Remove All External Media & Controllers:**\n   - Detach both Left and Right Joy-Cons.\n   - Eject any Game Card from the top slot.\n   - Open the rear kickstand and eject the **microSDXC card** (if installed).\n5. **ESD & Fastener Organization:** Work on a clean, non-conductive mat, ground yourself before touching exposed PCBs, and place removed screws into a labeled magnetic compartmentalized tray\u2014**Switch screw lengths vary by `0.5 mm` to `2.5 mm`, and driving a long screw into a short blind boss will puncture the front bezel or damage PCB traces.**\n\n---\n\n## 2. Required Tools & Fastener Map\n\n### 2.1 Required Tools\n- **`Y00` (1.5 mm) Tri-Point Precision Driver** *(for the 4 corner screws on the Switch rear plastic shell)*\n- **`JIS 00` / `PH00` Precision Driver** *(for all Joy-Con rail, top/bottom bezel, microSD, and EMI shield screws \u2014 a true `JIS 00` tip prevents cam-out on Nintendo's soft screws)*\n- **Hex `H1.5` / `PH0` Driver** *(for Drop Planck Rev 6 case screws)*\n- **Nylon Spudger (Flat & Pointed Ends)** *(for battery connector & ZIF latch actuation \u2014 NEVER use metal tweezers on battery or ZIF connectors)*\n- **ESD-Safe Angled Tweezers** *(for guiding ribbon tails and coaxial antenna routing only)*\n- **Keycap Puller & Digital Calipers (`0.01 mm` resolution)**\n\n### 2.2 Nintendo Switch v1 (`HAC-001`) Fastener Reference Map\n\n| Step | Location | Driver Bit | Thread & Length | Qty | Disposition in Cyberdeck Build |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| **A1** | Rear Plastic Backplate Corners | **`Y00` Tri-Point** | `M1.7 \u00d7 6.3 mm` (self-tapping) | 4 | Store in labeled bag with stock plastic backplate |\n| **A2** | Bottom Edge (Flanking USB-C Port) | **`JIS 00`** | `M2.0 \u00d7 3.0 mm` (machine thread) | 2 | **Reuse** (or replace with `M2\u00d75 mm` in custom lid bottom retainer) |\n| **A3** | Top Edge (Center Vent) | **`JIS 00`** | `M2.0 \u00d7 3.0 mm` (machine thread) | 1 | **Reuse** in custom lid top vent bracket |\n| **A4** | Under Kickstand (microSD Slot Area) | **`JIS 00`** | `M1.7 \u00d7 2.5 mm` (ultra-short!) | 2 | Store in labeled bag with stock backplate |\n| **A5** | Left & Right Joy-Con Side Rails (`5 per side`) | **`JIS 00`** | `M2.0 \u00d7 3.5 mm` (countersunk machine) | 10 *(5L + 5R)* | Store with OEM rails; **the 10 M2 threaded midframe holes are reused with `M2\u00d78 mm` stainless screws to bolt the Switch core into the lid!** |\n| **A6** | microSD Card Reader Board | **`JIS 00`** | `M1.7 \u00d7 3.0 mm` (black washer-head) | 1 | **Reinstall immediately** in Step A10 after reattaching EMI shield |\n| **A7** | Rear Aluminum EMI Shield | **`JIS 00`** | `M1.7 \u00d7 3.8 mm` (silver pan-head) | 6 | **Reinstall in Step A9** (or swap outer 4 with longer `M1.7/M2` standoffs if using rear lid bosses) |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Part A: Nintendo Switch v1 (`HAC-001`) Non-Destructive Disassembly\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    S0[\"Pre-Flight: Battery <25%, Power OFF, SD & Game Card Removed\"] --> S1[\"Step A1\u2013A4: Remove 4x Y00 + 5x Perimeter JIS 00 Screws\"]\n    S1 --> S2[\"Step A5: Unscrew 10x JIS 00 Side Rail Screws (Keep Rails Loose on Ribbons!)\"]\n    S2 --> S3[\"Step A6: Lift Rear Plastic Backplate + Gently Unplug microSD Reader B2B\"]\n    S3 --> S4[\"Step A7: Remove 6x JIS 00 Screws & Lift Aluminum EMI Shield\"]\n    S4 --> S5[\"Step A8 [CRITICAL]: Disconnect 4310mAh Battery Connector with Nylon Spudger\"]\n    S5 --> S6[\"Step A9: Flip Up ZIF Latches & Release Left/Right Joy-Con Rail Ribbons\"]\n    S6 --> S7[\"Step A10: Connect Spare Right RCM Flex, Reconnect Battery, Reinstall EMI Shield & microSD Reader\"]\n```\n\n### Step A1\u2013A4: Remove the Rear Plastic Backplate Fasteners\n1. Place the Switch face-down on a soft, lint-free microfiber cloth (protecting the front digitizer glass).\n2. **`[WARNING \u2014 Screw Stripping]`** Using the **`Y00` Tri-Point driver**, apply firm downward axial pressure and remove the **4\u00d7 `6.3 mm` `Y00` screws** at the four corners of the rear plastic backplate. *If your driver slips even once, stop and check that you are using `Y00` (not `Y0` or `Y000`).*\n3. Switch to the **`JIS 00` driver**:\n   - Remove the **2\u00d7 `M2 \u00d7 3.0 mm` screws** flanking the bottom USB-C port.\n   - Remove the **1\u00d7 `M2 \u00d7 3.0 mm` screw** centered on the top edge next to the exhaust vent.\n   - Flip open the rear kickstand and remove the **2\u00d7 ultra-short `2.5 mm` screws** inside the kickstand recess.\n\n### Step A5: Unscrew the Left & Right Joy-Con Rails (Do NOT Pull Away Yet!)\n1. Using the **`JIS 00` driver**, remove the **5\u00d7 `M2 \u00d7 3.5 mm` black countersunk screws** along the **Left Joy-Con rail** and the **5\u00d7 `M2 \u00d7 3.5 mm` screws** along the **Right Joy-Con rail**.\n2. **`[CRITICAL WARNING \u2014 Fragile Joy-Con Rail Flex Cables]`**\n   > [!CAUTION]\n   > **DO NOT pull the Joy-Con rails away from the console yet!** Each rail is tethered to the inside of the mainboard by a thin 10-pin flexible printed circuit (FPC) ribbon passing through a slot in the magnesium midframe. Pulling a loose rail now will tear the ribbon in half. Leave both rails resting loosely in their side channels or secure them temporarily with a strip of painter's tape until Step A9.\n\n### Step A6: Lift the Rear Plastic Backplate & Remove the microSD Reader Board\n1. Gently lift the bottom edge of the rear plastic backplate (near the USB-C port) upward by `~5 mm`, then slide it slightly toward the top edge to clear the headphone jack lip and remove the backplate completely. Store the backplate and kickstand safely.\n2. You will now see the **silver aluminum EMI shield** and the small **microSD card reader daughterboard** sitting on top of the shield in the bottom-left quadrant:\n   - Remove the **1\u00d7 `JIS 00` black screw** securing the microSD reader board.\n   - **`[WARNING \u2014 Press-Fit Board-to-Board Connector & Foam Gasket]`** Using the flat tip of a **nylon spudger** directly under the top edge of the microSD PCB, gently pry straight up (`90\u00b0` perpendicular to the mainboard) to pop its tiny 16-pin press-fit board-to-board (`B2B`) connector free. *Do not twist or lever against the fragile black conductive sponge gasket surrounding the connector.* Set the microSD board in an ESD bag until Step A10.\n\n### Step A7: Remove the Rear Aluminum EMI Shield\n1. Remove the **6\u00d7 `JIS 00` silver pan-head screws** around the perimeter of the aluminum EMI shield.\n2. **`[NOTE \u2014 Thermal Paste on Heatpipe]`** When you lift the aluminum EMI shield straight up, you will notice a patch of grey/pink high-viscosity thermal putty (`Shin-Etsu` gap filler) in the center where the copper heatpipe transfers heat to the EMI shield.\n   - Keep the inside of the EMI shield facing upward on a clean paper towel so dust does not stick to the thermal putty\u2014we will reinstall this exact EMI shield in Step A10 to preserve the factory thermal path!\n\n### Step A8: Immediately Disconnect the Internal 4310 mAh Battery\n> [!CAUTION]\n> **`[CRITICAL ELECTRICAL SAFETY WARNING]`**\n> Before touching **any** ribbon cable latch on the mainboard, you **MUST** disconnect the internal battery. Unplugging or plugging ZIF ribbons while the mainboard's `3.3V` / `1.8V` standby rails are live can short adjacent pins and blow the `BQ24193` power management IC or backlight boost converter.\n\n1. Locate the white/black 5-wire **Battery Connector** at the bottom-right edge of the battery bay (just left of the lower part of the mainboard).\n2. Using the flat nylon spudger (never metal!), pry **straight upward** (`90\u00b0` away from the mainboard surface) under the wires/lip of the battery plug until it pops vertically out of its board header. *(It is a vertical board-to-board Molex header, NOT a horizontal sliding plug!)*\n3. Bend the battery wires slightly back by `2 mm` so the plug cannot accidentally spring back onto the header pins while you work.\n\n### Step A9: Safely Release the Left & Right Joy-Con Rail ZIF Ribbons\n1. Locate the **Left Joy-Con Rail ZIF Connector** (middle-left edge of the battery/midframe pass-through) and the **Right Joy-Con Rail ZIF Connector** (lower-right edge of the mainboard).\n2. **`[CRITICAL WARNING \u2014 ZIF Flip Latches]`**\n   - Using the pointed tip of your nylon spudger, gently flip the tiny black plastic locking bail **upward `90\u00b0`** to unlock the ZIF socket. *Never pry the housing base itself\u2014only flip the hinged actuator tab.*\n   - Use angled tweezers to slide the Left and Right Joy-Con rail ribbons smoothly out of their sockets and thread them out through the side slots of the magnesium midframe.\n3. Place both original OEM Left and Right Joy-Con rails (along with their 10 screws) in a labeled zip-top bag for 100% future reversibility.\n\n### Step A10: Do-Not-Touch Zones, Spare RCM Flex Installation & Core Button-Up\n> [!WARNING]\n> **`[DO-NOT-TOUCH ZONES \u2014 PRESERVE FACTORY INTEGRITY]`**\n> Because the Switch core mounts into our upper lid as a complete unit, **DO NOT disconnect or disturb any of the following components:**\n> 1. **Glued 4310 mAh LiPo Battery (Left Half):** Never pry or apply alcohol to the battery pouch. It stays factory-glued in its magnesium midframe tray.\n> 2. **53-Pin LCD MIPI DSI ZIF Connector (Bottom-Center of Mainboard, under battery tray lip):** Has an ultra-fragile gold locking bail. Leave 100% untouched.\n> 3. **34-Pin Capacitive Digitizer ZIF & 4-Pin Backlight ZIF (Right Edge near Game Card Reader):** Leave 100% untouched.\n> 4. **Black & White Coaxial Wi-Fi / Bluetooth Antenna Cables (`U.FL` / `MHF1`, Right Edge):** Leave snapped onto their PCB jacks and routed inside their factory midframe clips.\n> 5. **Copper Heatpipe & Cooling Fan:** Leave the 3-screw heatpipe and fan bolted to the SoC and magnesium midframe.\n\n1. **Install the Spare Right Joy-Con RCM Trigger Flex (`DON-03` + `RCM-01`):**\n   - Take your **spare Right Joy-Con rail flex cable** (prepared in Part B below with two thin `30 AWG` leads wired from **Pin 10 (`HOME/RCM`)** and **Pin 1 (`GND`)** to the `6\u00d76\u00d75 mm` momentary tactile button).\n   - Thread the ribbon tail through the right-side midframe slot, slide the gold fingers fully into the **Right Joy-Con ZIF socket** on the mainboard (up to the white insertion line), and press the black ZIF locking bail flat (`0\u00b0`) to lock it.\n2. **Reconnect the Internal Battery:**\n   - Align the 5-pin battery plug directly over its vertical header on the mainboard and press straight down with your finger until it clicks home.\n3. **Reinstall the Aluminum EMI Shield & microSD Reader Board:**\n   - Place the **aluminum EMI shield** back onto the magnesium midframe and secure it with its **6\u00d7 `JIS 00` screws** (ensuring the thermal putty contacts the copper heatpipe).\n   - Align the **microSD card reader board's** 16-pin B2B connector over its socket opening in the EMI shield, press gently with your fingertip until it clicks, and reinstall its **1\u00d7 `JIS 00` black screw**.\n   - **Your Switch Core Module is now complete and ready for the upper lid!**\n\n---\n\n## 4. Part B: Preparing Your Spare Right Joy-Con Rail / RCM Trigger Switch\n\nSince you have spare Joy-Con / RCM hardware (`DON-03`), you have two clean, non-destructive ways to wire the lid's recessed **`6\u00d76\u00d75 mm` Momentary RCM Button (`RCM-01`)**:\n\n- **Method 1 (Using a Spare RCM Jig Inserted into a Spare Right Rail):**\n  1. Open the plastic shell of your spare RCM jig (where the 2 metal contact legs touch **Pin 1 `GND`** and **Pin 10 `HOME/RCM`**).\n  2. Instead of bridging Pin 1 and Pin 10 permanently with a solid wire, cut the bridge in the center of the jig and solder two `10 cm` lengths of `28\u201330 AWG` flexible silicone wire to the Pin 1 leg and Pin 10 leg, routing them to the two terminals of the **`6\u00d76\u00d75 mm` momentary tactile switch (`RCM-01`)**.\n  3. Slide this modified jig permanently into your spare Right Joy-Con rail connector tucked inside the right channel of the upper lid!\n  4. **Result:** Normally open (`Pin 10` floating) = pressing `Power` boots 100% pure Stock Horizon OS (`sysNAND`). Holding the recessed **`RCM` button** while pressing `Vol+` and `Power` grounds `Pin 10` and enters RCM for Hekate (`emuNAND` / L4T Ubuntu)!\n- **Method 2 (Direct Solder to Spare Right Rail FPC Test Pads):**\n  1. On the back of the spare Right Joy-Con rail's 10-pin connector PCB, solder two `30 AWG` wires to **Pad 10 (`RCM`)** and **Pad 1 (`GND` / metal rail body)** and connect them to the `6\u00d76\u00d75 mm` momentary switch.\n  2. Verify with a multimeter in continuity mode that **Pin 9 (`+5V`) has `\u221e \u03a9` (open circuit) to both Pin 10 and GND**, and that Pin 10 connects to GND **only while the button is pressed**.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Part C: Drop \u00d7 OLKB MIT Planck (Rev 6.x) Disassembly\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    P1[\"1. Unplug USB-C Cable\"] --> P2[\"2. Pull Keycaps Above Case Mounting Screws Only\"]\n    P2 --> P3[\"3. Unscrew 5x\u20136x M2 Case Screws (Top or Bottom Depending on Case Style)\"]\n    P3 --> P4[\"4. Lift Bare 233x81mm Switch-Plate + PCB Sandwich Out of Aluminum Case\"]\n    P4 --> P5[\"5. Reinstall Pulled Keycaps & Store Aluminum Case + Screws Safely\"]\n```\n\n### Step C1: Unplug & Identify Your Drop Planck Case Style\n1. Unplug the USB-C cable from the back of the Planck.\n2. Check whether your Drop \u00d7 MIT Planck aluminum case is:\n   - **Lo-Pro / Mid-Pro (Top-Mount Screws):** 5 or 6 small `M2` screws pass **downward through the top switch plate** (hidden beneath specific keycaps) into standoffs in the aluminum base tray.\n   - **Hi-Pro (Bottom-Mount / Sandwich Screws):** Screws pass **upward through the bottom of the aluminum case** or hold a bottom plate onto the top frame.\n\n### Step C2: Remove Only the Necessary Keycaps (Do NOT Pull Switches!)\n1. Using a wire keycap puller, pull straight up to remove the keycaps located above the `M2` mounting screws on the switch plate:\n   - Typically located between keys `(R1, C2)\u2013(R2, C2)`, `(R1, C11)\u2013(R2, C11)`, `(R3, C2)\u2013(R4, C2)`, `(R3, C11)\u2013(R4, C11)`, and center `(R2, C6)\u2013(R3, C6)`.\n2. **`[CRITICAL WARNING \u2014 Hotswap Sockets on Planck Rev 6 PCB]`**\n   > [!CAUTION]\n   > **DO NOT pry or separate the PCB from the metal switch plate!** The 47 MX mechanical switches snap into the `1.5 mm` metal switch plate and plug into surface-mount **Kailh hotswap sockets** on the Planck Rev 6 PCB. Our cyberdeck base mounts the entire **Switch Plate + 47 Switches + Hotswap PCB** together as a single rigid sandwich (`233.0 \u00d7 81.0 mm`). Keep all 47 switches seated keeping the plate and PCB locked together.\n\n### Step C3: Unbolt the Planck Sub-Assembly from the Aluminum Case\n1. Using your **`H1.5` Hex** or **`PH0` / `JIS 0`** driver, unscrew the **5 or 6 `M2` screws** securing the switch plate/PCB assembly to the aluminum case.\n2. Gently tilt the front edge of the `233.0 \u00d7 81.0 mm` switch-plate + PCB assembly upward by `10\u00b0` first so the rear **USB-C receptacle** slides cleanly out of the aluminum case cutout without scraping.\n3. **`[WARNING \u2014 Bottom-Side SMD Components & Piezo Speaker]`**\n   - Look at the underside of the Planck Rev 6 PCB: note the small cylindrical **piezo speaker buzzer**, the **STM32F303 MCU**, the **physical `RESET` micro-button**, and the **47 Kailh hotswap sockets**.\n   - Place the bare Planck assembly only on a flat, soft foam pad (never on stray metal screws that could bridge solder joints or crush the piezo speaker).\n4. Re-seat the keycaps you pulled in Step C2, thread the original case screws partially back into the empty aluminum Planck case so they cannot get lost, and store the aluminum case in a labeled box.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Part D: Pre-CAD Caliper Verification Worksheet (`cad/config.scad` Inputs)\n\nBefore we generate the final print-ready STLs in **Phase 5 (CAD)** (or when checking the test-fit jigs in Phase 6), measure these 8 dimensions on your disassembled hardware with digital calipers to verify our nominal `cad/config.scad` values:\n\n| # | Dimension to Measure | Nominal Value in `config.scad` | Your Measured Value (mm) | Why It Matters |\n| :---: | :--- | :---: | :---: | :--- |\n| **1** | **Switch Core Width** *(Left midframe rail seat to Right midframe rail seat, rails removed)* | `166.5 mm` *(173.0 mm w/ rails)* | `_______ mm` | Sets the exact internal pocket width and side-bolt spacing inside the upper lid. |\n| **2** | **Switch Core Height** *(Bottom edge to top edge of magnesium midframe/bezel)* | `102.0 mm` | `_______ mm` | Sets vertical clearance and top button actuator alignment. |\n| **3** | **Switch Core Thickness** *(Front glass surface to top of rear aluminum EMI shield, backplate removed)* | `11.8 mm` *(13.9 mm w/ backplate)* | `_______ mm` | Determines upper lid internal cavity depth. |\n| **4** | **Switch Side Rail M2 Hole Pitch** *(Center-to-center distance of the 5\u00d7 M2 holes along the side edge)* | `[12.0, 31.5, 51.0, 70.5, 90.0 mm]` from bottom | `_______ mm` | Aligns the 10 structural M2 bolts securing the Switch core to the lid hinge brackets. |\n| **5** | **Planck Switch Plate Width \u00d7 Depth** | `233.0 \u00d7 81.0 mm` | `_______ mm` | Sets the top-deck recess cutout (`+0.35 mm` SLA clearance per side). |\n| **6** | **Planck Plate-to-PCB-Bottom Z-Depth** *(Underside of `1.5 mm` plate lip to lowest component on PCB bottom)* | `9.5 mm` *(11.0 mm cavity depth)* | `_______ mm` | Ensures hotswap sockets and piezo speaker never touch the power-bank barrier wall below. |\n| **7** | **Planck Keycap Height Above Switch Plate** *(Top of plate to highest row keycap peak)* | `10.5 mm` *(OEM/MT3 clearance)* | `_______ mm` | Ensures keycaps never press against the Switch glass screen when the clamshell is closed. |\n| **8** | **Planck USB-C Port Offset** *(Distance from left edge of plate to center of USB-C receptacle)* | `19.05 mm` *(or exact Rev 6 offset)* | `_______ mm` | Aligns the internal USB-C cable channel inside the base deck. |\n",
  "phase4_wiring": "# Phase 4: Electronics & Wiring Plan (`docs/wiring.md`)\n\nThis document specifies the internal electrical architecture, USB-C data and Power Delivery (PD) routing, inline overcurrent protection, RCM payload injection access, DIY trackball SPI pinout, and thermal management for the `ns-conv` clamshell cyberdeck.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Architecture Trade-Off: Internal USB-C PD Hub vs. Direct Soldered Harness\n\nRequirement 4 asks us to compare connecting the **Drop \u00d7 MIT Planck** and **Trackball** to the Switch's USB-C bus via a **small internal USB-C PD hub** vs. a **direct soldered wire harness**, and recommend one.\n\n| Criterion | **Option A: Compact Internal USB-C PD 3.0 Hub (RECOMMENDED)** | **Option B: Direct Soldered Parallel Wire Harness (REJECTED)** |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **USB 2.0 Data Integrity (`D+` / `D-`)** | **Active Hub Controller IC (`VL817` / `GL3523`):** Properly buffers and arbitrates USB packets from multiple downstream HID endpoints (Planck keyboard + Trackball + external USB-A port) onto the Switch's single upstream `D+/D-` pair with matched `90 \u03a9` differential impedance. | **Fails USB Specification:** USB is a point-to-point tiered-star bus, *not* a multi-drop shared bus like I2C or CAN. Soldering two USB devices in parallel onto `D+/D-` without a hub IC causes packet collisions and complete enumeration failure. |\n| **Simultaneous `15V` PD Charging + USB Host Mode** | **Built-in USB-PD 3.0 Controller:** Automatically negotiates `15V @ 2.6A\u20133.0A` from the power bank on its PD input port and executes a **USB-PD Power Role Swap (`PR_Swap`)** over `CC1/CC2` so the Switch acts simultaneously as **USB Data Host (`DFP`)** and **15V Power Sink (`SNK`)**. | **Cannot Charge While Using Keyboard/Trackball:** A passive harness pulling `CC` to ground via a `5.1 k\u03a9` `Rd` resistor forces the Switch to output `5V VBUS` rather than sinking `15V` charge. |\n| **Console Preservation & Reversibility** | **100% Plug-and-Play:** Connects to the Switch's stock bottom USB-C receptacle via a low-profile 90\u00b0 flat FPC plug. Zero soldering on the Switch motherboard. | **High Risk of Board Damage:** Soldering wires to the `0.4 mm`-pitch `M92T36` / `P13USB` pads or USB-C tail violates Requirement 2 (reversibility) and risks lifting pads. |\n| **Bonus External I/O** | Exposes **1\u00d7 spare external USB 3.0 Type-A port** and **1\u00d7 full-size 4K HDMI port** on the side wall of the base deck for free. | No extra ports or video output capability. |\n\n**Engineering Verdict:** **Option A (Internal USB-C PD 3.0 Hub \u2014 `HUB-01`)** is mandatory for valid USB bus arbitration and simultaneous `15V` USB-PD charging while typing.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Internal Packaging & Compartment Fit Analysis\n\n### 2.1 Why the Hub & Power Bank Live in the Base Half (Not the Switch Battery Bay)\n- **Upper Lid (Switch Internal Battery Bay):** The Switch's factory-glued `4310 mAh` (`16 Wh`, `HAC-003`) LiPo cell measures `96.5 \u00d7 64.5 \u00d7 5.2 mm` and fills `100%` of the magnesium midframe's battery recess. We retain this internal battery in the lid so the Switch has uninterrupted UPS backup power whenever the base power bank is switched off or renegotiates PD.\n- **Lower Base (Underneath the Planck + Trackball Deck):**\n  - Base interior footprint: **`298 mm (W) \u00d7 155 mm (D) \u00d7 21 mm (Internal Z-Clearance below Planck PCB)`**.\n  - **Front-Left Bay (`120 \u00d7 75 \u00d7 20 mm`):** Houses the **INIU 45W Slim Power Bank (`PWR-01`, `110 \u00d7 68 \u00d7 18.5 mm`)** cushioned on `1.5 mm` flame-retardant EVA/Poron pads with a `>= 3.5 mm` air gap from all fasteners.\n  - **Rear-Center / Right Bay (`165 \u00d7 65 \u00d7 20 mm`):** Houses the **100W USB-C PD Hub (`HUB-01`, `115 \u00d7 27 \u00d7 12 mm`)**, the **Inline `5A` Blade Fuse Holder (`ELC-01`)**, the **Power Cutoff Switch (`ELC-02`)**, and the **Trackball Socket (`62 \u00d7 54 mm`)** with ample room for strain-relieved cable loops and passive airflow.\n  - *Note:* Because the `HUB-01` aluminum body is only **`12.0 mm` thick**, it fits inside the `21.0 mm` base cavity **without even needing to decase its factory aluminum heat-spreader shell!**\n\n---\n\n## 3. Complete System Wiring Diagram\n\n### 3.1 Mermaid System Schematic\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TB\n    subgraph LID[\"UPPER LID ENCLOSURE (Translucent Lilac SLA)\"]\n        SW_MB[\"Nintendo Switch v1 Mainboard (HAC-001)<br/>\u2022 Internal 4310mAh (16Wh) Battery Connected<br/>\u2022 53-pin LCD & 34-pin Digitizer Untouched\"]\n        SW_USBC[\"Switch Bottom USB-C Port\"]\n        SW_RRAIL[\"Right Joy-Con ZIF Socket (10-Pin)\"]\n        SPARE_JIG[\"Spare Right Joy-Con Rail Flex / Jig<br/>(Pin 10 HOME/RCM & Pin 1 GND)\"]\n        RCM_SW[\"Recessed Momentary Tactile Switch (RCM-01)<br/>Top-Right Lid Edge (Normally Open)\"]\n\n        SW_MB --- SW_USBC\n        SW_MB --- SW_RRAIL\n        SW_RRAIL ==>|10-Pin ZIF| SPARE_JIG\n        SPARE_JIG -->|Pin 10 RCM & Pin 1 GND<br/>30 AWG Silicone Pair| RCM_SW\n    end\n\n    subgraph HINGE[\"CENTRAL HINGE CHANNEL & REAR MODE JUNCTION\"]\n        CAB01[\"CAB-01: 90\u00b0 Right-Angle Flat Flexible USB-C 3.1 Ribbon<br/>(20 cm, 100W PD + 10Gbps, Service Loop in Hinge)\"]\n        REAR_PKT[\"Rear Recessed Coupler Pocket<br/>\u2022 Normal Mode: Hub Upstream Plugged into CAB-01<br/>\u2022 RCM / Hekate UMS Mode: Unplug Hub & Connect PC/Dongle to CAB-01\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph BASE[\"LOWER BASE ENCLOSURE (Translucent Lilac SLA)\"]\n        HUB[\"HUB-01: Internal 5-in-1 USB-C PD 3.0 Hub (115\u00d727\u00d712 mm)<br/>\u2022 Upstream USB-C Cable (15 cm)<br/>\u2022 100W USB-C PD Input Port<br/>\u2022 3\u00d7 USB-A Data Ports + 1\u00d7 4K HDMI\"]\n        PLANCK[\"DON-02: Drop \u00d7 MIT Planck Rev 6 PCB<br/>(USB-C Receptacle, QMK 6KRO Mode)\"]\n        TBALL[\"PER-01: 38mm QMK Trackball<br/>(Ploopy Nano 2 / RP2040-Zero + PMW3360, USB-C)\"]\n        EXT_IO[\"Right-Side / Rear Exposed Cutouts<br/>\u2022 1\u00d7 Spare USB-A 3.0 Port<br/>\u2022 1\u00d7 4K HDMI Out Port\"]\n\n        subgraph PWR_SUB[\"Isolated Power Bank & Fused PD Subsystem\"]\n            EXT_PD[\"CAB-03: Rear Panel-Mount USB-C PD Socket<br/>(External Wall Charger Input \u2014 45W\u201365W PD)\"]\n            PBANK[\"PWR-01: INIU 45W Slim Power Bank (10,000mAh / 37Wh)<br/>\u2022 UN 38.3 Certified, 15V @ 3.0A PD Output<br/>\u2022 Port C1: In/Out Pass-Through | Port C2/Out: 15V PD Out\"]\n            SW_CUT[\"ELC-02: High-Current Power Cutoff Switch<br/>(Inline on VBUS \u2014 Isolates Bank in Storage)\"]\n            FUSE[\"ELC-01: Inline 5A Fast-Acting Blade Fuse<br/>(16 AWG Holder on VBUS \u2014 Overcurrent Protection)\"]\n        end\n    end\n\n    SW_USBC ==>|Low-Profile 90\u00b0 Plug| CAB01\n    CAB01 ==> REAR_PKT\n    REAR_PKT ==>|Upstream Host + 15V PD Sink| HUB\n\n    HUB -->|USB-A1 via CAB-02a<br/>15cm Flat USB-A to USB-C| PLANCK\n    HUB -->|USB-A2 via CAB-02b<br/>15cm Flat USB-A to USB-C| TBALL\n    HUB -.->|USB-A3 & HDMI Flush at Wall| EXT_IO\n\n    EXT_PD ==>|20cm Panel Cable| PBANK\n    PBANK ==>|15V PD Output<br/>CC1/CC2 + GND Continuous| SW_CUT\n    SW_CUT ==>|VBUS (15V max 3A)| FUSE\n    FUSE ==>|15V PD Feed into Hub PD Port| HUB\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3.2 Detailed ASCII Wiring & Fused PD Cable Splice Diagram\n\nTo ensure the **INIU 45W Power Bank (`PWR-01`)** negotiates **15V USB-PD** with the **Internal Hub (`HUB-01`)** while still having a physical **Power Cutoff Switch (`ELC-02`)** and **Inline `5A` Blade Fuse (`ELC-01`)**, the `CC1/CC2` configuration channel and `GND` return must remain unbroken while `VBUS` (`+5V` to `+15V`) passes in series through the switch and `5A` fuse:\n\n```text\n================================================================================\n       FUSED 15V USB-C PD POWER LINE DETAIL (POWER BANK -> INTERNAL HUB)\n================================================================================\n\n  [INIU 45W Slim Power Bank]                       [Internal USB-C PD Hub]\n  (USB-C PD Output Port: 15V/3A)                   (100W USB-C PD Input Port)\n  +----------------------------+                   +---------------------------+\n  |                            |                   |                           |\n  |  VBUS (+5V / +15V PD) o----+---[ SW: ELC-02 ]--+--[ FUSE: 5A Fast ELC-01 ]-+-o VBUS\n  |                            |   (Panel/Inline   |  (16 AWG Mini Blade Fuse) |\n  |                            |    Power Cutoff)  |                           |\n  |  CC1 (PD BMC Comms)   o----+-------------------+---------------------------+-o CC1\n  |  CC2                  o----+-------------------+---------------------------+-o CC2\n  |  GND (Power Return)   o----+-------------------+---------------------------+-o GND\n  +----------------------------+                   +---------------------------+\n\n  HOW TO ASSEMBLE THIS CABLE IN 5 MINUTES (Using ELC-01 + ELC-02):\n  1. Take the short USB-C PD Switch Cable (ELC-02).\n  2. Carefully slit 25 mm of the outer PVC jacket midway along the cable (do not\n     nick the inner wire insulation).\n  3. Separate the thick RED wire (VBUS). Leave the BLACK (GND) and thin BLUE/WHITE/\n     YELLOW (CC1/CC2) wires completely uncut!\n  4. Cut only the RED (VBUS) wire and solder/crimp the two 16 AWG leads of the\n     Inline 5A Blade Fuse Holder (ELC-01) in series with the two red ends.\n  5. Insulate the splice with heat-shrink tubing and insert the 5A fast blade fuse.\n================================================================================\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Solving the RCM Payload Injection & Hekate UMS Mode Challenge\n\n### 4.1 The Electrical Constraint\n- During normal use in **Horizon OS** or **Switchroot L4T Ubuntu**, the Switch is a **USB Host (`DFP`)** reading the Planck keyboard and Trackball through `HUB-01`.\n- However, when entering **Recovery Mode (`RCM`, USB `APX 0955:7321`)** to inject the `hekate` payload\u2014or when using **Hekate's USB Mass Storage (`UMS`)** tool to transfer files to the microSD card from a PC\u2014the Switch acts as a **USB Device (`UFP`)**. A USB Device cannot be enumerated *backwards* through the downstream port of a standard USB hub.\n\n### 4.2 The Zero-Solder Solution: Rear Recessed Mode Coupler Pocket\nOur CAD design routes the female end of the **`20 cm` 90\u00b0 Flat Flexible USB-C Extension Ribbon (`CAB-01`)** (which comes directly from the Switch's bottom USB-C port through the hinge) to a **Recessed Rear Coupler Pocket** at the back of the base enclosure, right alongside the male upstream plug of the internal hub (`HUB-01`):\n\n```text\n  REAR VIEW OF BASE ENCLOSURE \u2014 RECESSED COUPLER & CHARGING POCKET\n  +----------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  |  [1: Rear Panel USB-C PD In]   [2: Switch Direct USB-C]  [3: Hub Plug]|\n  |         (CAB-03)                     (CAB-01 Female)     (HUB-01 Male)|\n  |           (===)                          (===) <------------ [===]   |\n  |     Charges Power Bank               Normal Mode: Hub Plugged In     |\n  |                                      RCM Mode: Plug PC/Dongle Here!  |\n  +----------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```\n\n- **Mode 1 \u2014 Normal Desktop / Gaming Use (Default):** The short flexible upstream tail of `HUB-01` plugs directly into `CAB-01` inside the recessed rear pocket and snaps under a printed retainer clip. The Planck, Trackball, and 15V PD charging all route automatically to the Switch.\n- **Mode 2 \u2014 RCM Payload Injection / Hekate UMS SD Card Access:** Unplug the `HUB-01` male plug from `CAB-01` at the rear pocket and plug your PC USB-C cable (or a pocket RCM payload dongle) directly into `CAB-01`. Hold the lid's **RCM Button (`RCM-01`) + `Volume +`** and tap **`Power`** to inject `hekate`, then plug `HUB-01` back into `CAB-01`!\n\n---\n\n## 5. DIY AliExpress 38 mm Trackball (`RP2040-Zero` + `PMW3360`) SPI Wiring\n\nIf you purchase the **`\u20ac21.50` AliExpress DIY Trackball Kit (`PER-01`)** instead of the pre-assembled `$69.99 CAD` Ploopy Nano 2 from Canada, solder these **6 short `28\u201330 AWG` silicone wires** between the **Waveshare `RP2040-Zero`** and the **`PMW3360` Optical Sensor Breakout Board**:\n\n| `PMW3360` Breakout Pin | Function | `RP2040-Zero` Pin | Wire Color (Suggested) | Electrical Notes |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **`VCC` / `VDD`** | `+3.3V` Logic & Sensor Power | **`3V3`** *(Pin 36 / 3.3V LDO Out)* | Red | **WARNING:** Connect to `3V3` (`3.3V`), **NEVER** to `5V`/`VBUS`! |\n| **`GND`** | Ground Return | **`GND`** | Black | Common ground reference |\n| **`SCLK` / `SCK`** | SPI0 Clock | **`GP2`** (`SPI0 SCK`) | Yellow | Standard QMK `RP2040` hardware SPI0 clock |\n| **`MISO` / `SO`** | SPI0 Master-In Slave-Out | **`GP0`** (`SPI0 RX`) | Green | Sensor data to MCU |\n| **`MOSI` / `SI`** | SPI0 Master-Out Slave-In | **`GP3`** (`SPI0 TX`) | Blue | MCU commands to sensor |\n| **`NCS` / `CS`** | SPI0 Chip Select (Active Low) | **`GP1`** (`SPI0 CSn`) | White | Pull-up handled by QMK driver |\n| **`RST`** *(if exposed)* | Sensor Reset (Active Low) | Tie to **`3V3`** *(or `GP4`)* | Orange | Most breakouts pull `NRESET` high internally via `10 k\u03a9` |\n\n### Flashing QMK to the `RP2040-Zero` Trackball\n1. Hold the **`BOOT`** button on the `RP2040-Zero` while plugging it into your PC via USB-C; it mounts as a USB drive named `RPI-RP2`.\n2. Compile or download the standard QMK `ploopyco/nano` or `pmw3360` RP2040 `.uf2` firmware with `POINTING_DEVICE_DRIVER = pmw3360` and drag-and-drop the `.uf2` file onto `RPI-RP2`.\n3. It immediately reboots as a standard **1000 Hz USB HID Mouse** that works plug-and-play in **Switchroot L4T Ubuntu** and mouse-enabled **Horizon OS** games!\n\n---\n\n## 6. Thermal Dissipation & Battery Safety Engineering\n\n```text\n  SIDE CROSS-SECTION \u2014 THERMAL ISOLATION & AIRFLOW PATHS\n  \n               UPPER LID (Switch Core ~12\u201318W Peak)\n              //==================================\\\\\n             //  [Top Exhaust Louver: 42 x 6 mm]   \\\\  ---> Hot Air Out (Fan)\n            //         ^ Copper Heatpipe/Fan        \\\\\n           //          |                             \\\\\n          //   [Switch Mainboard + 4310mAh Battery]   \\\\\n         //    [Rear Intake Slots: 2x 18 x 4 mm] <-----\\\\-- Cool Air In\n        //==============================================\\\\\n       ( O )  <-- Hinge Axis + Air Gap (~12mm Thermal Break)\n  +-------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  |  [ Drop x MIT Planck 233x81mm ]    [ 38mm Trackball ]             |\n  |  ---------------------------------------------------------------  |\n  |  ====== 2.0mm SLA Barrier Wall + 1.5mm EVA/Poron Foam Pad ======  |\n  |  [ INIU 45W Slim Power Bank ]      [ UGREEN 100W PD Hub ]         |\n  |    (Max \u0394T < 12\u00b0C at 15V/1.2A)       (Aluminum Heat-Spreader)     |\n  +------^^^^^------------------------------^^^^^---------------------+\n         ||||| Bottom Intake Louvers        ||||| Rear/Side Exhaust\n```\n\n1. **Full Physical Separation of Heat Sources:**\n   - The **Switch Tegra X1 SoC (`~12\u201318W` peak thermal load)** sits in the **upper lid**, actively cooled by its stock centrifugal fan. Our upper lid rear shell (`cad/lid_rear.scad`) replicates the exact OEM intake grille geometry (`2\u00d7 18 \u00d7 4 mm` bottom-rear mesh slots) and top exhaust louver (`42 \u00d7 6 mm`) with zero restriction.\n   - The **INIU 45W Slim Power Bank (`PWR-01`)** sits in the **lower base**, separated from the Switch mainboard by the hinge air gap and isolated from the Planck PCB above by a **`2.0 mm` solid SLA structural rib wall + `1.5 mm` flame-retardant EVA/Poron foam sheet**.\n2. **Low-Stress Power Bank Operating Point:**\n   - Even when the Switch is under 100% load while charging (`~18W` at `15V @ 1.2A`), the `45W`-rated INIU power bank operates at only **`40%` of its rated continuous output (`18W / 45W`)**, keeping DC-DC converter efficiency above `91%` and surface temperature below `36\u00b0C`.\n3. **Mechanical Fastener Clearance Around the Power Bank:**\n   - The power bank retention bay uses a **bolt-on SLA strap bracket (`cad/battery_retainer.scad`)** whose `M3` screws thread into bosses located **`4.5 mm` outside** the perimeter of the INIU power bank\u2014no screw tip ever points toward the lithium-polymer casing.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Complete Cabling & Electrical Shopping List Checklist\n\nAll cabling and electrical items below match [`docs/bom.md`](bom.md) and [`hardware/BOM.csv`](../hardware/BOM.csv):\n\n- [ ] **`HUB-01`:** `1\u00d7` 5-in-1 100W USB-C PD Hub (`UGREEN Revodok 105` or `Baseus`, `115 \u00d7 27 \u00d7 12 mm`, with `100W PD In` + `3\u00d7 USB-A` + `HDMI`).\n- [ ] **`CAB-01`:** `1\u00d7` `20 cm` 90\u00b0 Right-Angle Flat Flexible USB-C 3.1 Male-to-Female Extension Ribbon (`100W PD` + `10 Gbps` data, routes from Switch bottom port through hinge to rear coupler pocket).\n- [ ] **`CAB-02`:** `2\u00d7` `15 cm` Flat Silicone USB-A Male to USB-C Male Data Cables (connects `HUB-01` USB-A1/A2 to Planck Rev 6 and 38 mm Trackball).\n- [ ] **`CAB-03`:** `1\u00d7` `20 cm` Rear Panel-Mount USB-C Female-to-Male PD Extension Cable (`M2/M3` screw ears, `16 mm` hole spacing, connects external wall charger to Power Bank input).\n- [ ] **`ELC-01`:** `1\u00d7` `16 AWG` Inline Blade Fuse Holder + `5A` Fast-Acting Blade Fuse (spliced in series with the `VBUS` red wire between Power Bank output and Hub PD input).\n- [ ] **`ELC-02`:** `1\u00d7` `15\u201320 cm` USB-C Male-to-Female Inline Power Cutoff Switch Cable (connects Power Bank `15V` PD output to `HUB-01` PD input through the `5A` fuse).\n- [ ] **`RCM-01`:** `1\u00d7` `6\u00d76\u00d75 mm` Momentary Tactile Pushbutton Switch + `20 cm` of `28\u201330 AWG` flexible silicone wire (wired to Pin 10 `RCM` and Pin 1 `GND` on your spare Right Joy-Con rail/jig).\n",
  "phase5_cad": "# Phase 5: Parametric OpenSCAD CAD Package & Dimensioned Overview (`docs/cad-overview.md`)\n\nAll custom enclosure components for the `ns-conv` clamshell cyberdeck are authored as modular, parametric OpenSCAD source files in [`cad/`](../cad/) driven by a single shared configuration file ([`cad/config.scad`](../cad/config.scad)). Every part has been compiled and validated as a watertight **2-manifold mesh** (`Status: NoError`) using **OpenSCAD 2026 Manifold** into both [`.stl`](../cad/stl/) and [`.3mf`](../cad/3mf/) formats.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Visual Renders of the Current Design\n\n### 1.1 Open Clamshell Isometric View (`112\u00b0` Typing Angle)\n![Open Clamshell Render](renders/assembly_open_iso.png)\n\n### 1.2 Exploded Assembly View (Showing Internal Power Bank, Retainer & Switch Core)\n![Exploded Assembly Render](renders/assembly_exploded.png)\n\n### 1.3 Closed Clamshell View (`0\u00b0` \u2014 Showing 38 mm Trackball Nested in Right Lid Wing)\n![Closed Clamshell Render](renders/assembly_closed.png)\n\n---\n\n## 2. Dimensioned Orthographic Overview Drawing (Units: `mm`)\n\n```text\n================================================================================\n  TOP VIEW \u2014 BASE TOP DECK (cad/base_top_deck.scad + cad/base_bottom.scad)\n  All dimensions in millimeters (mm). Origin (0,0) = Center-X, Front Edge Y=0.\n================================================================================\n\n  |<------------------------------ 306.00 mm (deck_w) ----------------------------->|\n  +---------------------------------------------------------------------------------+ --- Y = 162.00 mm (Rear Edge)\n  |  [==== Southco Hinge (-96.0) ====]   [CAB-01]   [==== Southco Hinge (+96.0) ====] |     (16.0mm Hinge Spine)\n  |---------------------------------------------------------------------------------| --- Y = 146.00 mm\n  |  (o) M3                               (o) M3                                (o) |\n  |                                                                                 |\n  |       |<------------- 233.00 mm [USER_VERIFY: planck_w] ------------->|         |\n  |       +---------------------------------------------------------------+         | --- Y = 97.00 mm\n  |       |  (o) (21.5, 59.5)                             (211.5, 59.5) (o)|         |\n  |       |                                                               |  /---\\  | --- Y = 68.00 mm (tball_cy)\n  |       |       DROP x MIT PLANCK REV 6 RECESSED TRAY                   | |38mm | |     (tball_cx = +121.0mm)\n  | (o)   |                   (o) (116.5, 40.5)                           | |Ball | |  <- Right-Side USB-A &\n  |       |            (2.0mm Perimeter Support Ledge +                   |  \\---/  |     4K HDMI Window (HUB-01)\n  |       |             2.0mm Solid SLA Battery Barrier Floor)            | [MX][MX]| --- 2x 14x14mm Thumb Clicks\n  |       |  (o) (21.5, 21.5)                             (211.5, 21.5) (o)|         |\n  |       +---------------------------------------------------------------+         | --- Y = 16.00 mm (planck_y0)\n  |  (o) M3                               (o) M3                                (o) |\n  +---------------------------------------------------------------------------------+ --- Y = 0.00 mm (Front Wrist Bevel)\n  |<10.0>|<-------------------------- 233.00 --------------------------->|<--63.0-->|\n\n\n================================================================================\n  INNER VIEW \u2014 UPPER LID SHELL & SWITCH CRADLE (cad/lid_rear.scad + lid_bezel.scad)\n================================================================================\n\n  |<------------------------------ 306.00 mm (deck_w) ----------------------------->|\n  +---------------------------------------------------------------------------------+ --- Y = 162.00 mm (Top Edge)\n  | (o)          [Pwr][Vol+/-]     [=== 42.0mm Exhaust ===] [Audio][GameCard]   (o) |\n  |              +---------------------------------------------------------+        | --- Y = 128.00 mm\n  |              |o (Y=90.0)                                     (Y=90.0) o|[RCM]   | <-- Recessed 6x6mm RCM\n  |              |o (Y=70.5)     NINTENDO SWITCH v1 CORE         (Y=70.5) o|      _ |     Momentary Switch Pocket\n  |  \\           |o (Y=51.0)    166.50 x 102.00 x 11.80 mm       (Y=51.0) o|    /   \\\n  |   \\ Diagonal |               [USER_VERIFY: sw_core_*]                  |   | \u00d841 | <- Trackball Parking\n  | (o)\\ Ribs    |  [microSD]       (137.0 x 77.2mm LCD)                   |    \\ _ /     Dome (Closed Lid)\n  |     \\        |o (Y=31.5)                                     (Y=31.5) o|        |\n  |              |o (Y=12.0)   [Intake Grille]     [Intake Grille](Y=12.0)o|        |\n  |              +-----------------------+---------+-----------------------+        | --- Y = 26.00 mm (sw_bottom_y)\n  | (o)          [==== Hinge (-96) ====] | CAB-01  | [==== Hinge (+96) ====]    (o) |\n  +--------------------------------------+---------+--------------------------------+ --- Y = 0.00 mm (Hinge Edge)\n                 |<--- 10x M2 Side-Rail Bolts (5 Left + 5 Right) --->|\n\n\n================================================================================\n  SIDE CROSS-SECTION \u2014 CLOSED CLAMSHELL STACKUP (Z-Height = 46.50 mm Total)\n================================================================================\n\n  Z = 46.50 mm  +------------------------------------------------------------+  --- Outer Rear Face of Upper Lid\n                |  2.50 mm Lid Rear Wall + OEM Fan Intake / Exhaust Louvers  |\n                |  11.80 mm Switch v1 Core (Magnesium Midframe + LCD + Glass)|\n                |  3.00 mm Lid Front Bezel Retainer (cad/lid_bezel.scad)     |\n  Z = 28.50 mm  +================== [1.5mm Silicone Bumpers] ================+  --- Split Line (12.0mm Keycap Gap)\n  Z = 24.50 mm  |  4.00 mm Base Top Deck Flange (cad/base_top_deck.scad)     |\n                |  10.50 mm Planck Rev 6 PCB & Kailh Hotswap Cavity          |\n                |  2.00 mm Solid SLA Battery Isolation Barrier Floor         |\n                |  18.50 mm INIU 45W Slim Power Bank + 1.5mm EVA Foam Pad    |\n                |  2.50 mm Base Bottom Floor + Intake Ventilation Louvers    |\n  Z =  0.00 mm  +------------------------------------------------------------+  --- Desk Surface (+3mm Silicone Feet)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Custom Printable Part Inventory & Manifold Mesh Verification\n\nAll 7 custom parts compile with `--backend=Manifold --hardwarnings` with **zero non-manifold edges or self-intersections**:\n\n| Part ID | OpenSCAD Source | Exported STL / 3MF | Bounding Box (`X \u00d7 Y \u00d7 Z mm`) | Vertices / Facets | Manifold Status | Preview |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| **1. Base Bottom** | [`cad/base_bottom.scad`](../cad/base_bottom.scad) | [`base_bottom.stl`](../cad/stl/base_bottom.stl)<br>[`base_bottom.3mf`](../cad/3mf/base_bottom.3mf) | `306.0 \u00d7 162.0 \u00d7 24.5` | `8,662 / 17,464` | `NoError` (2-Manifold) | [Render](renders/base_bottom.png) |\n| **2. Base Top Deck** | [`cad/base_top_deck.scad`](../cad/base_top_deck.scad) | [`base_top_deck.stl`](../cad/stl/base_top_deck.stl)<br>[`base_top_deck.3mf`](../cad/3mf/base_top_deck.3mf) | `306.0 \u00d7 146.0 \u00d7 23.5` | `7,325 / 14,730` | `NoError` (2-Manifold) | [Render](renders/base_top_deck.png) |\n| **3. Lid Rear Shell** | [`cad/lid_rear.scad`](../cad/lid_rear.scad) | [`lid_rear.stl`](../cad/stl/lid_rear.stl)<br>[`lid_rear.3mf`](../cad/3mf/lid_rear.3mf) | `306.0 \u00d7 162.0 \u00d7 15.0` | `8,698 / 17,548` | `NoError` (2-Manifold) | [Render](renders/lid_rear.png) |\n| **4. Lid Front Bezel** | [`cad/lid_bezel.scad`](../cad/lid_bezel.scad) | [`lid_bezel.stl`](../cad/stl/lid_bezel.stl)<br>[`lid_bezel.3mf`](../cad/3mf/lid_bezel.3mf) | `306.0 \u00d7 162.0 \u00d7 4.2` | `3,616 / 7,276` | `NoError` (2-Manifold) | [Render](renders/lid_bezel.png) |\n| **5. Battery Strap** | [`cad/battery_retainer.scad`](../cad/battery_retainer.scad) | [`battery_retainer.stl`](../cad/stl/battery_retainer.stl)<br>[`battery_retainer.3mf`](../cad/3mf/battery_retainer.3mf) | `18.0 \u00d7 96.0 \u00d7 5.2` | `764 / 1,544` | `NoError` (2-Manifold) | [Render](renders/battery_retainer.png) |\n| **6. USB-C Clamps** | [`cad/cable_clamp.scad`](../cad/cable_clamp.scad) | [`cable_clamp.stl`](../cad/stl/cable_clamp.stl)<br>[`cable_clamp.3mf`](../cad/3mf/cable_clamp.3mf) | `38.0 \u00d7 26.0 \u00d7 4.5` | `1,465 / 2,938` | `NoError` (2-Manifold) | [Render](renders/cable_clamp.png) |\n| **7. Test-Fit Jig** | [`cad/test_fit_jig.scad`](../cad/test_fit_jig.scad) | [`test_fit_jig.stl`](../cad/stl/test_fit_jig.stl)<br>[`test_fit_jig.3mf`](../cad/3mf/test_fit_jig.3mf) | `105.0 \u00d7 55.0 \u00d7 17.0` | `2,773 / 5,582` | `NoError` (2-Manifold) | [Render](renders/test_fit_jig.png) |\n\n---\n\n## 4. `[USER_VERIFY]` Dimension Table (Check Before Final Print)\n\nEvery variable below in [`cad/config.scad`](../cad/config.scad) is marked with `// [USER_VERIFY]`. Measure your disassembled Switch v1 core and Drop \u00d7 MIT Planck Rev 6 with digital calipers (or test them against `test_fit_jig.stl`):\n\n| Variable in `cad/config.scad` | Default Value | Hardware Feature to Measure | How to Adjust if Different |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- | :--- |\n| `sw_core_w` | `166.50 mm` | Width of Switch magnesium midframe with Left/Right Joy-Con rails removed | Edit `sw_core_w` in `cad/config.scad` and run `make -C cad all` |\n| `sw_core_h` | `102.00 mm` | Height of Switch tablet from bottom edge to top edge | Edit `sw_core_h` in `cad/config.scad` |\n| `sw_core_thick` | `11.80 mm` | Thickness from front glass digitizer to rear aluminum EMI shield (backplate off) | Edit `sw_core_thick` in `cad/config.scad` |\n| `sw_rail_hole_y` | `[12.0, 31.5, 51.0, 70.5, 90.0]` | Center-to-center Y positions of the 5\u00d7 M2 side-rail holes from Switch bottom edge | Edit array values in `cad/config.scad` |\n| `sw_rail_hole_z` | `5.80 mm` | Distance from front glass surface to the center of the side M2 holes | Edit `sw_rail_hole_z` in `cad/config.scad` |\n| `planck_w` / `planck_d` | `233.00 \u00d7 81.00 mm` | Outer dimensions of the Drop \u00d7 MIT Planck Rev 6 switch plate | Edit `planck_w` / `planck_d` in `cad/config.scad` |\n| `planck_mount_pts` | `[[21.5, 21.5], ...]` | M2 standoff positions from front-left corner of Planck PCB *(Note: holes are slotted `\u00b10.6 mm` in X for tolerance)* | Edit coordinates in `cad/config.scad` |\n| `pbank_w / d / h` | `110.0 \u00d7 68.0 \u00d7 18.5 mm` | Outer dimensions of your slim 15V USB-C PD power bank (`INIU 45W Slim` default) | Edit `pbank_w`, `pbank_d`, `pbank_h` in `cad/config.scad` |\n| `hinge_hole_span_x / y` | `25.40 \u00d7 19.10 mm` | Hole spacing on your `E6-10-301-20` / `CL226` adjustable torque hinges | Edit `hinge_hole_span_x` / `y` in `cad/config.scad` |\n",
  "phase6_print": "# Phase 6: 3D Print Order Specification \u2014 100% Premade Factory-Finished (`docs/print-spec.md`)\n\nPer your requirement that **all enclosure parts arrive 100% premade and factory-finished in Translucent Lilac with zero home dyeing or spray painting**, **PCBWay (`SLA UTR-8100 Transparent` + Factory Custom Pantone `2577 C` Immersion Dyeing + Factory UV Clear Spray)** is the required manufacturing service.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Why PCBWay Instead of JLC3DP for Premade Translucent Lilac?**\n> JLC3DP's `8001 Translucent` SLA resin ships clear/un-dyed and JLC3DP's factory painting service only supports 5 opaque colors (Black, White, Red, Silver, Sky Blue\u2014no custom Pantone dyeing or translucent purple/lilac). **PCBWay** offers turnkey **factory resin dyeing to any custom Pantone code (`Pantone 2577 C` / `2645 C` Translucent Lilac) plus factory UV-resistant clear urethane spraying**, so the parts arrive at your door in Germany completely finished and ready to bolt together.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Two-Stage Print Strategy: Print `test_fit_jig.stl` First!\n\nBecause SLA photopolymer resins undergo `~0.10%\u20130.15%` UV post-cure shrinkage\u2014and donor hardware tolerances can vary slightly between manufacturing batches\u2014we recommend a **two-stage print workflow** to guarantee a perfect first-try fit before ordering the factory-dyed `306.0 \u00d7 162.0 mm` main shells:\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    S1[\"Stage 1: Print Only<br/>cad/stl/test_fit_jig.stl<br/>(Un-dyed raw SLA, ~18g)\"] --> S2[\"Test 5 Interfaces Against<br/>Your Switch, Planck,<br/>Hinges, Bearings & Inserts\"]\n    S2 --> DEC{\"All 5 Interfaces<br/>Fit Smoothly?\"}\n    DEC -- \"Yes\" --> S3[\"Stage 2: Order Full 6-Part Set<br/>on PCBWay (UTR-8100 + Factory<br/>Pantone 2577 C Lilac Dyeing)\"]\n    DEC -- \"Any Tight/Loose Fit\" --> FIX[\"Update Named Variable in<br/>cad/config.scad & Run<br/>'make -C cad all'\"]\n    FIX --> S3\n```\n\n### 1.1 How to Evaluate [`cad/stl/test_fit_jig.stl`](../cad/stl/test_fit_jig.stl) Upon Arrival\n\n| Gauge Zone on `test_fit_jig.stl` | Physical Check to Perform | Pass Criterion | If Adjustment Is Needed (`cad/config.scad`) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **1. Switch Thickness U-Jaw** *(Left end of jig: `12.20 mm` slot)* | Slide the edge of your disassembled Switch core (backplate & rails removed) into the U-jaw. | Slides in smoothly with `~0.1\u20130.2 mm` play per side; does not bind on the glass digitizer or rear EMI shield. | Adjust `sw_core_thick` (default `11.80`) or `sla_clear_slip` (`0.20`). |\n| **2. Switch 5\u00d7 Side-Rail `M2` Pitch Gauge** *(Front edge: `X = 12, 31.5, 51, 70.5, 90 mm`)* | Hold the jig edge against the left and right edges of the Switch magnesium midframe and thread `M2 \u00d7 8 mm` screws through all 5 holes at once. | All 5 `M2` screws thread smoothly into the Switch midframe without binding. | Update the `sw_rail_hole_y` array in `cad/config.scad`. |\n| **3. Planck Corner Ledge & `M2` Boss** *(Top-right raised pocket)* | Drop the front-left corner of your bare Drop \u00d7 MIT Planck Rev 6 (`233 \u00d7 81 mm`) into the corner shelf. | Switch plate rests flat on the `2.0 mm` ledge and the `M2` screw aligns with the PCB standoff at `(21.5, 21.5)`. | Adjust `planck_plate_t` (`1.50`) or `planck_mount_pts`. |\n| **4. Southco `E6-10-301` Hinge Pattern & `MR63ZZ` Bearing Seat** *(Center of jig)* | Place one `E6-10-301` / `CL226` hinge leaf over the 4-hole pattern (`25.4 \u00d7 19.1 mm`), and snap an `MR63ZZ (3\u00d76\u00d72.5 mm)` bearing + `3 mm` shaft into the bearing cradle. | Hinge holes align; `MR63ZZ` outer ring spins freely without rubbing the walls. | Adjust `hinge_hole_span_x/y` or `tball_bearing_od` (`6.00`). |\n| **5. Thermoset SLA Brass Insert Tolerance Ladder** *(`-0.05`, `0.00`, `+0.05 mm` test bores)* | Test-push an `M2\u00d73\u00d73.2 mm` and `M3\u00d74\u00d74.5 mm` knurled brass insert into the 3 test bores by hand / light clamp pressure. | Pick the bore where the insert presses in snugly with light clamp pressure (for CA glue bonding) without cracking the wall. | Set `m2_insert_d` (`3.15`) and `m3_insert_d` (`4.45`) to match the best hole diameter. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Turnkey Order Configuration: PCBWay (`SLA UTR-8100 Transparent` + Factory Lilac Dyeing)\n\nUpload the STL files from [`cad/stl/`](../cad/stl/) (or 3MF files from [`cad/3mf/`](../cad/3mf/)) to **[PCBWay 3D Printing Instant Quote (`pcbway.com/rapid-prototyping/manufacture/?type=2`)](https://www.pcbway.com/rapid-prototyping/manufacture/?type=2)** and select these exact settings:\n\n### 2.1 Global PCBWay Checkout Settings\n- **3D Technology:** `SLA (Stereolithography)`\n- **Material:** **`UTR-8100 (Transparent)`** *(Choose `UTR-8100 (Transparent)` for a glossy, glass-like retro Game Boy Atomic Purple/Lilac look, or `UTR-8100 (Translucent)` for a slightly softer frosted-glass lilac look)*\n- **Color:** `Transparent` *(Base resin color; the lilac tint is selected under Surface Finish below)*\n- **Layer Thickness:** `0.10 mm` *(Standard high-precision SLA)*\n- **Surface Finish (Post-Processing):**\n  1. Select **`Dyeing`** \u2192 Choose **`Custom Color (Pantone)`** \u2192 Enter **`Pantone 2577 C`** *(Bright Translucent Lilac)* or **`Pantone 2645 C`** *(Pastel Lavender-Lilac)*.\n  2. Select **`Clear Spraying`** *(Factory-applied UV-resistant clear urethane topcoat that seals the dye and gives optical clarity)*.\n- **Wall Thickness Risk Confirmation:** Check `Accept thin wall risk` if prompted by automated DFM for the `0.8 mm` recessed bumper seats.\n- **Units:** `mm (Millimeters)`\n- **Tapping / Threaded Inserts:** `No` *(All screw bosses use captive `DIN 934` stainless hex nuts or cold-press brass inserts to avoid manual tapping fees).*\n\n### 2.2 Copy-Paste Special Instruction for the PCBWay Engineer\nPaste the following instruction into the **\"Other Special Requirements\"** box on PCBWay:\n> *\"1. DYEING: Please immersion-dye all parts in TRANSLUCENT LILAC matching Pantone 2577 C (keep ~65%\u201370% light transmission so internal ribs and electronics remain visible through the shell; do not paint opaque) and finish with UV-resistant clear coat.*\n> *2. ORIENTATION & SUPPORTS: Please place all support structures on the INSIDE (non-cosmetic cavity side) of `base_bottom`, `base_top_deck`, `lid_rear`, and `lid_bezel`. Keep the spherical trackball cup (`\u00d839.3 mm`) on `base_top_deck` and the outer cosmetic shells free of heavy support marks.*\n> *3. MASKING: Do not apply thick clear coat inside the three small bearing slots inside the `base_top_deck` trackball cup or inside the `M2`/`M3` blind insert holes.\"*\n\n---\n\n## 3. Part-by-Part Quantity, Orientation & Turnkey Cost Breakdown (PCBWay \u2192 Germany)\n\n| File in `cad/stl/` | Qty | Dimensions (`mm`) | Est. Resin Mass | Recommended SLA Build Orientation | Est. Base Print (EUR) | Est. Factory Lilac Dye + Clear Coat (EUR) | Line Total (EUR) |\n| :--- | :-: | :---: | :---: | :--- | :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| [`test_fit_jig.stl`](../cad/stl/test_fit_jig.stl) | `1` | `105.0 \u00d7 55.0 \u00d7 17.0` | `~18 g` | Flat (`Z+` up), ordered *un-dyed* in Stage 1 | `~\u20ac4.50` | `\u20ac0.00` *(Stage 1 raw)* | `~\u20ac4.50` |\n| [`base_bottom.stl`](../cad/stl/base_bottom.stl) | `1` | `306.0 \u00d7 162.0 \u00d7 24.5` | `~128 g` | Tilted `15\u00b0\u201320\u00b0`, supports on **inside floor** only | `~\u20ac24.00` | `~\u20ac16.00` | `~\u20ac40.00` |\n| [`base_top_deck.stl`](../cad/stl/base_top_deck.stl) | `1` | `306.0 \u00d7 146.0 \u00d7 23.5` | `~92 g` | Tilted `15\u00b0\u201320\u00b0`, supports on **underside** only (keep top deck & trackball cup support-free) | `~\u20ac18.50` | `~\u20ac15.00` | `~\u20ac33.50` |\n| [`lid_rear.stl`](../cad/stl/lid_rear.stl) | `1` | `306.0 \u00d7 162.0 \u00d7 15.0` | `~105 g` | Tilted `15\u00b0\u201320\u00b0`, supports on **inner Switch cavity** only | `~\u20ac20.50` | `~\u20ac15.50` | `~\u20ac36.00` |\n| [`lid_bezel.stl`](../cad/stl/lid_bezel.stl) | `1` | `306.0 \u00d7 162.0 \u00d7 4.2` | `~36 g` | Tilted `20\u00b0` with full inner-face support grid | `~\u20ac9.50` | `~\u20ac12.00` | `~\u20ac21.50` |\n| [`battery_retainer.stl`](../cad/stl/battery_retainer.stl) | `1` | `18.0 \u00d7 96.0 \u00d7 5.2` | `~6 g` | Flat (`Z+` up) | `~\u20ac2.50` | `~\u20ac4.00` | `~\u20ac6.50` |\n| [`cable_clamp.stl`](../cad/stl/cable_clamp.stl) | `1` *(pair)* | `38.0 \u00d7 26.0 \u00d7 4.5` | `~4 g` | Flat (`Z+` up) | `~\u20ac2.00` | `~\u20ac3.50` | `~\u20ac5.50` |\n| **Shipping & IOSS VAT (Germany)** | \u2014 | \u2014 | `~389 g` total | *DHL / PCBWay Air Line IOSS (incl. 19% German MwSt.)* | \u2014 | \u2014 | `~\u20ac17.50` |\n| **Total Turnkey PCBWay Order** | **7 files** | | | **Arrives 100% Factory-Dyed in Translucent Lilac** | **`~\u20ac81.50`** | **`~\u20ac66.00`** | **`~\u20ac165.00`** |\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Tip to Reduce PCBWay's Per-File Dyeing Fee (`Saves ~\u20ac18\u2013\u20ac22`):**\n> Because PCBWay calculates dyeing/polishing setup fees per uploaded STL file, you can upload `battery_retainer.stl` and `cable_clamp.stl` **un-dyed (`UTR-8100 Transparent` + `Clear Spraying` only, no dyeing fee)** since they sit hidden *inside* the base and lid! Leaving those two small internal brackets clear-transparent reduces the PCBWay turnkey total from **`~\u20ac165.00` down to `~\u20ac145.00`**.\n\n---\n\n## 4. All 100% Premade Factory SLA Color Options (Same `.stl` Files, Zero Home Work)\n\nBecause **all industrial SLA photopolymer resins share the exact same `0.10 mm` layer resolution and `\u00b10.10 mm` dimensional tolerance**, you can pick any of the following **100% premade factory color options** at checkout using the exact same files in [`cad/stl/`](../cad/stl/) without modifying a single CAD parameter:\n\n| Premade Color Option | 3D Print Service | Exact Material & Finish Selection at Checkout | Total Shipped to DE (incl. 19% VAT) | Savings vs. Factory-Dyed Lilac | Visual Appearance |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :---: | :---: | :--- |\n| **Option A: Premade Opaque Matte White / Ivory** *(Lowest Cost)* | **[JLC3DP](https://jlc3dp.com/)** | `SLA` \u2192 **`9000R` (or `LEDO 6060`)** \u2192 Color: `Matte White` \u2192 Surface: `Sanded` | **`~\u20ac26.00`** | **Saves `\u20ac119.00`** | Clean matte white/ivory engineering resin; lowest per-gram resin rate (`~$0.035/g`) |\n| **Option B: Premade Opaque Matte Grey** | **[JLC3DP](https://jlc3dp.com/)** | `SLA` \u2192 **`8111X`** \u2192 Color: `Dark Grey` \u2192 Surface: `Sanded` | **`~\u20ac28.00`** | **Saves `\u20ac117.00`** | Industrial matte gunmetal/grey enclosure |\n| **Option C: Premade Opaque Matte Black** | **[JLC3DP](https://jlc3dp.com/)** | `SLA` \u2192 **`Imagine Black`** \u2192 Color: `Matte Black` \u2192 Surface: `Sanded` | **`~\u20ac30.00`** | **Saves `\u20ac115.00`** | Stealth matte black (costs `~\u20ac4` more than white due to black pigment resin rate) |\n| **Option D: Premade Translucent Clear (\"Ice Clear\")** | **[JLC3DP](https://jlc3dp.com/)** | `SLA` \u2192 **`8001 Translucent`** \u2192 Finish: **`Polishing + Glossy Clear Oil Spray`** | **`~\u20ac50.00`** | **Saves `\u20ac95.00`** | 100% premade crystal-clear/frosted-ice translucent shell showing internal PCB & ribs, without purple dye |\n| **Option E: Premade Opaque Painted (Red / Silver / Sky Blue)** | **[JLC3DP](https://jlc3dp.com/)** | `SLA` \u2192 **`9000R`** \u2192 Finish: **`Spray Painting` (`Red`, `Silver`, or `Sky Blue`)** | **`~\u20ac58.00`** | **Saves `\u20ac87.00`** | Turnkey factory spray-painted opaque color from JLC3DP's standard paint palette |\n| **Option F: Premade Translucent Lilac (\"Atomic Purple\")** *(Primary Spec)* | **[PCBWay](https://www.pcbway.com/rapid-prototyping/manufacture/?type=2)** | `SLA` \u2192 **`UTR-8100 (Transparent)`** \u2192 Finish: **`Dyeing (Pantone 2577 C)` + `Clear Spraying`** | **`~\u20ac145.00`** *(`\u20ac165` all 7 dyed)* | *Baseline* | 100% premade factory vat-dyed translucent lilac with UV gloss clear coat |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Incoming Inspection & Fit Troubleshooting (Zero Re-Print Recovery)\n\nWhen your factory-finished parts arrive:\n1. **Verify Flatness on a Desk:** Place `base_bottom` and `lid_rear` on a flat glass or granite surface. If thin-walled `lid_bezel` has minor shipping bow (`>0.5 mm`), warm it gently with a hairdryer (`~45 \u00b0C` for `30 seconds`) and let it cool under a flat textbook for 10 minutes before assembly.\n2. **Check `MR63ZZ` Bearing Slots in `base_top_deck`:** Drop the three `3 \u00d7 6 \u00d7 2.5 mm` bearings onto their `3 mm` dowel pins and snap them into the trackball cup. Spin each bearing with your finger to verify the outer ring rotates freely without touching the cup wall.\n3. **Never Use a Hot Soldering Iron on SLA Bosses:** SLA resin (`UTR-8100` / `8001` / `9000R`) is a cross-linked thermoset plastic\u2014it does not melt like FDM PLA/ABS. Install all knurled brass inserts (`MEC-03`) using a tiny drop of medium cyanoacrylate gel (`TOL-02`) on the outer knurls and pressing them flush at room temperature.\n",
  "phase7_assembly": "# Phase 7: Step-by-Step Mechanical & Electrical Assembly Guide (`docs/assembly.md`)\n\nThis guide covers the complete mechanical and electrical assembly of the **`ns-conv`** Nintendo Switch v1 clamshell cyberdeck into your premade SLA enclosure.\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Pre-Requisite Before Starting Assembly:**\n> 1. Complete your donor Switch v1 and Drop \u00d7 MIT Planck preparation per [`docs/teardown.md`](teardown.md).\n> 2. Verify all 5 interfaces on [`cad/stl/test_fit_jig.stl`](../cad/stl/test_fit_jig.stl) per [`docs/print-spec.md`](print-spec.md).\n> 3. Ensure the Switch's internal battery is switched **OFF** and the **INIU 45W Slim Power Bank (`PWR-01`)** is switched **OFF** (`ELC-02` toggle open) throughout mechanical assembly.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Assembly Workflow Overview\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    P0[\"Stage 0: Cold-Press Brass Inserts &<br/>Captive DIN 934 Hex Nuts into SLA Shells\"] --> P1[\"Stage 1: Base Lower Shell (base_bottom)<br/>Install EVA Foam, INIU Power Bank, 5A Fuse,<br/>100W PD Hub (Exposed USB-A/HDMI) & Rear Ports\"]\n    P1 --> P2[\"Stage 2: Hinges & Ribbon Bridge<br/>Bolt Southco E6-10-301 Hinges, Route 90\u00b0 USB-C<br/>Ribbon (CAB-01) & Clamp Strain Relief\"]\n    P2 --> P3[\"Stage 3: Upper Lid (lid_rear + lid_bezel)<br/>Seat Switch Core, Secure Wi-Fi Patch Antennas,<br/>Wire Recessed RCM Button & Bolt 10x M2 Side Rails\"]\n    P3 --> P4[\"Stage 4: Base Top Deck (base_top_deck)<br/>Mount Bare Drop Planck (6x M2), Install 38mm<br/>Trackball + MR63ZZ Bearings & Close Base (8x M3)\"]\n    P4 --> P5[\"Stage 5: Hinge Torque Calibration (0.20 N\u00b7m)<br/>& First-Power-On Pre-Flight Checklist\"]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Stage 0: Fastener & Insert Preparation in Thermoset SLA Resin\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> **NEVER Use a Hot Soldering Iron on SLA Photopolymer Resin (`UTR-8100` / `8001` / `9000R`):**\n> Unlike FDM thermoplastics (PLA/PETG/ABS), SLA resin is a cross-linked **thermoset**. Heating it with a `250 \u00b0C` soldering iron will char and crack the boss rather than melt it. All blind brass inserts (`MEC-03`) are sized in [`cad/config.scad`](../cad/config.scad) (`\u00d83.15 mm` for `M2`, `\u00d84.45 mm` for `M3`) for **room-temperature press-fit + medium cyanoacrylate (CA) gel bonding (`TOL-02`)**.\n\n### 2.1 Blind Knurled Brass Inserts (`MEC-03`) Installation Map\n\nApply a micro-drop of medium CA gel (`TOL-02`) to the outer knurls of each insert (keep adhesive out of the internal threads!) and press it flush at room temperature using the flat face of an `M2`/`M3` screw and washer:\n\n| Printed Part | Insert Size (`MEC-03`) | Qty | Exact Locations |\n| :--- | :--- | :-: | :--- |\n| **[`base_bottom.stl`](../cad/stl/base_bottom.stl)** | `M3 \u00d7 4 \u00d7 4.5 mm` | `8\u00d7` | Top faces of the 8 perimeter standoff pillars (`base_boss_pts`) that hold `base_top_deck`. |\n| **[`base_bottom.stl`](../cad/stl/base_bottom.stl)** | `M2 \u00d7 3 \u00d7 3.2 mm` | `2\u00d7` | Rear center spine (`X = \u00b114 mm, Y = 146 mm`) for the lower [`cable_clamp.stl`](../cad/stl/cable_clamp.stl). |\n| **[`base_top_deck.stl`](../cad/stl/base_top_deck.stl)** | `M2 \u00d7 3 \u00d7 3.2 mm` | `6\u00d7` | Underside of the 6 Planck mounting bosses (`X = 21.5, 116.5, 211.5 mm`; `Y = 21.5, 59.5 mm`). |\n| **[`base_top_deck.stl`](../cad/stl/base_top_deck.stl)** | `M2 \u00d7 3 \u00d7 3.2 mm` | `2\u00d7` | Underside of the trackball optical sensor PCB cradle (`X = +106 \u00b1 12 mm`). |\n| **[`lid_rear.stl`](../cad/stl/lid_rear.stl)** | `M2.5 / M2 \u00d7 3 \u00d7 3.2 mm` | `6\u00d7` | Top faces of the 6 perimeter bezel bosses (`bezel_boss_pts`) that hold `lid_bezel`. |\n| **[`lid_rear.stl`](../cad/stl/lid_rear.stl)** | `M2 \u00d7 3 \u00d7 3.2 mm` | `2\u00d7` | Inner hinge exit tunnel (`X = \u00b114 mm, Y = 14 mm`) for the upper [`cable_clamp.stl`](../cad/stl/cable_clamp.stl). |\n\n*Let the CA gel cure for **15 minutes** before threading any screws into the inserts.*\n\n### 2.2 Captive Stainless Hex Nuts (`DIN 934`, `MEC-02`) Installation Map\n\nPress the following stainless steel `DIN 934` hex nuts into their hexagonal counterbores (secured with a tiny dot of CA gel on the outer hex flat if desired):\n- **[`base_bottom.stl`](../cad/stl/base_bottom.stl) underside:**\n  - `2\u00d7 M3 DIN 934` hex nuts under the power bank retainer bosses (`X = -80 mm`, `Y = 15.5 mm` and `Y = 93.5 mm`).\n  - `4\u00d7 M3 DIN 934` hex nuts under the left and right hinge mounting pads (`X = -95 \u00b1 12.7 mm` and `X = +95 \u00b1 12.7 mm`, `Y = 153.5 mm`).\n- **[`lid_rear.stl`](../cad/stl/lid_rear.stl) outer rear face:**\n  - `4\u00d7 M3 DIN 934` hex nuts in the rear hinge leaf pockets (`X = -95 \u00b1 12.7 mm` and `X = +95 \u00b1 12.7 mm`, `Y = 8.5 mm`).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Stage 1: Base Lower Shell (`base_bottom`) \u2014 Power, Hub & Exposed Ports\n\n### 3.1 Exposed External USB, HDMI & Charging Ports Map\n\nBefore installing the internal components into [`base_bottom.stl`](../cad/stl/base_bottom.stl), review how the external I/O ports are exposed through the base walls:\n\n| Exposed Port Location on `base_bottom` | Exposed Connector | Function in Horizon OS & L4T Linux |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Right-Side Flush I/O Window** (`X = +153 mm, Y = 108..131 mm`) | **`1\u00d7 USB-A 3.0 (5 Gbps)`** + **`1\u00d7 4K HDMI`** *(directly on `HUB-01`)* | Plug in external USB flash drives, USB Ethernet, SDR dongles, controllers, or an external HDMI monitor without opening the deck. |\n| **Rear Panel Left** (`X = -42 mm, Y = 162 mm`) | **`1\u00d7 Panel-Mount USB-C PD Socket (`CAB-03`)`** | Plug in your external `15V / 2.6A\u20133A` USB-C PD wall charger to charge both the INIU power bank and the Switch simultaneously. |\n| **Rear Panel Center Pocket** (`X = 0 mm, Y = 150..162 mm`) | **Recessed `CAB-01` USB-C Coupler** | Normal operation: plugged into `HUB-01` upstream lead. RCM payload injection: unplug `HUB-01` here to connect `CAB-01` directly to your PC/RCM loader. |\n| **Rear Panel Right** (`X = +42 mm, Y = 162 mm`) | **Master Power Cutoff Switch (`ELC-02`)** | Physically disconnects the power bank `VBUS` output during storage/transport so zero parasitic current is drawn by the hub. |\n\n### 3.2 Step-by-Step Base Wiring & Component Mounting\n\n1. **Install Rear Panel-Mount USB-C Socket (`CAB-03`) & Power Switch (`ELC-02`):**\n   - Feed the `CAB-03` USB-C female nose into the rear-left cutout (`X = -42 mm`) and fasten its ears with `2\u00d7 M2 \u00d7 8 mm` screws + `M2` nuts (`0.15 N\u00b7m`).\n   - Snap the `ELC-02` rocker/toggle switch into the rear-right rectangular window (`X = +42 mm`).\n2. **Seat the 5-in-1 100W USB-C PD Hub (`HUB-01`) Against the Right-Side Cutout Window:**\n   - Place a strip of `1.5 mm` EVA foam (`MEC-04`) on the floor of the rear-right hub cradle (`X = +22..137 mm, Y = 105..133 mm`).\n   - Press `HUB-01` (`UGREEN Revodok 105` / `Baseus 5-in-1`) into the cradle with its **end-cap `USB-A 3.0` and `4K HDMI` ports facing right (`+X`)**, flush with the right-side cutout window on [`base_bottom.stl`](../cad/stl/base_bottom.stl#L207-L209).\n   - Verify that a standard USB-A thumb drive and HDMI plug insert cleanly from the outside right edge of the case.\n3. **Mount the INIU 45W Slim Power Bank (`PWR-01`) & Inline `5A` Blade Fuse (`ELC-01`):**\n   - Adhere two `100 \u00d7 20 \u00d7 1.5 mm` strips of high-density EVA foam (`MEC-04`) onto the floor of the front-left battery bay (`X = -135..-25 mm, Y = 20..88 mm`), keeping the 8 bottom intake louver slots unobstructed.\n   - Lay the **INIU `P50-E1` 45W Slim Power Bank** into the bay with its USB-C ports facing right (`+X`) toward the center wiring channel.\n   - Place [`battery_retainer.stl`](../cad/stl/battery_retainer.stl) across the top of the power bank (with a `1.5 mm` EVA foam strip on the underside of the strap) and fasten with **`2\u00d7 M3 \u00d7 22 mm` screws** into the external bosses (`0.35 N\u00b7m`).\n   - **Safety Verification:** Visually confirm that both `M3` screws sit completely outside the battery bay perimeter ribs (`\u22654.5 mm` lateral clearance from the pouch cell casing).\n   - Connect the **Inline `5A` Fast-Acting Blade Fuse (`ELC-01`)** and **`ELC-02` Cutoff Switch** in series between the power bank's `15V PD` output and the `100W PD IN` port of `HUB-01` per [`docs/wiring.md`](wiring.md).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Stage 2: Torque Hinges (`MEC-01`) & Hinge USB-C Ribbon Routing (`CAB-01`)\n\n1. **Bolt the Southco `E6-10-301-20` / `CL226` Hinges to the Base:**\n   - Seat the lower leaf of each friction hinge into the left (`X = -95 mm`) and right (`X = +95 mm`) rear spine pockets of [`base_bottom.stl`](../cad/stl/base_bottom.stl).\n   - Apply one drop of blue **Medium Threadlocker `243` (`TOL-02`)** to **`4\u00d7 M3 \u00d7 12 mm` socket-head screws** (with `M3` flat washers under the heads) and thread them down into the captive `M3` hex nuts on the underside of `base_bottom`. Tighten to **`0.50 N\u00b7m`**.\n2. **Route the 90\u00b0 Flat Flexible USB-C Ribbon (`CAB-01`) Through the Center Hinge Tunnel:**\n   - Feed the female coupler end of the `20 cm` 90\u00b0 flat FPC USB-C cable (`CAB-01`) from the upper lid cavity down through the `22 \u00d7 6 mm` center tunnel between the two hinges into the rear coupler pocket of `base_bottom`.\n   - Leave a gentle **`15 mm` S-curve service loop** at the hinge pivot axis (`Y = 154 mm, Z = 24.5 mm`) so the `0.5 mm`-thick FPC ribbon rolls smoothly without tension over the full `0\u00b0` (closed) to `125\u00b0` (open) travel.\n   - Fasten the lower [`cable_clamp.stl`](../cad/stl/cable_clamp.stl) over the ribbon inside `base_bottom` using **`2\u00d7 M2 \u00d7 6 mm` screws** (`0.15 N\u00b7m`).\n3. **Bolt the Upper Lid Shell (`lid_rear`) to the Upper Hinge Leaves:**\n   - Align the upper hinge leaves into the rear pockets of [`lid_rear.stl`](../cad/stl/lid_rear.stl) (`X = \u00b195 mm, Y = 8.5 mm`).\n   - Apply blue Threadlocker `243` to **`4\u00d7 M3 \u00d7 10 mm` button-head screws** and fasten into the captive `M3` hex nuts (`0.50 N\u00b7m`).\n   - Fasten the upper [`cable_clamp.stl`](../cad/stl/cable_clamp.stl) over the ribbon inside `lid_rear` with **`2\u00d7 M2 \u00d7 6 mm` screws** (`0.15 N\u00b7m`).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Stage 3: Upper Lid Assembly (`lid_rear` + `lid_bezel`) \u2014 Switch Core, Wi-Fi Antennas & RCM Button\n\n### 5.1 How Wi-Fi & Bluetooth Work Inside the Lid (Zero Signal Loss)\n\nThe Switch v1 mainboard uses a **Broadcom/Cypress `BCM4356` 2\u00d72 MIMO 802.11ac (2.4 GHz / 5 GHz) + Bluetooth 4.1** radio connected to two flat **PCB patch antennas** via white and black micro-coaxial (`U.FL`) cables:\n- Because [`lid_rear.stl`](../cad/stl/lid_rear.stl) and [`lid_bezel.stl`](../cad/stl/lid_bezel.stl) are printed in **non-conductive SLA photopolymer resin (`2.5 mm` wall)** with zero metallic fillers, the lid is **100% RF-transparent**\u2014matching the RF attenuation of Nintendo's original ABS backplate.\n- During assembly, keep both `U.FL` coaxial connectors snapped onto the mainboard and secure the two flat PCB patch antennas into the non-metallic upper-left and lower-right bays of `lid_rear` using a strip of double-sided tape or Kapton tape (ensuring neither antenna is tucked *underneath* the magnesium midframe or copper EMI shield).\n\n### 5.2 Step-by-Step Switch Core & Lid Bezel Installation\n\n1. **Install the Recessed RCM Momentary Button (`RCM-01`) on the Right Lid Wing:**\n   - Solder or clip two `10 cm` `30 AWG` wires from your spare Right Joy-Con rail / RCM jig (`DON-03`: **Pin 10 `HOME/RCM`** and **Pin 1 `GND`**) to the terminals of the `6 \u00d7 6 \u00d7 5 mm` tactile switch (`RCM-01`).\n   - Seat `RCM-01` into the right-wing pinhole pocket of [`lid_rear.stl`](../cad/stl/lid_rear.stl) (`X = +118 mm, Y = 28 mm`) with a dot of CA gel on the switch body corners, and slide the Joy-Con flex connector onto the Switch's right-hand rail header.\n2. **Connect `CAB-01` and Seat the Switch v1 Core (`DON-01`):**\n   - Plug the 90\u00b0 right-angle male USB-C plug of `CAB-01` into the Switch's bottom USB-C port (`X = 0, Y = 30 mm`).\n   - Lower the Switch core (`166.5 \u00d7 102.0 \u00d7 11.8 mm`) into the centered cradle of [`lid_rear.stl`](../cad/stl/lid_rear.stl), verifying that:\n     - The rear cooling intake grille (`X = -15..+25 mm, Y = 55..85 mm`) aligns over the rear louvers.\n     - The top Power button, Volume `+/-` buttons, `3.5 mm` audio jack, Game Card slot, and top heatsink exhaust align with the top-edge cutouts (`Y = 162 mm`).\n     - The microSDXC slot aligns with the bottom-left access cutout (`X = -52 mm`).\n   - Reconnect the Switch's internal `4310 mAh` battery `BM05` connector onto the mainboard (`docs/teardown.md` Step 2.3).\n3. **Bolt the Switch Core via the 10\u00d7 Side-Rail `M2` Screws (Crisscross Torque Sequence):**\n   - Thread **`10\u00d7 M2 \u00d7 8 mm` stainless screws (`MEC-02`)** through the left and right internal side-wall flanges of [`lid_rear.stl`](../cad/stl/lid_rear.stl) directly into the 10 factory `M2` tapped holes on the Switch's die-cast magnesium midframe (`Y = 12.0, 31.5, 51.0, 70.5, 90.0 mm`).\n   - Tighten in a **center-outward star sequence** to **`0.18 N\u00b7m`** (snug finger-tight; do not over-torque `M2` threads in magnesium):\n     1. Left `Y = 51.0 mm` \u2192 2. Right `Y = 51.0 mm`\n     3. Left `Y = 31.5 mm` \u2192 4. Right `Y = 70.5 mm`\n     5. Right `Y = 31.5 mm` \u2192 6. Left `Y = 70.5 mm`\n     7. Left `Y = 12.0 mm` \u2192 8. Right `Y = 90.0 mm`\n     9. Right `Y = 12.0 mm` \u2192 10. Left `Y = 90.0 mm`\n4. **Fasten the Front Screen Bezel (`lid_bezel`):**\n   - Place [`lid_bezel.stl`](../cad/stl/lid_bezel.stl) over the Switch core so the `1.6 mm` inner lip gently frames the outer black border of the touch digitizer without pinching the active `137.4 \u00d7 77.6 mm` LCD area.\n   - Fasten with **`6\u00d7 M2.5 \u00d7 8 mm` (or `M2 \u00d7 8 mm`) button-head screws** around the perimeter (`bezel_boss_pts`) to **`0.20 N\u00b7m`**.\n   - Press `4\u00d7 \u00d86 \u00d7 1.5 mm` silicone lid bumpers (`MEC-04`) into the four corner recesses on the front face of `lid_bezel`.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Stage 4: Base Top Deck (`base_top_deck`) \u2014 Planck Keyboard & 38 mm Trackball\n\n1. **Mount the Bare Drop \u00d7 MIT Planck Keyboard (`DON-02`):**\n   - Plug one `15 cm` flat silicone USB-A to USB-C cable (`CAB-02`) into the Planck's rear-left USB-C port (`X = -104.5 mm`).\n   - Lower the bare Planck switch-plate + PCB assembly (`233.0 \u00d7 81.0 mm`) into the recessed left pocket of [`base_top_deck.stl`](../cad/stl/base_top_deck.stl).\n   - From the underside (or through the switch plate standoffs), thread **`6\u00d7 M2 \u00d7 6 mm` screws** into the 6 Planck bosses in a **center-outward order** (`X = 116.5 mm` center pair first, then `X = 21.5 mm` left pair and `X = 211.5 mm` right pair) to **`0.15 N\u00b7m`**.\n2. **Install the 38 mm Trackball (`PER-01`):**\n   - Slide the three **`MR63ZZ (3 \u00d7 6 \u00d7 2.5 mm)` roller bearings** onto their `3 \u00d7 10 mm` stainless dowel pins and snap them into the three `120\u00b0`-spaced slots inside the spherical trackball socket (`X = +106 mm, Y = 62 mm`) of [`base_top_deck.stl`](../cad/stl/base_top_deck.stl). Spin each bearing with your fingertip to confirm free rotation.\n   - Bolt the `PMW3360` + `RP2040` optical sensor PCB beneath the `\u00d88.0 mm` bottom lens aperture using **`2\u00d7 M2 \u00d7 5 mm` screws** (`0.12 N\u00b7m`), verifying the sensor lens sits `2.4 mm` below the bottom surface of the `38 mm` ball.\n   - Plug the second `15 cm` USB-A to USB-C cable (`CAB-02`) into the trackball MCU.\n3. **Connect Downstream USB Cables & Close the Base Enclosure:**\n   - Lower `base_top_deck` above `base_bottom` and plug both `CAB-02` USB-A plugs (Planck + Trackball) into the two internal USB-A ports of `HUB-01`.\n   - Plug the `HUB-01` upstream USB-C pigtail into the `CAB-01` female coupler inside the rear center pocket.\n   - Seat `base_top_deck` onto the `1.5 mm` alignment lip of `base_bottom` and fasten with **`8\u00d7 M3 \u00d7 10 mm` button-head screws** in a center-outward crisscross pattern to **`0.30 N\u00b7m`**.\n   - Drop the `38.0 mm` trackball into the right-hand socket and press `4\u00d7 \u00d810 \u00d7 3 mm` self-adhesive silicone feet (`MEC-04`) into the bottom corner recesses of `base_bottom`.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Stage 5: Hinge Torque Calibration & First-Power-On Pre-Flight Checklist\n\n### 7.1 Hinge Torque Calibration (`0.20 N\u00b7m` per Hinge)\n1. Open the lid to **`112\u00b0`**.\n2. Using the **`H1.5` hex key (`TOL-01`)**, turn the radial friction adjustment set-screw on the barrel of the left and right **Southco `E6-10-301-20` / `CL226`** hinges in equal **`1/8`-turn increments** clockwise until:\n   - The lid holds any angle between **`90\u00b0` and `125\u00b0`** without drooping when you tap the touchscreen, and\n   - Opening the lid slowly requires smooth, even resistance (`~0.40 N\u00b7m` combined across both hinges).\n3. Close the lid to **`0\u00b0`** and verify that the `38 mm` trackball nests cleanly inside the spherical parking pocket in the right wing of `lid_bezel` while the 4 silicone lid bumpers rest evenly on the palm rest.\n\n### 7.2 Fastener Torque Summary Table\n\n| Fastener Location | Screw Spec (`MEC-02`) | Target Torque | Thread Treatment |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| **Hinge Leaves \u2192 `base_bottom` & `lid_rear`** | `8\u00d7 M3 \u00d7 10\u201312 mm` + `DIN 934` Nut | **`0.50 N\u00b7m`** | Blue Threadlocker `243` (`TOL-02`) |\n| **Power Bank Retainer \u2192 `base_bottom`** | `2\u00d7 M3 \u00d7 22 mm` + `DIN 934` Nut | **`0.35 N\u00b7m`** | Dry (nylon washer optional) |\n| **`base_top_deck` \u2192 `base_bottom` (8\u00d7 Bosses)** | `8\u00d7 M3 \u00d7 10 mm` into Brass Inserts | **`0.30 N\u00b7m`** | Dry |\n| **`lid_bezel` \u2192 `lid_rear` (6\u00d7 Bosses)** | `6\u00d7 M2.5/M2 \u00d7 8 mm` into Brass Inserts | **`0.20 N\u00b7m`** | Dry |\n| **Switch Magnesium Midframe \u2192 `lid_rear` (10\u00d7)** | `10\u00d7 M2 \u00d7 8 mm` into Switch Midframe | **`0.18 N\u00b7m`** | Dry (Star sequence) |\n| **Planck Plate (`6\u00d7`), Clamps (`4\u00d7`) & Rear USB-C (`2\u00d7`)** | `12\u00d7 M2 \u00d7 6\u20138 mm` into Brass Inserts | **`0.15 N\u00b7m`** | Dry |\n| **Trackball Sensor PCB \u2192 `base_top_deck` (`2\u00d7`)** | `2\u00d7 M2 \u00d7 5 mm` into Brass Inserts | **`0.12 N\u00b7m`** | Dry |\n\n### 7.3 First-Power-On Pre-Flight Checklist\n\nBefore pressing the Switch Power button or flipping `ELC-02` ON:\n- [ ] **1. Short-Circuit / Continuity Check:** With `ELC-02` **OFF**, use a multimeter across the rear `CAB-03` USB-C `VBUS` and `GND` pins (or verify the `5A` blade fuse `ELC-01` is intact and unblown).\n- [ ] **2. Battery Screw Clearance Check:** Confirm both `M3 \u00d7 22 mm` retainer screws sit outside the INIU power bank ribs with `1.5 mm` EVA foam above and below the bank.\n- [ ] **3. Standalone Switch Boot Check (`ELC-02` OFF):** Press the top-edge **Switch Power Button** for 3 seconds. Verify the Switch LCD illuminates, touchscreen responds, fan spins quietly, and Wi-Fi detects local networks.\n- [ ] **4. Internal Hub + Power Bank Activation (`ELC-02` ON):** Flip the rear **`ELC-02` Power Switch ON**. Verify:\n  - The Switch top-right battery icon displays the **lightning bolt charging indicator** (`15V USB-C PD` active).\n  - The **Drop \u00d7 MIT Planck** RGB/LEDs initialize and typing works in the Horizon OS text keyboard (`6KRO` mode) and L4T Ubuntu Linux.\n  - Rolling the **38 mm Trackball** moves the cursor smoothly in L4T Ubuntu Linux (and Hekate NYX).\n- [ ] **5. Recessed RCM Button Check:** Power the Switch completely **OFF**, unplug `HUB-01` inside the rear center pocket to connect `CAB-01` to your PC/RCM dongle, hold the recessed **RCM button (`RCM-01`) + Volume `+`**, and verify `TegraRcmGUI` / `fusee-nano` detects `APX / RCM OK`.\n",
  "phase8_software": "# Phase 8: Complete Software Setup Guide \u2014 Kefir CFW + `chimera-l4s` (Linux 6.18 Enigma R20) (`docs/software.md`)\n\nThis guide provides the complete, step-by-step software setup for the **`ns-conv`** clamshell cyberdeck, combining:\n1. **Unmodified Stock Horizon OS (`sysNAND`):** 100% clean internal eMMC for legitimate online Nintendo Switch gameplay.\n2. **Horizon OS Custom Firmware via [Kefir (`v927`)](https://github.com/rashevskyv/kefir/releases/tag/927):** Atmosph\u00e8re + Hekate Nyx GUI + `exosphere` serial blanking + `dns.mitm` Nintendo telemetry blocking on **`emuNAND`**.\n3. **Chimera Linux `aarch64` (`musl` + `dinit`) with Linux `6.18.0-enigma-r20-erista+` via [`../chimera-l4s`](file:///Users/jonasnowak/Documents/repos/chimera-l4s) ([`JonasNowak/chimera-switch-6.18`](https://github.com/JonasNowak/chimera-switch-6.18)):** Mainline-tracking `linux-nx` 6.18 kernel with Enigma R20 patches, Erista Device Tree (`tegra210-odin.dtb`), USB-C CDC-NCM Ethernet (`usb0` at `10.42.0.2/24` + OpenSSH), and built-in Tegra X1 xHCI USB HID support for the **Drop \u00d7 MIT Planck keyboard** and **38 mm Trackball**.\n4. **Optional Co-Existing [Switchroot L4T Ubuntu 24.04 (Noble)](https://wiki.switchroot.org/wiki/linux/l4t-ubuntu-noble-installation-guide) Rescue Path (`L4T 4.9`):** Preserved in `/bootloader/ini/L4T.ini` and `/switchroot/ubuntu/` for full hardware-accelerated desktop GUI & onboard Broadcom Wi-Fi while Enigma R20/R21 PCIe LTSSM is brought up.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Multi-Boot Architecture on the Clamshell Cyberdeck\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    COLD[\"Cold Power-On (Switch Top Power Button)\"] --> MODE{\"Hold Recessed Lid<br/>RCM Button (RCM-01)<br/>+ Volume Up (+)?\"}\n    MODE -- \"No (Normal Press)\" --> SYS[\"Stock Horizon OS (sysNAND)<br/>100% Unmodified Internal eMMC<br/>Safe for Nintendo Online Play\"]\n    MODE -- \"Yes (RCM Mode via Rear<br/>CAB-01 USB-C Coupler)\" --> HEK[\"Hekate Bootloader (Nyx Touchscreen GUI)<br/>Installed by Kefir v927 on SD Partition 1 (FAT32)\"]\n\n    HEK --> OPT1[\"Launch -> Kefir CFW (emuNAND)<br/>exosphere Serial Blanking + 90DNS/dns.mitm<br/>Planck 6KRO USB Keyboard Active\"]\n    HEK --> OPT2[\"More Configs -> Chimera Linux 6.18 (Erista)<br/>(/bootloader/ini/CHIMERA.ini from ../chimera-l4s)<br/>uImage 6.18.0-enigma-r20-erista+ + tegra210-odin.dtb<br/>Mounts /dev/mmcblk0p2 (ext4 LABEL=SWR-CHI)\"]\n    HEK --> OPT3[\"More Configs -> Chimera Linux 6.18 (UART-B Debug)<br/>Streams 115200 8N1 earlycon + dinit logs<br/>over Right Joy-Con Rail Pins 5/8 (1.8V)\"]\n    HEK --> OPT4[\"More Configs -> Switchroot L4T Ubuntu (Optional Rescue)<br/>(/bootloader/ini/L4T.ini + /switchroot/ubuntu/)\"]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. `emuNAND` vs. `sysNAND` Comparison & Ban-Risk Trade-Offs (Kefir `v927`)\n\nKefir supports running Atmosph\u00e8re CFW on either **`emuNAND` (SD Card)** or **`sysNAND` (Internal eMMC)**. Below are the exact ban-risk and partition-layout trade-offs for our cyberdeck:\n\n| Configuration | Ban Risk | SD Space Used | How It Interacts with `chimera-l4s` (`LABEL=SWR-CHI`) | Recommendation |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- | :--- |\n| **Option 1: File-Based `emuNAND` on FAT32 (`mmcblk0p1`) + Clean `sysNAND`** | **Near-Zero on `sysNAND`** (`emuNAND` uses Kefir `exosphere.ini` + `dns.mitm`) | `~29.8 GB` inside `/emuMMC/SD00/` on `p1` | **Best compatibility with `chimera-l4s`!** Keeps the SD card as a clean **2-partition MBR layout**: `mmcblk0p1` (`FAT32`) + `mmcblk0p2` (`ext4`, `LABEL=SWR-CHI`). `rootdev=mmcblk0p2` in [`CHIMERA.ini`](file:///Users/jonasnowak/Documents/repos/chimera-l4s/out/sd-boot/bootloader/ini/CHIMERA.ini) works unmodified! | **Strongly Recommended for `chimera-l4s` + Kefir** |\n| **Option 2: SD Partition `emuNAND` (`mmcblk0p3`) + Clean `sysNAND`** | **Near-Zero on `sysNAND`** (`emuNAND` uses Kefir `exosphere.ini` + `dns.mitm`) | `29.1 GB` raw partition (`12\u201315%` faster I/O than file-based) | Creates a **3-partition MBR layout**. If Hekate places `emuMMC` on `p2` and Linux `ext4` on `p3`, you must set `rootdev=mmcblk0p3` in `bootloader/ini/CHIMERA.ini` (automated by [`software/deploy-chimera-kefir-sd.sh`](../software/deploy-chimera-kefir-sd.sh)). | **Recommended if you prioritize maximum `emuNAND` load speed** |\n| **Option 3: CFW Directly on `sysNAND` (No `emuNAND`)** | **HIGH (Permanent Console Ban Risk)** | `0 GB` | Even with Airplane Mode or `90DNS`, any homebrew NSP, custom profile icon, or crash report written to `sysNAND` telemetry logs will trigger a ban as soon as `sysNAND` reconnects to Nintendo servers. | **Do Not Use if You Care About Online Play** |\n\n### Three Layers of Ban Protection Included in Kefir (`v927`)\n1. **`exosphere.ini` (Incognito / PRODINFO Blanking on `emuNAND`):** Automatically zeroes out your Switch's serial number (`XAW00000000000`) in memory whenever booted into `emuNAND`, while leaving the real serial intact in `sysNAND`.\n2. **`dns.mitm` (`atmosphere/hosts/default.txt`):** Kernel-level hostname redirection built into Atmosph\u00e8re that blocks all `*.nintendo.net`, `*.nintendo.com`, and `receive-lp1.dg.srv.nintendo.net` telemetry servers across every Wi-Fi network (stronger than manual `90DNS` IP settings, which only apply per Wi-Fi SSID).\n3. **Strict `emmc=0` Enforcement in `chimera-l4s`:** In [`../chimera-l4s/out/sd-boot/bootloader/ini/CHIMERA.ini`](file:///Users/jonasnowak/Documents/repos/chimera-l4s/out/sd-boot/bootloader/ini/CHIMERA.ini), `emmc=0` and `/etc/fstab` (`LABEL=SWR-CHI`) guarantee that Chimera Linux never mounts or touches internal eMMC (`/dev/mmcblk1`).\n\n---\n\n## 3. How `chimera-l4s` (`6.18.0-enigma-r20-erista+`) Works with the Cyberdeck Hardware\n\nWe inspected [`../chimera-l4s/configs/chimera-erista-r20.config`](file:///Users/jonasnowak/Documents/repos/chimera-l4s/configs/chimera-erista-r20.config) and [`../chimera-l4s/README.md`](file:///Users/jonasnowak/Documents/repos/chimera-l4s/README.md) to verify how every cyberdeck hardware subsystem interacts with your Linux 6.18 build:\n\n| Cyberdeck Hardware Subsystem | Kernel / Driver Status in `chimera-l4s` (`6.18.0-enigma-r20-erista+`) | Operational Notes & Workarounds |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Drop \u00d7 MIT Planck Keyboard (`DON-02`)** | **Built-in (`=y`):** `CONFIG_USB_XHCI_TEGRA=y`, `CONFIG_USB_HID=y`, `CONFIG_HID_GENERIC=y`, `CONFIG_INPUT_KEYBOARD=y`, `CONFIG_VT_CONSOLE=y` | Works immediately on Linux virtual terminals (`tty1`) and under Horizon OS (ensure QMK `NKRO` is toggled **OFF** via `Lower + Raise + N` for Horizon OS `6KRO` compatibility). |\n| **38 mm Trackball (`PER-01`)** | **Built-in (`=y`):** `CONFIG_USB_HID=y`, `CONFIG_HID_GENERIC=y`, `CONFIG_INPUT_MOUSEDEV=y` (`1280\u00d7720`) | Enumerates immediately via `xhci-tegra` on `/dev/input/mice` and `/dev/input/event*` when `HUB-01` is connected. |\n| **Rear Center USB-C Coupler Pocket (`CAB-01`)** | **Dual-Role (`tegra-xudc` Gadget vs. `xhci-tegra` Host)** | \u2022 **Plugged into Mac:** `dinit` starts `/etc/dinit.d/usb-gadget` (`CDC-NCM` USB Ethernet on `usb0` at `10.42.0.2/24` + `ACM` serial `/dev/cu.usbmodem*`) for headless `ssh chimera@10.42.0.2`.<br>\u2022 **Plugged into Internal `HUB-01`:** Switch runs in USB Host mode (`xhci-tegra`) powering the Planck, Trackball, and exposed right-side `USB-A 3.0` port while receiving `15V PD` power from the INIU power bank. |\n| **Wi-Fi / Networking in Linux 6.18 vs. Horizon OS** | \u2022 **Horizon OS & L4T 4.9:** Onboard Broadcom `BCM4356` 2.4/5 GHz Wi-Fi works natively through the RF-transparent SLA lid.<br>\u2022 **`chimera-l4s` (Linux 6.18 R20):** Onboard PCIe Wi-Fi (`brcmfmac`) is currently blocked upstream by the Tegra PCIe LTSSM timeout (`enigma-r20-ltssm.patch`). | In `chimera-l4s` 6.18, network access works via: **(a)** USB-C Ethernet gadget (`usb0`, `10.42.0.2/24`) to your Mac, or **(b)** plugging a standard **USB-A Ethernet or USB Wi-Fi dongle** into the cyberdeck's **exposed right-side `USB-A 3.0` port (`HUB-01`)**! |\n| **Right Joy-Con Rail `1.8V` UART-B Debug (`Pin 5 TX` / `Pin 8 RX`)** | **Supported (`uart_port=2`, `earlycon=1`)** via the `Chimera Linux 6.18 (UART-B Joy-Con Debug)` entry in `CHIMERA.ini` | Your spare Right Joy-Con rail flex inside the lid (`DON-03`) is already wired for Pin 10 (`RCM-01`) and Pin 1 (`GND`). Tapping **Pin 5 (`TX`)** and **Pin 8 (`RX`)** with a `1.8V` TTL USB-UART adapter captures full ATF (`bl31`), U-Boot (`bl33`), and Linux 6.18 `earlycon` logs at `115200 8N1`. |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Step-by-Step Installation: Combining Kefir `v927` + `chimera-l4s` on Your microSD Card\n\nAll pre-built Chimera Linux 6.18 artifacts are already compiled and verified in [`/Users/jonasnowak/Documents/repos/chimera-l4s/out/`](file:///Users/jonasnowak/Documents/repos/chimera-l4s/out):\n- [`../chimera-l4s/out/chimera-switch-erista.img`](file:///Users/jonasnowak/Documents/repos/chimera-l4s/out/chimera-switch-erista.img) (`1.88 GB` flashable 2-partition image: `p1` `SWITCHBOOT` FAT32 + `p2` `SWR-CHI` ext4)\n- [`../chimera-l4s/out/sd-boot/`](file:///Users/jonasnowak/Documents/repos/chimera-l4s/out/sd-boot) (`bootloader/ini/CHIMERA.ini` + `switchroot/chimera/*`)\n- [`../chimera-l4s/out/rootfs.tar.zst`](file:///Users/jonasnowak/Documents/repos/chimera-l4s/out/rootfs.tar.zst) (`159 MB` Chimera Linux `aarch64` rootfs archive with `6.18.0-enigma-r20-erista+` modules)\n\n### Step 4.1: Partition the microSD Card (`256 GB` Recommended)\n\nYou have two clean ways to prepare the microSD card on macOS:\n\n#### Path A \u2014 Fast Turnkey Image Flash + Partition Expansion (Recommended for Dedicated Test Card)\n1. Flash [`/Users/jonasnowak/Documents/repos/chimera-l4s/out/chimera-switch-erista.img`](file:///Users/jonasnowak/Documents/repos/chimera-l4s/out/chimera-switch-erista.img) onto your microSD card using [balenaEtcher](https://etcher.balena.io/) or the interactive script in `chimera-l4s`:\n   ```bash\n   cd /Users/jonasnowak/Documents/repos/chimera-l4s\n   ./scripts/make-sd.sh --device /dev/diskX\n   ```\n2. This creates:\n   - **Partition 1 (`/dev/mmcblk0p1`, `FAT32`, Label `SWITCHBOOT`):** Pre-populated with `/bootloader/ini/CHIMERA.ini` and `/switchroot/chimera/`.\n   - **Partition 2 (`/dev/mmcblk0p2`, `ext4`, Label `SWR-CHI`):** Pre-populated with the Chimera Linux `aarch64` rootfs and `6.18.0-enigma-r20-erista+` kernel modules.\n\n#### Path B \u2014 Large Multi-Boot Card via Hekate Partition Manager (Kefir `emuNAND` + Chimera Linux 6.18)\n1. Format your `256 GB` microSD card as `FAT32` (`MBR / Master Boot Record`) on macOS and extract the latest **[Kefir `v927` release (`kefir927.zip`)](https://github.com/rashevskyv/kefir/releases/tag/927)** to the root of the SD card.\n2. Insert the SD card into the cyberdeck's bottom-lid microSD slot, hold the recessed **`RCM-01` button + `Volume +`**, press **`Power`**, and inject `payload.bin` (Hekate) from your Mac via the rear `CAB-01` USB-C coupler.\n3. In Hekate's touchscreen Nyx GUI, tap **`Tools \u2192 Partition SD Card`**:\n   - **FAT32 (`hos_data`):** Drag slider to allocate `~160\u2013190 GB` (for Horizon OS games + File-Based `emuMMC`).\n   - **Linux (`EXT4`):** Drag slider to allocate `32\u201364 GB` (becomes `/dev/mmcblk0p2`, formatted as `ext4`).\n   - **emuMMC (`RAW`):** Leave at `0 GB` if using **File-Based `emuMMC`** (keeps Linux on `mmcblk0p2`), or set to `29 FULL` if using **SD Partition `emuMMC`**.\n   - Tap **`Next Step \u2192 Start`** to partition.\n4. Populate the Linux `ext4` partition (`LABEL=SWR-CHI`) with [`../chimera-l4s/out/rootfs.tar.zst`](file:///Users/jonasnowak/Documents/repos/chimera-l4s/out/rootfs.tar.zst) and copy the `sd-boot` files using the automated deployment script in Step 4.2 below.\n\n---\n\n### Step 4.2: Run the Automated `ns-conv` SD Deployment Script (`software/deploy-chimera-kefir-sd.sh`)\n\nWith the microSD card's `FAT32` partition mounted on your Mac (either via a card reader or via **`Hekate \u2192 Tools \u2192 USB Tools \u2192 SD Card`** over the rear USB-C coupler), run [`software/deploy-chimera-kefir-sd.sh`](../software/deploy-chimera-kefir-sd.sh) from this repository:\n\n```bash\ncd /Users/jonasnowak/Documents/repos/ns-conv\n./software/deploy-chimera-kefir-sd.sh --sd-mount /Volumes/SWITCHBOOT\n```\n\nWhat this script does automatically:\n1. Verifies all SHA256 checksums in [`../chimera-l4s/out/sd-boot/MANIFEST.sha256`](file:///Users/jonasnowak/Documents/repos/chimera-l4s/out/sd-boot/MANIFEST.sha256) (`bl31.bin`, `bl33.bin`, `uImage`, `initramfs`, `nx-plat.dtimg`, `tegra210-odin.dtb`).\n2. Downloads and extracts **Kefir `v927`** (or merges with an existing Kefir install on the SD card) while preserving `exosphere.ini` and `atmosphere/hosts/default.txt`.\n3. Copies `/bootloader/ini/CHIMERA.ini` and `/switchroot/chimera/*` onto the `FAT32` partition without touching any existing `/bootloader/ini/L4T.ini` or `/switchroot/ubuntu/` rescue installation.\n4. Checks whether your SD card has an `emuMMC` raw partition (`--rootdev mmcblk0p2` vs `mmcblk0p3`) and updates `rootdev=` in `CHIMERA.ini` accordingly.\n\n---\n\n### Step 4.3: Create `emuNAND` & Backup `sysNAND` in Hekate (Mandatory Before CFW Boot)\n\n1. Boot into **Hekate Nyx GUI** on the cyberdeck touchscreen.\n2. **Backup Clean `sysNAND` First:**\n   - Tap **`Tools \u2192 Backup eMMC`**.\n   - Tap **`eMMC BOOT0 & BOOT1`**, then **`eMMC RAW GPP`** (`rawnand.bin`). Store a copy of `/backup/` on your Mac.\n3. **Create `emuMMC` (`emuNAND`):**\n   - Tap **`emuMMC` (on the home screen) \u2192 `Create emuMMC`**.\n   - Select **`SD File`** (if you chose Option 1 to keep `/dev/mmcblk0p2` as `SWR-CHI`) or **`SD Partition`** (if you allocated a raw partition in Step 4.1).\n   - Once complete, confirm the green **`emuMMC: Enabled!`** status badge appears in the `emuMMC` panel.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Booting & Operating Each OS in the Clamshell Cyberdeck\n\n### 5.1 Booting Unmodified Stock Horizon OS (`sysNAND`) \u2014 No Dongle Required\n- Leave `AutoRCM` **OFF**.\n- Simply press the top-edge **Switch Power Button** normally (do **not** hold the recessed `RCM-01` button).\n- The console boots straight into clean Stock `sysNAND` Horizon OS.\n\n### 5.2 Booting Kefir CFW (`emuNAND`)\n1. Power the Switch completely **OFF**.\n2. Unplug `HUB-01` inside the rear center coupler pocket and connect `CAB-01` to your Mac (or portable RCM dongle).\n3. Insert a paperclip/stylus tip lightly onto the recessed **Right-Wing RCM Button (`RCM-01`)**, hold **`Volume +`**, and tap **`Power`**.\n4. Inject `payload.bin` (Kefir's Hekate payload) from macOS (`webcfw.sh` or `fusee-launcher.py`).\n5. Reconnect `HUB-01` to `CAB-01` inside the rear pocket and flip the rear power bank switch **`ELC-02` ON**.\n6. On the Switch touchscreen in Hekate, tap **`Launch \u2192 Kefir (emuMMC)`**.\n\n### 5.3 Booting `chimera-l4s` (`Chimera Linux 6.18.0-enigma-r20-erista+`)\n1. In Hekate Nyx GUI, tap **`More Configs`**.\n2. Tap **`Chimera Linux 6.18 (Erista)`** (or **`Chimera Linux 6.18 (UART-B Joy-Con Debug)`** if capturing `1.8V` serial logs on Right Joy-Con Rail Pins 5/8).\n3. **For Headless USB-SSH Bring-Up (`usb0`):**\n   - Keep `CAB-01` connected to your Mac. Within 15 seconds, `tegra-xudc` enumerates as `Switch Erista USB Network` (`10.42.0.2/24`).\n   - From macOS Terminal:\n     ```bash\n     ssh chimera@10.42.0.2\n     # Default password: chimera (escalate via: doas -s)\n     ```\n   - Run the verification commands and record your Erista bring-up output in [`/Users/jonasnowak/Documents/repos/chimera-l4s/docs/TEST-REPORT.md`](file:///Users/jonasnowak/Documents/repos/chimera-l4s/docs/TEST-REPORT.md):\n     ```bash\n     uname -a\n     cat /sys/firmware/devicetree/base/model && echo\n     dinitctl list\n     lsusb\n     dmesg | grep -E \"input|hid|usb|xudc|xhci\"\n     ```\n4. **For Standalone Cyberdeck Input Mode (`xhci-tegra`):**\n   - Plug `HUB-01` into the rear `CAB-01` coupler and flip `ELC-02` **ON**.\n   - The **Drop \u00d7 MIT Planck keyboard** and **38 mm Trackball** enumerate over `xhci-tegra` (`CONFIG_USB_XHCI_TEGRA=y`, `CONFIG_USB_HID=y`), and the right-side exposed **`USB-A 3.0` port** accepts any USB Ethernet or USB Wi-Fi adapter (`ax88179_178a` / `r8152` / `cdc_ether`).\n",
  "phase9_testing": "# Phase 9: Test & Acceptance Checklist (`docs/testing.md`)\n\nUse this structured acceptance test protocol after completing [`docs/assembly.md`](assembly.md) to verify console preservation, dual-OS USB HID input, Wi-Fi/Bluetooth signal integrity, `15V` USB-C PD pass-through charging, thermal margins, and mechanical hinge durability.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Test Suite A: Console Preservation & RF (Wi-Fi / Bluetooth) Acceptance\n\n| Test ID | Procedure | Expected Result / Pass Criterion | Status |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :---: |\n| **`TST-A1`** | **Dongle-Free Stock `sysNAND` Boot:** With `AutoRCM` disabled and `ELC-02` OFF, press the top-edge **Switch Power Button**. | Console boots directly into unmodified Stock Horizon OS (`sysNAND`) in `< 12 seconds`. | `[ ]` |\n| **`TST-A2`** | **Capacitive Touchscreen & Display Check:** Sweep an icon across all four corners and center of the `6.2\"` LCD inside [`lid_bezel`](../cad/lid_bezel.scad). | Zero dead touch zones; no bezel pinch points or LCD edge light-bleed along the `1.6 mm` front retainer lip. | `[ ]` |\n| **`TST-A3`** | **Top-Edge Native I/O & microSDXC Check:** Insert a physical Switch Game Card, plug headphones into the `3.5 mm` jack, click Volume `+`/`-`, and verify the microSDXC card in System Settings. | Game card mounts immediately; stereo audio switches between internal speakers and `3.5 mm` jack; microSDXC shows full capacity. | `[ ]` |\n| **`TST-A4`** | **2.4 GHz / 5 GHz Wi-Fi & Bluetooth RSSI Check:** Connect to a 5 GHz Wi-Fi router `5 meters` away and pair your wireless Joy-Cons / Pro Controller (`BCM4356` patch antennas inside the non-conductive SLA lid). | 5 GHz Wi-Fi achieves `3/3` bars (`RSSI >= -60 dBm` in L4T `iwconfig`); Bluetooth controller exhibits zero dropped inputs at `5 m`. | `[ ]` |\n| **`TST-A5`** | **Recessed RCM Hardware Trigger (`RCM-01`):** Power OFF the Switch, unplug `HUB-01` in the rear coupler pocket, connect `CAB-01` to a PC/RCM dongle, and hold **`RCM-01` + `Volume +`**. | Switch enters `APX / RCM` mode cleanly and payloads (`hekate_ctcaer.bin`) inject on the first attempt. | `[ ]` |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Test Suite B: Internal & Exposed USB HID / HDMI Matrix (Both OSes)\n\n| Test ID | Target OS / Environment | Procedure | Expected Result / Pass Criterion | Status |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :---: |\n| **`TST-B1`** | **Hekate NYX Bootloader** | Boot into Hekate NYX GUI; tap menu items on the touchscreen and move the `38 mm` trackball. | Capacitive touchscreen and USB HID trackball cursor navigate NYX menus smoothly. | `[ ]` |\n| **`TST-B2`** | **Stock Horizon OS (`sysNAND`) & Kefir (`emuNAND`)** | Open `System Settings \u2192 System \u2192 Change Console Nickname` (or eShop/Browser search box) and type all 47 keys on the **Drop \u00d7 MIT Planck**. | Every Planck key registers immediately; `6KRO` boot-protocol descriptor is active (`NKRO` disabled). | `[ ]` |\n| **`TST-B3`** | **Switchroot L4T Ubuntu Linux** | Boot L4T Ubuntu; test the **Drop \u00d7 MIT Planck** (` Lower` / `Raise` layers) and **38 mm Trackball** (`PMW3360` / `RP2040`) at the login screen and desktop terminal (`xinput list`). | Both `OLKB Planck` and `Ploopy Nano Trackball` enumerate via `xhci-tegra` (`USB 2.0/3.0`) with zero missed keystrokes and smooth `360\u00b0` ball tracking. | `[ ]` |\n| **`TST-B4`** | **Exposed Right-Side `USB-A 3.0` Port (`HUB-01`)** | Plug an external USB 3.0 flash drive into the flush right-side `USB-A` window of [`base_bottom`](../cad/base_bottom.scad#L207-L209) under L4T Ubuntu. | Drive mounts at `USB 3.0 SuperSpeed (5 Gbps)` (`lsusb -t` shows `5000M` `xhci-tegra` link) and achieves `>= 100 MB/s` sequential read. | `[ ]` |\n| **`TST-B5`** | **Exposed Right-Side `4K HDMI` Port (`HUB-01`)** | Connect an external HDMI monitor to the flush right-side `HDMI` window while `15V PD` power (`ELC-02` ON) is active. | External display receives `1080p60` (Horizon OS Docked Mode / L4T Ubuntu dual-head output) with audio over HDMI. | `[ ]` |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Test Suite C: `15V` USB-C PD Charging, Pass-Through & Runtime Benchmark\n\n| Test ID | Procedure | Expected Result / Pass Criterion | Status |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :---: |\n| **`TST-C1`** | **Internal Power Bank \u2192 Switch `15V PD` Negotiation:** With external wall power unplugged, flip rear switch **`ELC-02` ON**. | `INIU P50-E1` (`37 Wh`) negotiates `15V` PD through `HUB-01`; Switch displays the charging lightning bolt icon and battery percentage increases during active gameplay. | `[ ]` |\n| **`TST-C2`** | **Single-Port External Pass-Through Charging (`CAB-03`):** Plug a `45W\u201365W` `15V` USB-C PD wall charger into the rear panel socket (`CAB-03`) with `ELC-02` ON. | Both the `INIU` power bank LED percentage and the Switch battery indicator charge simultaneously (`True Pass-Through`), with brief `~1s` PD re-handshake upon plug-in. | `[ ]` |\n| **`TST-C3`** | **Combined `53.0 Wh` Extended Runtime Benchmark:** Fully charge both batteries (`16.0 Wh` Switch + `37.0 Wh` INIU = `53.0 Wh` total), set screen brightness to `50%`, and run an active 3D game or L4T Ubuntu workload. | Total continuous untethered runtime reaches **`7.5 to 9.5 hours`** (nearly `3\u00d7` stock Erista runtime). | `[ ]` |\n| **`TST-C4`** | **Zero Parasitic Drain Cutoff (`ELC-02` OFF):** Flip `ELC-02` **OFF** and leave the cyberdeck stored for `48 hours`. | Power bank state-of-charge drops by **`0%`** over `48 hours` (confirming `HUB-01` quiescent current is completely isolated). | `[ ]` |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Test Suite D: Thermal & Acoustic Stress Test (`30-Minute` Full Load)\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> **SLA Photopolymer Thermal Limit (`HDT ~ 52\u201358 \u00b0C`):**\n> Standard translucent/opaque SLA resins (`UTR-8100`, `8001`, `9000R`) have a Heat Deflection Temperature of `~54 \u00b0C`. Verify during `TST-D1` that no external SLA enclosure surface exceeds **`45 \u00b0C`**.\n\n| Test ID | Procedure | Expected Result / Pass Criterion | Status |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **`TST-D1`** | **Lid Tegra X1 SoC & Exhaust Thermal Test:** Run `30 minutes` of heavy 3D load (or `stress-ng --cpu 4` + `glmark2` in L4T Ubuntu) with the lid at `112\u00b0`. Monitor `/sys/class/thermal/thermal_zone*/temp` (or Tesla `Status Monitor`). | Tegra X1 SoC stays **`<= 62 \u00b0C`**; internal fan spins unobstructed through the rear intake louvers (`Y = 55..85 mm`) and top exhaust cutout; outer [`lid_rear`](../cad/lid_rear.scad) SLA surface stays **`<= 40 \u00b0C`**. | `[ ]` |\n| **`TST-D2`** | **Base Power Bank & PD Hub Thermal Isolation Test:** During simultaneous `15V PD` discharge (`TST-D1`), measure the bottom intake louvers under [`base_bottom`](../cad/base_bottom.scad) (`pbank_bay` and `hub_bay`). | Power bank bay and USB-C PD hub stay **`<= 42 \u00b0C`** (thermally isolated inside the base half, separated by the hinge air gap from the Switch SoC in the lid). | `[ ]` |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Test Suite E: Mechanical & 50-Cycle Hinge Durability Test\n\n| Test ID | Procedure | Expected Result / Pass Criterion | Status |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **`TST-E1`** | **Static Tip-Over & Typing Ergonomics Test:** Open the lid to **`100\u00b0`**, **`112\u00b0`**, and **`120\u00b0`** on a flat desk and type vigorously on the **Drop \u00d7 MIT Planck**. | Center of gravity remains forward of the hinge axis (`Y = 154 mm`) thanks to the `210 g` power bank + `295 g` Planck in the base; deck does **not** tip backward at `120\u00b0`. | `[ ]` |\n| **`TST-E2`** | **50-Cycle Clamshell Open/Close Endurance Test (`0\u00b0 \u2194 120\u00b0`):** Open and close the lid `50 times` continuously while L4T Ubuntu runs `dmesg -w` in a terminal. | Zero USB disconnects or `xhci-tegra` link resets on the `CAB-01` 90\u00b0 flat FPC ribbon; hinge holding torque remains steady (`~0.20 N\u00b7m` per hinge) with zero `M3` bolt loosening; `38 mm` trackball nests cleanly in the right-wing lid recess on every closure. | `[ ]` |\n",
  "phase10_risks": "# Phase 10: Engineering Risk Register \u2014 Top 10 Risks & Mitigations (`docs/risks.md`)\n\nThis risk register documents the **top 10 technical, mechanical, electrical, and operational risks** across the **`ns-conv`** Nintendo Switch v1 clamshell cyberdeck conversion, along with the preventive design controls built into the CAD/wiring architecture and step-by-step recovery mitigations.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Risk Matrix Summary\n\n| ID | Risk Title | Category | Likelihood | Impact | Built-In Preventive Design Control |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :---: | :---: | :--- |\n| **`RSK-01`** | **Nintendo Account / Console Telemetry Ban on `sysNAND`** | Software / Security | Medium | Critical | Strict isolation of Kefir CFW & L4T Linux on microSD `emuNAND` + `exosphere` blanking + `dns.mitm`; `AutoRCM` left OFF for clean `sysNAND` boot. |\n| **`RSK-02`** | **Switch `M92T36` / `P13USB` IC Damage from Non-Compliant PD Hub or Charger** | Electrical / Power | Low | Critical | Certified `15V @ 3.0A` USB-C PD 3.0 power bank (`INIU P50-E1`) + compliant `100W` PD hub (`HUB-01`) + inline `5A` fast-acting fuse (`ELC-01`). |\n| **`RSK-03`** | **Mainboard Ribbon Tear or Display Flex Damage During Teardown** | Teardown / Board | Low | High | **No-Mainboard-Removal Architecture:** Display (`53-pin` MIPI DSI), digitizer, fan, and Wi-Fi coax stay factory-mounted inside the magnesium midframe (`docs/teardown.md`). |\n| **`RSK-04`** | **SLA Photopolymer Shrinkage, Thin-Wall Bowing, or Boss Cracking** | CAD / 3D Print | Medium | Medium | Two-stage print (`test_fit_jig.stl` first); captive `DIN 934` stainless hex nuts + cold-press CA-bonded brass inserts (zero hot-iron thermal stress). |\n| **`RSK-05`** | **Drop \u00d7 MIT Planck Keyboard Ignored by Stock Horizon OS (`NKRO` Trap)** | USB HID / Firmware | High *(if unconfigured)* | Medium | Disable QMK `NKRO` (`Lower + Raise + N` or `NKRO_ENABLE = no`) so the Planck enumerates with a standard `6KRO` boot-protocol HID descriptor (`docs/wiring.md`). |\n| **`RSK-06`** | **Lithium-Ion Power Bank Mechanical Puncture, Swelling, or Thermal Runaway** | Battery Safety | Low | Critical | UN 38.3 certified `INIU P50-E1` mounted in the base half (thermally isolated from the lid SoC), cushioned by `1.5 mm` EVA foam, with all `M3` screws `>= 4.5 mm` outside the cell perimeter. |\n| **`RSK-07`** | **SLA Thermal Softening / Creep Around Switch Exhaust or Hinge Pads (`HDT ~ 54 \u00b0C`)** | Thermal / Structural | Low | High | Top heatsink exhaust (`Y = 162 mm`) and rear intake (`Y = 55..85 mm`) are 100% unobstructed; hinges bolt through `4.5 mm`-thick SLA spine pads backed by steel washers and `DIN 934` nuts. |\n| **`RSK-08`** | **Hinge `CAB-01` Flat USB-C Ribbon Fatigue or RCM Payload Injection Lockout** | Cabling / Hinge | Low | Medium | `20 cm` ultra-flat FPC ribbon (`CAB-01`) routed with a `15 mm` rolling service loop clamped by `2\u00d7 cable_clamp.stl`; accessible rear coupler pocket allows direct 1:1 RCM USB-C connection. |\n| **`RSK-09`** | **Parasitic Battery Drain During Multi-Day Clamshell Storage** | Electrical / Power | High *(without switch)* | Low | Physical series power cutoff switch (`ELC-02`) on the rear panel completely isolates the power bank from the USB-C PD hub (`0 mA` standby draw). |\n| **`RSK-10`** | **UV Yellowing or Dye Fading of Translucent Lilac SLA Resin** | Materials / Finish | Medium | Low | Factory UV-resistant clear urethane topcoat (`Clear Spraying` on PCBWay `UTR-8100` / JLC3DP `8001`); store out of direct midday sunlight. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Detailed Risk Analysis & Recovery Playbooks\n\n### `RSK-01` \u2014 Nintendo Server Telemetry Ban (`sysNAND` Contamination)\n- **Root Cause:** Running unsigned `.nsp` homebrew, custom user avatars, or modified crash logs on `sysNAND` (or allowing `emuNAND` without `exosphere` serial blanking to go online) flags the console's hardware certificate on Nintendo's CDN.\n- **Preventive Control:** Keep `sysNAND` 100% unmodified. Install Kefir CFW exclusively onto an SD card **`emuNAND` (SD Partition)** where Kefir's pre-configured `exosphere.ini` zeroes the prodinfo serial (`XAW00000000000`) and `hosts/default.txt` (`dns.mitm`) blocks all `*.nintendo.net` telemetry endpoints.\n- **Contingency / Recovery:** Restore the pre-modification raw `BOOT0/BOOT1` and `rawnand.bin` backup created in Hekate before connecting `sysNAND` to Wi-Fi.\n\n### `RSK-02` \u2014 Switch `M92T36` / `BQ24193` / `P13USB` IC Failure from Bad PD Negotiation\n- **Root Cause:** Early Switch v1 boards (`HAC-CPU-10/20`) are notorious for blowing the `M92T36` USB-C PD controller or `P13USB` video/data mux if subjected to over-voltage spikes or non-compliant `15V` PD resistor profiles.\n- **Preventive Control:** We use only an USB-IF / UN 38.3 compliant **`15V @ 3.0A` PD 3.0 power bank (`INIU P50-E1`)** paired with a reputable **`100W` PD 3.0 hub (`UGREEN Revodok 105` / `Baseus`)** and a **`5A` fast-acting inline blade fuse (`ELC-01`)**.\n- **Contingency / Recovery:** Never connect unbranded/DIY buck-boost modules directly to the Switch USB-C port. If `ELC-01` blows, inspect `CAB-01` and `HUB-01` for pin shorts before replacing the `5A` blade fuse.\n\n### `RSK-03` \u2014 Tearing the `53-Pin` MIPI DSI LCD Ribbon or Micro-Coax Antennas\n- **Root Cause:** Attempting to unbond the Switch LCD/digitizer from the midframe or extending the high-speed `53-pin` MIPI DSI ribbon across a laptop hinge almost always results in torn ZIF latches or black screens.\n- **Preventive Control:** Our architecture **never removes the mainboard, LCD, digitizer, fan, or Wi-Fi coax cables from the magnesium midframe** (`docs/teardown.md`). Only the plastic rear shell (`HAC-001`) and side Joy-Con rails (`2\u00d7 5` exterior `M2` screws) are removed, reducing teardown risk to near zero.\n- **Contingency / Recovery:** Keep the removed OEM rear backplate, metal kickstand bracket, and screws in a labeled storage bag so the Switch can be returned to its original handheld form factor in `< 15 minutes` at any time.\n\n### `RSK-04` \u2014 SLA Photopolymer Dimensional Shrinkage or Boss Cracking\n- **Root Cause:** SLA photopolymer resins (`UTR-8100`, `8001`, `9000R`) can exhibit `\u00b10.15%` post-cure shrinkage, and thermoset resins crack if a user attempts to heat-set brass inserts with a hot soldering iron or over-torques self-tapping screws.\n- **Preventive Control:**\n  1. Order the `18 g` [`cad/stl/test_fit_jig.stl`](../cad/stl/test_fit_jig.stl) first (`~\u20ac4.50`) to verify the Switch `M2` rail pitch, Planck corner ledge, hinge hole pattern, `MR63ZZ` bearing snap fit, and brass insert hole ladder (`-0.05 / 0.00 / +0.05 mm`).\n  2. All blind bosses use **cold-pressed + medium CA gel-bonded brass inserts (`MEC-03`)**, and all high-load joints (hinges and battery strap) use **through-bolts with captive stainless `DIN 934` hex nuts (`MEC-02`)**.\n- **Contingency / Recovery:** If a thin bezel part (`lid_bezel.stl`) arrives with slight shipping bow (`>0.5 mm`), warm gently with a hairdryer (`~45 \u00b0C` for `30 s`) and cool under a flat book for `10 minutes`.\n\n### `RSK-05` \u2014 Drop \u00d7 MIT Planck Keyboard Fails to Type in Stock Horizon OS (`NKRO`)\n- **Root Cause:** Custom QMK keyboards with `NKRO` (N-Key Rollover) enabled present a composite non-boot HID report descriptor that Linux (`hid-generic`) accepts natively, but Nintendo's stock Horizon OS USB HID stack completely ignores.\n- **Preventive Control:** Toggle `NKRO` **OFF** on the Planck using QMK Magic Key (`Lower + Raise + N`) or set `NKRO_ENABLE = no` in `rules.mk` so the keyboard presents a standard `6KRO` (`1-byte modifier + 6-byte keycode`) USB HID descriptor (`docs/wiring.md`).\n- **Contingency / Recovery:** Test the Planck in Horizon OS `System Settings \u2192 Change Console Nickname` (`TST-B2` in [`docs/testing.md`](testing.md)) before bolting down `base_top_deck`.\n\n### `RSK-06` \u2014 Internal Power Bank Puncture, Swelling, or Thermal Hazard\n- **Root Cause:** Uncertified bare LiPo pouch cells or metal screw tips protruding into a battery compartment can puncture the cell pouch during transport or vibration.\n- **Preventive Control:**\n  1. Only a hard-cased, **UN 38.3 / CE certified commercial power bank (`INIU Carry P50-E1`)** with built-in BMS over-current/over-temperature protection is used.\n  2. In [`cad/base_bottom.scad`](../cad/base_bottom.scad), the two `M3` retainer bosses are placed **`4.5 mm` outside** the battery bay perimeter walls, and the bank rests on `1.5 mm` shock-absorbing EVA foam above `8` passive intake louvers.\n- **Contingency / Recovery:** Inspect the power bank every `6 months` by unscrewing the `8\u00d7 M3` top-deck screws; if the bank shows any casing bulge, unbolt `battery_retainer.stl` (`2\u00d7 M3` screws) and replace the bank immediately.\n\n### `RSK-07` \u2014 SLA Enclosure Softening Near Heatsink Exhaust or Hinge Creep\n- **Root Cause:** Standard SLA resins have an `HDT` of `~52\u201358 \u00b0C`; blocking the Switch's top exhaust vent or subjecting thin resin hinge bosses to `0.40 N\u00b7m` bending torque at elevated temperatures can cause resin creep.\n- **Preventive Control:**\n  1. [`cad/lid_rear.scad`](../cad/lid_rear.scad) leaves a full `44 \u00d7 8 mm` unobstructed window over the Switch's top copper heatsink exhaust (`Y = 162 mm`) and `7` rear intake louvers (`Y = 55..85 mm`) directly over the blower intake.\n  2. The Southco `E6-10-301` torque hinges clamp across a solid `14 mm`-deep rear spine backed by stainless `M3` washers and captive `DIN 934` steel hex nuts.\n- **Contingency / Recovery:** Never operate the Switch with the clamshell lid closed (`0\u00b0`) while running a heavy 3D game; ensure L4T Ubuntu sleep-on-lid-close (`HandleLidSwitch=suspend` or manual sleep button press) is used before closing the deck.\n\n### `RSK-08` \u2014 Hinge USB-C Ribbon (`CAB-01`) Fatigue or RCM Payload Blockage by Hub\n- **Root Cause:** Repeated `0\u00b0\u2013120\u00b0` flexing can fatigue stiff round USB-C cables, and USB-C hubs block the raw USB 2.0 `APX` bulk transfer required by `fusee-gelee` RCM payload injection.\n- **Preventive Control:**\n  1. `CAB-01` is an ultra-flat `0.5 mm`-thick flexible polyimide FPC ribbon rated for `>10,000` flex cycles, routed through a `22 \u00d7 6 mm` central hinge slot with a `15 mm` rolling service loop clamped at both ends by [`cad/cable_clamp.scad`](../cad/cable_clamp.scad).\n  2. The `CAB-01` female coupler sits inside the **recessed rear center pocket (`44 \u00d7 12 mm`)** of [`cad/base_bottom.scad`](../cad/base_bottom.scad#L190-L196), allowing you to unplug `HUB-01` in `2 seconds` to inject RCM payloads directly over `CAB-01`.\n- **Contingency / Recovery:** Keep a spare `\u20ac3.40` `20 cm` 90\u00b0 flat USB-C FPC ribbon (`CAB-01`) on hand; replacing it requires removing only the `6\u00d7` lid bezel screws and `2\u00d7` cable clamp screws.\n\n### `RSK-09` \u2014 Parasitic Power Bank Drain During Storage\n- **Root Cause:** Leaving a USB-C PD hub (`HUB-01`) permanently plugged into a power bank draws `35\u201380 mA` continuously (`~8\u201318 Wh/day`), draining a `37 Wh` power bank completely flat in `2\u20134 days` when the cyberdeck is turned off.\n- **Preventive Control:** The rear-panel **Master Power Cutoff Switch (`ELC-02`)** physically breaks the `VBUS` line between the power bank and `HUB-01` when flipped OFF (`0.0 mA` storage drain).\n- **Contingency / Recovery:** Always flip `ELC-02` to **OFF** when shutting down or stowing the cyberdeck in a backpack.\n\n### `RSK-10` \u2014 UV Yellowing or Dye Fading of Translucent SLA Resin\n- **Root Cause:** Uncoated photopolymer SLA resins (`UTR-8100`, `8001`) slowly yellow and turn brittle when exposed to prolonged outdoor UV-A/UV-B sunlight (`315\u2013400 nm`).\n- **Preventive Control:** The PCBWay (`UTR-8100`) and JLC3DP (`8001`) print specifications in [`docs/print-spec.md`](print-spec.md) include a **factory-applied UV-resistant clear urethane topcoat (`Clear Spraying`)** that blocks UV degradation while preserving optical clarity.\n- **Contingency / Recovery:** Store the cyberdeck in a padded `12\"` laptop sleeve when not in use and avoid leaving it on a sunlit windowsill.\n",
  "datasheets": "# Hardware Datasheets, Pinouts & Mechanical References (`hardware/datasheets.md`)\n\nThis file indexes the official datasheets, open-source CAD repositories, and connector pinouts referenced in [`docs/wiring.md`](../docs/wiring.md) and [`cad/config.scad`](../cad/).\n\n---\n\n## 1. Nintendo Switch v1 (`MOD. HAC-001`) Hardware References\n\n- **Battery Charger IC:** Texas Instruments `BQ24193` (`I2C` 4.5A Single-Cell USB-PD/Adapter Charger)\n  - Datasheet: [https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/bq24193.pdf](https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/bq24193.pdf)\n- **USB-PD Controller:** ROHM `BM92T36` (USB Type-C Power Delivery Controller supporting `5V` / `15V` sink profiles and DisplayPort Alt-Mode)\n- **Right Joy-Con Rail 10-Pin Connector Pinout (Facing Rail Contacts, Top = Pin 1, Bottom = Pin 10):**\n\n| Pin | Signal Name | Function | Cyberdeck Usage |\n| :-: | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **1** | `GND` | Ground Return (also tied to metal rail chassis) | **Used:** Common ground side of `RCM-01` momentary tactile button |\n| **2** | `TX` | Joy-Con UART Transmit (`1.8V`/`3.3V`) | Untouched |\n| **3** | `DET` | Joy-Con Insertion Detect | Untouched |\n| **4** | `GND` | Signal Ground | Untouched |\n| **5** | `RX` | Joy-Con UART Receive | Untouched |\n| **6** | `5V0_OUT` | `+5.0V` Joy-Con Charging Rail | **WARNING: DO NOT SHORT!** Keep isolated |\n| **7** | `GND` | Power Ground | Alternative Ground for `RCM-01` |\n| **8** | `UART_RTS` | Flow Control / Handshake | Untouched |\n| **9** | `NFC_OR_PWR`| Secondary Joy-Con Rail Signal (`+5V` adjacent) | **WARNING: DO NOT SHORT TO PIN 10!** |\n| **10**| **`HOME / RCM`** | **Tegra X1 BootROM Recovery Mode Strap (Active Low)** | **Used:** Wired via `RCM-01` momentary switch to **Pin 1 (`GND`)** |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Drop \u00d7 OLKB MIT Planck (Rev 6.x) CAD & Schematic References\n\n- **Official Open-Source Mechanical Parts & DXF Plates (`olkb/olkb_parts`):**\n  - Repository: [https://github.com/olkb/olkb_parts/tree/master/planck](https://github.com/olkb/olkb_parts/tree/master/planck)\n- **Official QMK Firmware Definition (`keyboards/planck/rev6`):**\n  - MCU: STMicroelectronics `STM32F303CBT6` (ARM Cortex-M4, `72 MHz`, Hardware USB 2.0 Full-Speed)\n  - Datasheet: [https://www.st.com/resource/en/datasheet/stm32f303cb.pdf](https://www.st.com/resource/en/datasheet/stm32f303cb.pdf)\n  - PCB Dimensions: `233.00 mm \u00d7 81.00 mm \u00d7 1.60 mm`\n\n---\n\n## 3. Trackball Subsystem (`Ploopy Nano 2` / `RP2040-Zero` + `PMW3360`)\n\n- **Ploopy Nano Open-Source STEP/STL & PCB Repository:**\n  - Repository: [https://github.com/ploopyco/nano-trackball](https://github.com/ploopyco/nano-trackball)\n- **Raspberry Pi `RP2040` Microcontroller (`Waveshare RP2040-Zero`):**\n  - RP2040 Datasheet: [https://datasheets.raspberrypi.com/rp2040/rp2040-datasheet.pdf](https://datasheets.raspberrypi.com/rp2040/rp2040-datasheet.pdf)\n  - Waveshare RP2040-Zero Wiki & Pinout (`23.5 \u00d7 18.0 mm`): [https://www.waveshare.com/wiki/RP2040-Zero](https://www.waveshare.com/wiki/RP2040-Zero)\n- **PixArt `PMW3360DM-T2QU` Optical Navigation Sensor:**\n  - Operating Voltage: `3.3V` (`VDD` max `3.6V` \u2014 **not 5V tolerant on `VDD`**)\n  - Interface: 4-Wire SPI (`SCK`, `MISO`, `MOSI`, `NCS`, up to `2 MHz` clock, `12,000 CPI`)\n  - Lens-to-Ball Surface Working Distance (`Z` height from PCB bottom of lens flange to bottom of `38.0 mm` ball): **`2.40 mm \u00b1 0.15 mm`**\n\n---\n\n## 4. Mechanical Hinges & SLA Photopolymer Resin Datasheets\n\n- **Southco `E6-10-301-20` Adjustable Friction Torque Position Hinge (`42.9 \u00d7 36.5 \u00d7 12.7 mm`):**\n  - Southco E6 Series Catalog & CAD Drawing: [https://southco.com/en_eu_int/e6-constant-torque-position-control-hinges](https://southco.com/en_eu_int/e6-constant-torque-position-control-hinges)\n  - Mounting Holes: `4\u00d7 \u00d84.4 mm` through-holes (compatible with `M4` or `M3` screws + washers; leaf hole centers: `25.4 mm` horizontal span \u00d7 `19.1 mm` vertical span).\n  - Torque Range: `0.00 to 0.80 N\u00b7m` static friction torque per hinge (adjusted via central Phillips screw).\n- **JLC3DP `SLA 8001 Translucent Resin` Technical Specifications:**\n  - Material Guide: [https://jlc3dp.com/3d-printing-quote](https://jlc3dp.com/3d-printing-quote)\n  - Tensile Strength: `~52 MPa` | Flexural Modulus: `~2,300 MPa` | Heat Deflection Temp (`HDT @ 0.45 MPa`): `~54\u201358\u00b0C`.\n"
};
window.NS_CONV_SCAD = {
  "assembly_preview.scad": "// ============================================================================\n// ns-conv: Nintendo Switch v1 (Erista) -> Clamshell Cyberdeck Conversion\n// File: cad/assembly_preview.scad\n// Purpose: Complete Clamshell Assembly Model (Open at 112-deg or Closed at 0-deg)\n//          Shows all custom Translucent Lilac SLA parts assembled with\n//          reference models of the Switch v1 Core, Drop x MIT Planck Rev 6,\n//          38mm Trackball, Southco E6 Hinges, INIU 45W Power Bank, and Hub.\n// ============================================================================\n\ninclude <config.scad>\nuse <base_bottom.scad>\nuse <base_top_deck.scad>\nuse <lid_rear.scad>\nuse <lid_bezel.scad>\nuse <battery_retainer.scad>\nuse <cable_clamp.scad>\n\n// Open angle in degrees: 0 = Closed Clamshell, 112 = Ergonomic Typing Angle (100-120 deg)\nlid_open_angle = 112;\nexploded_z     = 0; // Set >0 for exploded assembly view\n\n// Colors matching Translucent Lilac SLA & Donor Hardware\nc_lilac_shell = [0.74, 0.56, 0.88, 0.78]; // Translucent Lilac SLA (UTR-8100 / 8001 + Royal Purple dye)\nc_lilac_trim  = [0.66, 0.46, 0.82, 0.85]; // Slightly deeper lilac for bezel & straps\nc_switch_body = [0.16, 0.17, 0.19, 1.00]; // Switch magnesium midframe & black glass bezel\nc_switch_lcd  = [0.10, 0.48, 0.72, 1.00]; // 6.2\" LCD active screen\nc_planck_plate= [0.22, 0.22, 0.25, 1.00]; // Anodized Planck switch plate\nc_keycap_al   = [0.90, 0.90, 0.93, 1.00]; // Planck alpha keycaps\nc_keycap_mod  = [0.35, 0.32, 0.45, 1.00]; // Planck modifier keycaps\nc_keycap_spc  = [0.55, 0.35, 0.75, 1.00]; // MIT 2u spacebar accent\nc_trackball   = [0.82, 0.16, 0.22, 1.00]; // 38mm Crimson Snooker Trackball\nc_hinge       = [0.14, 0.14, 0.16, 1.00]; // Southco E6-10-301-20 black acetal hinge\nc_pbank       = [0.18, 0.20, 0.24, 1.00]; // INIU 45W Slim Power Bank\n\n// Reference Model: Drop x MIT Planck 47-Key Ortholinear Keyboard\nmodule ref_planck_keyboard() {\n    translate([planck_x0, planck_y0, base_bottom_h + base_top_h - planck_plate_t - 0.5]) {\n        // 1.5mm Switch Plate\n        color(c_planck_plate)\n            cube([planck_w, planck_d, planck_plate_t]);\n\n        // 4x12 Ortholinear Keycap Grid (with 2u MIT Spacebar at Row 0, Col 5..6)\n        pitch = 19.05;\n        x_start = (planck_w - 12 * pitch) / 2;\n        y_start = (planck_d - 4 * pitch) / 2;\n\n        for (r = [0 : 3], c = [0 : 11]) {\n            // In row 0 (bottom row), col 5 & 6 form a single 2u MIT spacebar\n            if (!(r == 0 && c == 6)) {\n                is_space = (r == 0 && c == 5);\n                is_mod   = (r == 0 || c == 0 || c == 11);\n                kw = is_space ? (2 * pitch - 1.8) : (pitch - 1.8);\n                kh = pitch - 1.8;\n\n                color(is_space ? c_keycap_spc : (is_mod ? c_keycap_mod : c_keycap_al))\n                    translate([x_start + c * pitch + 0.9, y_start + r * pitch + 0.9, planck_plate_t])\n                        hull() {\n                            cube([kw, kh, 1.0]);\n                            translate([1.8, 1.8, 7.5])\n                                cube([kw - 3.6, kh - 3.6, 1.0]);\n                        }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// Reference Model: Nintendo Switch v1 Core Module (166.5 x 102.0 x 11.8mm)\nmodule ref_switch_core() {\n    translate([sw_center_x - sw_core_w/2, sw_bottom_y, lid_rear_h - sw_core_thick - 1.25]) {\n        color(c_switch_body)\n            cube([sw_core_w, sw_core_h, sw_core_thick]);\n        // Active 6.2\" LCD Panel\n        color(c_switch_lcd)\n            translate([\n                (sw_core_w - sw_screen_view_w)/2,\n                (sw_core_h - sw_screen_view_h)/2,\n                sw_core_thick - 0.5\n            ])\n                cube([sw_screen_view_w, sw_screen_view_h, 0.8]);\n    }\n}\n\n// Reference Model: Southco E6-10-301-20 Hinges\nmodule ref_hinges() {\n    for (hx = [-hinge_x_offset, hinge_x_offset]) {\n        color(c_hinge) {\n            // Base Hinge Leaf\n            translate([hx - hinge_w/2, deck_d - 16.0, base_bottom_h - hinge_leaf_t])\n                cube([hinge_w, 16.0, hinge_leaf_t]);\n            // Hinge Knuckle Barrel at Pivot Axis (Y = deck_d - 6.0, Z = base_total_h)\n            translate([hx - hinge_w/2, deck_d - 6.0, base_total_h])\n                rotate([0, 90, 0])\n                    cylinder(d = hinge_knuckle_d, h = hinge_w);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nmodule full_cyberdeck_assembly() {\n    // ------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    // 1. LOWER BASE ASSEMBLY\n    // ------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    color(c_lilac_shell)\n        base_bottom();\n\n    // Internal INIU 45W Slim Power Bank + Retainer Strap\n    color(c_pbank)\n        translate([-deck_w/2 + 18.5, 20.5, wall_thick + pbank_foam_t])\n            cube([pbank_w, pbank_d, pbank_h]);\n\n    color(c_lilac_trim)\n        translate([-deck_w/2 + 18.0 + pbank_w/2, 20.0 + (pbank_d + 1.0)/2, wall_thick + pbank_h + pbank_foam_t])\n            battery_retainer();\n\n    // Base Top Deck (Planck Tray + Trackball Socket)\n    color(c_lilac_trim)\n        translate([0, 0, base_bottom_h + exploded_z])\n            base_top_deck();\n\n    // Donor Drop x MIT Planck Keyboard\n    translate([0, 0, exploded_z])\n        ref_planck_keyboard();\n\n    // 38.0mm Trackball Sphere\n    color(c_trackball)\n        translate([tball_cx, tball_cy, base_bottom_h + 2.5 + exploded_z])\n            sphere(d = tball_d);\n\n    // Southco Adjustable Friction Torque Hinges\n    ref_hinges();\n\n    // ------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    // 2. UPPER LID ASSEMBLY (Rotated around Hinge Pivot Axis at Y = deck_d - 6.0)\n    //    At lid_open_angle = 0 (closed): rotate([180, 0, 0]) folds lid flat over\n    //    base with screen facing down (-Z).\n    //    At lid_open_angle = 112 (open): rotate([68, 0, 0]) raises lid upward\n    //    at 112 deg to the keyboard deck with the Switch screen facing forward (-Y).\n    // ------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    pivot_y = deck_d - 6.0;\n    pivot_z = base_total_h + 2.0;\n\n    translate([0, pivot_y, pivot_z + exploded_z * 1.5])\n        rotate([180 - lid_open_angle, 0, 0])\n            translate([0, -6.0, -lid_total_h]) {\n                // Upper Lid Rear Shell\n                color(c_lilac_shell)\n                    lid_rear();\n\n                // Donor Nintendo Switch v1 Core Module\n                ref_switch_core();\n\n                // Upper Lid Front Bezel Retainer\n                color(c_lilac_trim)\n                    translate([0, 0, lid_rear_h + exploded_z * 0.8])\n                        lid_bezel();\n            }\n}\n\nfull_cyberdeck_assembly();\n",
  "base_bottom.scad": "// ============================================================================\n// ns-conv: Nintendo Switch v1 (Erista) -> Clamshell Cyberdeck Conversion\n// File: cad/base_bottom.scad\n// Part: Lower Base Enclosure (Translucent Lilac SLA)\n// Features:\n//   - Outer rounded tub (306 x 162 x 24.5 mm) with 2.5mm uniform walls\n//   - Ergonomic front wrist bevel (12-deg comfort slope)\n//   - Isolated INIU 45W Slim Power Bank bay (110x68x18.5mm) with bottom intake\n//     louvers and external M3 retention bosses (>=4.5mm away from cell wall)\n//   - Internal 100W USB-C PD Hub cradle (115x27.5x12.2mm) with right-side\n//     flush cutouts for spare USB 3.0 Type-A and 4K HDMI ports\n//   - Rear Recessed Mode/Charging Coupler Pocket (Panel USB-C PD In + Switch\n//     Direct USB-C coupler clip + Power Cutoff Switch window)\n//   - Left & Right Southco E6-10-301-20 adjustable torque hinge pads with\n//     M4/M3 through-holes and underside hex-nut traps\n//   - 8x M3 perimeter mounting bosses for base_top_deck.scad\n// ============================================================================\n\ninclude <config.scad>\n\n// Coordinate system: X=0 at center, Y=0 at front edge, Z=0 at bottom floor\n\n// Power bank bay origin (Front-Left quadrant under Planck)\npbank_bay_x0 = -deck_w/2 + 18.0;\npbank_bay_y0 = 20.0;\n\n// Internal USB-C PD Hub origin (Rear-Right quadrant)\nhub_bay_x0   = 22.0;\nhub_bay_y0   = 105.0;\n\n// 8x M3 Top-Deck Mounting Boss Coordinates [x, y]\nbase_boss_pts = [\n    [-deck_w/2 + 6.5,  10.0],\n    [ 0.0,             10.0],\n    [ deck_w/2 - 6.5,  10.0],\n    [-deck_w/2 + 6.5,  80.0],\n    [ deck_w/2 - 6.5,  80.0],\n    [-deck_w/2 + 6.5,  140.0],\n    [ 0.0,             140.0],\n    [ deck_w/2 - 6.5,  140.0]\n];\n\nmodule base_bottom() {\n    difference() {\n        union() {\n            // 1. Main Outer Shell Tub\n            difference() {\n                rounded_box_xcenter(deck_w, deck_d, base_bottom_h, corner_r);\n\n                // Ergonomic front wrist chamfer along Y=0 top edge\n                translate([-deck_w/2 - 1, -1.0, base_bottom_h - 4.5])\n                    rotate([32, 0, 0])\n                        cube([deck_w + 2, 12.0, 12.0]);\n\n                // Main interior hollow cavity (leaves 2.5mm floor and 2.5mm walls)\n                translate([0, wall_thick, wall_thick])\n                    rounded_box_xcenter(\n                        deck_w - 2*wall_thick,\n                        deck_d - 2*wall_thick - 14.0, // Reserves solid 14mm rear hinge spine block\n                        base_bottom_h,\n                        corner_r - wall_thick\n                    );\n\n                // Rear coupler & cable routing bay in the spine between the two hinges\n                translate([-hinge_x_offset + hinge_w/2 + 8.0, deck_d - 22.0, wall_thick + 2.0])\n                    cube([\n                        2*(hinge_x_offset - hinge_w/2 - 8.0),\n                        22.0 - wall_thick,\n                        base_bottom_h\n                    ]);\n            }\n\n            // 2. Internal Structural Grid Ribs (1.8mm thick for uniform SLA dye tint)\n            for (rx = [-65.0, 15.0, 85.0]) {\n                translate([rx - rib_thick/2, wall_thick - eps, wall_thick - eps])\n                    cube([rib_thick, deck_d - 18.0, 3.0 + eps]);\n            }\n            for (ry = [55.0, 98.0]) {\n                translate([-deck_w/2 + wall_thick - eps, ry - rib_thick/2, wall_thick - eps])\n                    cube([deck_w - 2*wall_thick + 2*eps, rib_thick, 3.0 + eps]);\n            }\n\n            // 3. Power Bank Containment Perimeter Walls (1.8mm walls, +1.0mm slip + foam margin)\n            translate([pbank_bay_x0 - rib_thick, pbank_bay_y0 - rib_thick, wall_thick - eps])\n                difference() {\n                    cube([pbank_w + 2*rib_thick + 1.0, pbank_d + 2*rib_thick + 1.0, 12.0 + eps]);\n                    translate([rib_thick, rib_thick, -eps])\n                        cube([pbank_w + 1.0, pbank_d + 1.0, 12.0 + 3*eps]);\n                    // Cable exit notch on right side of power bank bay\n                    translate([pbank_w, 12.0, 2.0])\n                        cube([rib_thick + 2.0, 44.0, 12.0]);\n                }\n\n            // 4. External Power Bank Retainer Strap Bosses (4.5mm clear of battery casing!)\n            for (sy = [-pbank_safe_gap, pbank_d + 1.0 + pbank_safe_gap]) {\n                translate([pbank_bay_x0 + pbank_w/2, pbank_bay_y0 + sy, wall_thick - eps])\n                    cylinder(d = 9.0, h = pbank_h + pbank_foam_t + eps);\n            }\n\n            // 5. Internal 100W USB-C PD Hub Cradle Ribs (Rear-Right)\n            translate([hub_bay_x0 - rib_thick, hub_bay_y0 - rib_thick, wall_thick - eps])\n                difference() {\n                    cube([hub_w + 2*rib_thick + 0.6, hub_d + 2*rib_thick + 0.6, 9.0 + eps]);\n                    translate([rib_thick, rib_thick, -eps])\n                        cube([hub_w + 0.6, hub_d + 0.6, 9.0 + 3*eps]);\n                    // Upstream & downstream cable slots on left and front walls\n                    translate([-eps, 4.0, 1.5])\n                        cube([rib_thick + 2.0, hub_d - 6.0, 9.0]);\n                    translate([10.0, -eps, 1.5])\n                        cube([hub_w - 20.0, rib_thick + 2.0, 9.0]);\n                }\n\n            // 6. 8x M3 Perimeter Standoff Pillars for Base Top Deck\n            for (pt = base_boss_pts) {\n                translate([pt[0], pt[1], wall_thick - eps])\n                    cylinder(d = 8.5, h = base_bottom_h - wall_thick + eps);\n            }\n        }\n\n        // ====================================================================\n        // SUBTRACTIONS (Vents, Fastener Bores, Hinge Mounts, Rear/Side I/O)\n        // ====================================================================\n\n        // A. Power Bank Retainer M3 Through-Holes + Bottom Hex-Nut Traps\n        for (sy = [-pbank_safe_gap, pbank_d + 1.0 + pbank_safe_gap]) {\n            translate([pbank_bay_x0 + pbank_w/2, pbank_bay_y0 + sy, -eps]) {\n                cylinder(d = m3_thru_d, h = base_bottom_h + 2);\n                hex_nut_trap(m3_nut_w, m3_nut_h + eps);\n            }\n        }\n\n        // B. 8x M3 Top-Deck Boss Bores (Knurled Brass Insert Bores from Top + M3 Thru)\n        for (pt = base_boss_pts) {\n            translate([pt[0], pt[1], base_bottom_h - m3_insert_h])\n                cylinder(d = m3_insert_d, h = m3_insert_h + eps);\n            translate([pt[0], pt[1], wall_thick])\n                cylinder(d = m3_thru_d, h = base_bottom_h);\n        }\n\n        // C. Bottom Passive Intake Ventilation Louvers Under Power Bank Bay\n        for (i = [0 : 7]) {\n            translate([pbank_bay_x0 + 12.0 + i * 11.5, pbank_bay_y0 + 12.0, -eps])\n                hull() {\n                    cylinder(d = 3.2, h = wall_thick + 2*eps);\n                    translate([0, pbank_d - 24.0, 0])\n                        cylinder(d = 3.2, h = wall_thick + 2*eps);\n                }\n        }\n\n        // D. Bottom Ventilation Louvers Under USB-C PD Hub Bay\n        for (i = [0 : 6]) {\n            translate([hub_bay_x0 + 14.0 + i * 13.0, hub_bay_y0 + 5.0, -eps])\n                hull() {\n                    cylinder(d = 3.0, h = wall_thick + 2*eps);\n                    translate([0, hub_d - 10.0, 0])\n                        cylinder(d = 3.0, h = wall_thick + 2*eps);\n                }\n        }\n\n        // E. Left & Right Southco E6-10-301-20 Hinge Leaf Pockets & M4/M3 Bolt Holes\n        for (hx = [-hinge_x_offset, hinge_x_offset]) {\n            // Recessed seat for lower hinge leaf on rear spine top\n            translate([hx - (hinge_w + 0.5)/2, deck_d - 16.0, base_bottom_h - hinge_leaf_t])\n                cube([hinge_w + 0.5, 16.5, hinge_leaf_t + eps]);\n\n            // 2x Mounting bolts per base hinge leaf + underside M4/M3 hex nut traps\n            for (dx = [-hinge_hole_span_x/2, hinge_hole_span_x/2]) {\n                translate([hx + dx, deck_d - 8.5, -eps]) {\n                    cylinder(d = m3_thru_d + 0.2, h = base_bottom_h + 2*eps);\n                    hex_nut_trap(m3_nut_w + 0.1, m3_nut_h + 1.5);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        // F. Rear Panel-Mount USB-C PD Charging Input Port (CAB-03, X = -42mm)\n        translate([-42.0, deck_d + eps, 12.0])\n            rotate([90, 0, 0]) {\n                // Rounded USB-C nose cutout\n                hull() {\n                    for (sx = [-1, 1])\n                        translate([sx * (panel_usbc_hole_w/2 - panel_usbc_hole_h/2), 0, 0])\n                            cylinder(d = panel_usbc_hole_h, h = 10.0);\n                }\n                // 2x M2/M3 panel-mount screw ears (16.0mm span)\n                for (sx = [-1, 1])\n                    translate([sx * panel_usbc_span/2, 0, 0])\n                        cylinder(d = m2_thru_d, h = 10.0);\n            }\n\n        // G. Rear Recessed Mode Coupler Pocket & Hinge USB-C Ribbon Entry (Center X = 0)\n        // Allows unplugging HUB-01 from CAB-01 to inject RCM payload from external PC/dongle\n        translate([-22.0, deck_d - 12.0, 8.0])\n            cube([44.0, 12.0 + eps, base_bottom_h]);\n        // Central hinge channel slot for 20cm 90-deg flat USB-C ribbon (CAB-01)\n        translate([-11.0, deck_d - 22.0, base_bottom_h - 6.0])\n            cube([22.0, 22.0 + eps, 6.0 + eps]);\n        // 2x M2 Brass Insert bores for Rear Coupler Strain-Relief Clamp (cable_clamp.scad)\n        for (sx = [-14.0, 14.0]) {\n            translate([sx, deck_d - 16.0, 4.0])\n                cylinder(d = m2_insert_d, h = m2_insert_h + 1.0);\n        }\n\n        // H. Rear Power Cutoff Slide/Rocker Switch Window (ELC-02, X = +42mm)\n        translate([35.0, deck_d - wall_thick - 2.0, 8.5])\n            cube([14.0, wall_thick + 4.0, 9.5]);\n\n        // I. Right-Side Flush Cutout Window for Hub Spare USB-A 3.0 & 4K HDMI Ports\n        translate([deck_w/2 - wall_thick - 1.0, hub_bay_y0 + 3.0, wall_thick + 1.5])\n            cube([wall_thick + 2.0, hub_d - 4.0, 11.0]);\n\n        // J. 4x Bottom Corner Recesses (\u00d810.4 x 0.8mm) for Self-Adhesive Silicone Feet (MEC-04)\n        for (fx = [-deck_w/2 + 18.0, deck_w/2 - 18.0], fy = [18.0, deck_d - 18.0]) {\n            translate([fx, fy, -eps])\n                cylinder(d = 10.4, h = 0.8 + eps);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nbase_bottom();\n",
  "base_top_deck.scad": "// ============================================================================\n// ns-conv: Nintendo Switch v1 (Erista) -> Clamshell Cyberdeck Conversion\n// File: cad/base_top_deck.scad\n// Part: Base Top Deck \u2014 Recessed Drop x MIT Planck Rev 6 Tray + Right-Side\n//       38mm QMK Trackball Socket (Translucent Lilac SLA)\n// Features:\n//   - Full-width top plate (306 x 146 x 4.0 mm) + 11.0mm recessed Planck tray\n//   - 2.0mm solid SLA barrier floor beneath the Planck PCB (physically and\n//     thermally isolating the hotswap sockets from the INIU power bank below)\n//   - 5x Slotted M2 OLKB Planck Rev 6 mounting bosses + 2.0mm perimeter shelf\n//   - Integrated Right-Side Contoured 38.0mm Trackball Cup with 3x MR63ZZ\n//     (3x6x2.5mm) roller bearing seats at 120-deg intervals, optical sensor\n//     aperture, and underside PMW3360 / Ploopy Nano sensor mounting pocket\n//   - 2x Optional 14.0x14.0mm Cherry MX thumb-click switch cutouts below ball\n// ============================================================================\n\ninclude <config.scad>\n\n// Coordinate system matches base_bottom.scad:\n// X=0 at center, Y=0 at front edge, Z=0 at top surface of base_bottom (Z=24.5mm in assembly)\n\ndeck_plate_d = deck_d - 16.0; // Leaves rear 16.0mm hinge spine exposed on base_bottom\ntray_drop_z  = 11.5;          // Depth of Planck PCB pocket below top deck plane\nbarrier_t    = 2.0;           // Solid SLA floor thickness isolating Planck from power bank\n\n// Same 8x M3 Mounting Boss X/Y coordinates as base_bottom.scad\nbase_boss_pts = [\n    [-deck_w/2 + 6.5,  10.0],\n    [ 0.0,             10.0],\n    [ deck_w/2 - 6.5,  10.0],\n    [-deck_w/2 + 6.5,  80.0],\n    [ deck_w/2 - 6.5,  80.0],\n    [-deck_w/2 + 6.5,  140.0],\n    [ 0.0,             140.0],\n    [ deck_w/2 - 6.5,  140.0]\n];\n\nmodule base_top_deck() {\n    difference() {\n        union() {\n            // 1. Main Top Deck Plate (Z = 0 to base_top_h = 4.0mm)\n            difference() {\n                rounded_box_xcenter(deck_w, deck_plate_d, base_top_h, corner_r);\n                // Front wrist comfort bevel matching base_bottom\n                translate([-deck_w/2 - 1, -1.0, base_top_h - 2.2])\n                    rotate([28, 0, 0])\n                        cube([deck_w + 2, 8.0, 6.0]);\n            }\n\n            // 2. Dropped Planck Tray Box & 2.0mm Power-Bank Isolation Floor\n            //    Extends downward into base_bottom cavity (Z = -tray_drop_z to 0)\n            translate([planck_x0 - wall_thick, planck_y0 - wall_thick, -tray_drop_z])\n                cube([\n                    planck_w + 2*wall_thick,\n                    planck_d + 2*wall_thick,\n                    tray_drop_z + eps\n                ]);\n\n            // 3. Contoured 38.0mm Trackball Socket Housing (Right of Planck)\n            translate([tball_cx, tball_cy, 0]) {\n                // Raised ergonomic volcano rim (+3.5mm above deck) + lower cup (-16.5mm below deck)\n                translate([0, 0, -16.5])\n                    cylinder(d1 = tball_d + 10.0, d2 = tball_d + 13.0, h = 16.5 + base_top_h + 3.0);\n            }\n\n            // 4. Underside Locator Lip around Perimeter (drops 1.8mm into base_bottom)\n            translate([0, wall_thick + sla_clear_slip, -1.8])\n                difference() {\n                    rounded_box_xcenter(\n                        deck_w - 2*(wall_thick + sla_clear_slip),\n                        deck_plate_d - wall_thick - sla_clear_slip,\n                        1.8 + eps,\n                        corner_r - wall_thick\n                    );\n                    translate([0, rib_thick, -eps])\n                        rounded_box_xcenter(\n                            deck_w - 2*(wall_thick + sla_clear_slip + rib_thick),\n                            deck_plate_d - wall_thick - 2*rib_thick,\n                            1.8 + 3*eps,\n                            corner_r - wall_thick - rib_thick\n                        );\n                }\n        }\n\n        // ====================================================================\n        // SUBTRACTIONS (Planck Recess, M2 Bosses, Trackball Cup, MX Switches)\n        // ====================================================================\n\n        // A. Drop x MIT Planck Switch Plate Upper Recess (233.4 x 81.4 x 2.0mm)\n        //    Supports the 1.5mm switch plate on a 2.0mm perimeter ledge\n        translate([\n            planck_x0 - sla_clear_slip,\n            planck_y0 - sla_clear_slip,\n            base_top_h - (planck_plate_t + 0.5)\n        ])\n            cube([\n                planck_w + 2*sla_clear_slip,\n                planck_d + 2*sla_clear_slip,\n                planck_plate_t + 1.0\n            ]);\n\n        // B. Planck PCB & Hotswap Socket Inner Cavity (inset by planck_lip_w = 2.0mm)\n        //    Leaves a solid 2.0mm barrier floor at the bottom (Z = -tray_drop_z to -tray_drop_z + barrier_t)\n        difference() {\n            translate([\n                planck_x0 + planck_lip_w,\n                planck_y0 + planck_lip_w,\n                -tray_drop_z + barrier_t\n            ])\n                cube([\n                    planck_w - 2*planck_lip_w,\n                    planck_d - 2*planck_lip_w,\n                    tray_drop_z + base_top_h\n                ]);\n\n            // Keep 5x OLKB Planck Rev 6 M2 Standoff Boss Pillars inside the cavity\n            for (pt = planck_mount_pts) {\n                translate([planck_x0 + pt[0], planck_y0 + pt[1], -tray_drop_z + barrier_t - eps])\n                    cylinder(d = 7.5, h = (tray_drop_z - barrier_t) + (base_top_h - planck_plate_t - 0.5));\n            }\n        }\n\n        // C. 5x Slotted M2 Through-Holes + Underside Hex Nut Traps for Planck PCB\n        for (pt = planck_mount_pts) {\n            translate([planck_x0 + pt[0], planck_y0 + pt[1], -tray_drop_z - eps]) {\n                // +-0.8mm X/Y slot tolerance so both Lo-Pro and Hi-Pro Rev 6 plates align effortlessly\n                hull() {\n                    translate([-0.6, 0, 0]) cylinder(d = m2_thru_d, h = tray_drop_z + base_top_h + 2*eps);\n                    translate([ 0.6, 0, 0]) cylinder(d = m2_thru_d, h = tray_drop_z + base_top_h + 2*eps);\n                }\n                hex_nut_trap(m2_nut_w, m2_nut_h + eps);\n            }\n        }\n\n        // D. Planck Rear USB-C Receptacle & 15cm Cable Exit Window (CAB-02a)\n        translate([\n            planck_x0 + planck_usbc_x_off - 9.0,\n            planck_y0 + planck_d - planck_lip_w - 1.0,\n            -tray_drop_z + barrier_t\n        ])\n            cube([18.0, planck_lip_w + wall_thick + 3.0, tray_drop_z]);\n\n        // E. Planck Bottom Reset Button Access Pinhole (Center-Left of Planck Floor)\n        translate([planck_x0 + 96.0, planck_y0 + 38.0, -tray_drop_z - eps])\n            cylinder(d = 4.0, h = barrier_t + 2*eps);\n\n        // F. 38.0mm Trackball Spherical Socket & 3x MR63ZZ Roller Bearing Seats\n        //    Ball center sits at Z = +2.5mm so 56% of the 38mm ball protrudes ergonomically\n        tball_cz = 2.50;\n        tball_r  = tball_d/2 + tball_cup_clear; // 19.65mm socket radius\n\n        translate([tball_cx, tball_cy, tball_cz]) {\n            // Spherical ball cavity\n            sphere(r = tball_r);\n            // Upper clearance bore so the 38.0mm ball drops in cleanly from the top\n            cylinder(r = tball_r - 0.2, h = 25.0);\n\n            // 3x MR63ZZ (3x6x2.5mm) Roller Bearing Seats at 120-deg intervals, 35-deg from bottom pole\n            for (ang = [0, 120, 240]) {\n                rotate([0, 0, ang + 30])\n                    rotate([tball_bearing_ang, 0, 0])\n                        translate([0, 0, -tball_r - 1.2]) {\n                            // Bearing outer wheel clearance slot (\u00d86.6 x 3.0mm)\n                            rotate([0, 90, 0])\n                                cylinder(d = tball_bearing_od + 0.6, h = tball_bearing_w + 0.6, center = true);\n                            // M3 / 3.0mm Dowel Pin axle cradle slot\n                            rotate([0, 90, 0])\n                                cylinder(d = tball_bearing_id + 0.1, h = 11.0, center = true);\n                        }\n            }\n\n            // Bottom Optical Sensor Aperture (8.0 x 8.0mm lens window at bottom pole)\n            translate([0, 0, -tball_r - 6.0])\n                cylinder(d = 9.0, h = 10.0);\n\n            // Underside Pocket for PMW3360 Sensor Breakout / Ploopy Nano PCB\n            // Positioned so lens surface sits 2.40mm below the 38mm ball bottom pole\n            translate([-tball_sensor_w/2, -tball_sensor_d/2, -tball_r - tball_lens_gap - 6.0])\n                cube([tball_sensor_w, tball_sensor_d, 6.2]);\n\n            // 2x M2 Brass Insert Bores to retain the PMW3360 Sensor Bracket\n            for (sx = [-11.5, 11.5]) {\n                translate([sx, 0, -tball_r - 5.5])\n                    cylinder(d = m2_insert_d, h = m2_insert_h + 1.0);\n            }\n        }\n\n        // G. 2x Optional Cherry MX Thumb-Click Switch Cutouts (14.0 x 14.0mm) Below Trackball\n        for (sx = [-10.5, 10.5]) {\n            translate([tball_cx + sx - mx_cutout_w/2, planck_y0 + 6.0, -2.0])\n                cube([mx_cutout_w, mx_cutout_w, base_top_h + 4.0]);\n            // Under-plate clearance for MX switch bottom housing & pins\n            translate([tball_cx + sx - 8.0, planck_y0 + 5.0, -12.0])\n                cube([16.0, 16.0, base_top_h + 12.0 - 1.5]);\n        }\n\n        // H. 8x M3 Perimeter Counterbored Mounting Holes (matching base_bottom bosses)\n        for (pt = base_boss_pts) {\n            translate([pt[0], pt[1], -tray_drop_z - eps])\n                cylinder(d = m3_thru_d, h = tray_drop_z + base_top_h + 2*eps);\n            translate([pt[0], pt[1], base_top_h - 2.0])\n                cylinder(d = m3_head_d, h = 2.0 + eps);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nbase_top_deck();\n",
  "battery_retainer.scad": "// ============================================================================\n// ns-conv: Nintendo Switch v1 (Erista) -> Clamshell Cyberdeck Conversion\n// File: cad/battery_retainer.scad\n// Part: Bolt-On Power Bank Retention Strap (Translucent Lilac SLA)\n// Purpose:\n//   Secures the INIU 45W Slim Power Bank (110 x 68 x 18.5 mm) inside the\n//   lower base enclosure over a 1.5mm EVA/Poron foam pad. Bolts into the two\n//   external M3 bosses located 4.5mm outside the battery casing so no screw\n//   ever approaches the lithium-polymer pouch.\n// ============================================================================\n\ninclude <config.scad>\n\nstrap_span_y = pbank_d + 1.0 + 2 * pbank_safe_gap; // 68 + 1 + 9 = 78.0 mm center-to-center\nstrap_w      = 18.0;\nstrap_t      = 3.0;\n\nmodule battery_retainer() {\n    difference() {\n        union() {\n            // Main flat bridge bar with rounded mounting ears\n            hull() {\n                for (sy = [-strap_span_y/2, strap_span_y/2]) {\n                    translate([0, sy, 0])\n                        cylinder(d = strap_w, h = strap_t);\n                }\n            }\n            // Side stiffener ribs along the bridge span\n            for (sx = [-strap_w/2 + 1.5, strap_w/2 - 3.3]) {\n                translate([sx, -pbank_d/2 + 2.0, strap_t - eps])\n                    cube([1.8, pbank_d - 4.0, 2.2]);\n            }\n        }\n\n        // 2x M3 Counterbored Mounting Holes at +-strap_span_y/2\n        for (sy = [-strap_span_y/2, strap_span_y/2]) {\n            translate([0, sy, -eps])\n                cylinder(d = m3_thru_d, h = strap_t + 4.0);\n            translate([0, sy, strap_t - 1.5])\n                cylinder(d = m3_head_d, h = 2.0);\n        }\n\n        // Weight-relief / ventilation slots in center of strap\n        for (sy = [-18.0, 0.0, 18.0]) {\n            translate([-4.0, sy - 4.5, -eps])\n                cube([8.0, 9.0, strap_t + 4.0]);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nbattery_retainer();\n",
  "cable_clamp.scad": "// ============================================================================\n// ns-conv: Nintendo Switch v1 (Erista) -> Clamshell Cyberdeck Conversion\n// File: cad/cable_clamp.scad\n// Part: USB-C Ribbon & Coupler Strain-Relief Clamps (2x Set, Translucent Lilac SLA)\n// Purpose:\n//   - Clamp A (x=0): Locks the 90-degree flat USB-C plug (CAB-01) into the\n//     Switch's bottom USB-C port inside lid_rear.scad so hinge motion never\n//     stresses the Switch's USB-C solder joints.\n//   - Clamp B (x=22): Retains the CAB-01 <-> HUB-01 coupler inside the rear\n//     base pocket (unclips with 2x M2 thumb/socket screws for RCM mode).\n// ============================================================================\n\ninclude <config.scad>\n\nclamp_span_x = 28.0; // Matches 2x M2 brass insert bosses at +-14.0mm\nclamp_w      = 10.0;\nclamp_h      = 4.5;\n\nmodule single_clamp(slot_w, slot_h) {\n    difference() {\n        hull() {\n            for (sx = [-clamp_span_x/2, clamp_span_x/2]) {\n                translate([sx, 0, 0])\n                    cylinder(d = clamp_w, h = clamp_h);\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Central cable / plug saddle cutout\n        translate([-slot_w/2, -clamp_w, -eps])\n            cube([slot_w, clamp_w * 2, slot_h + eps]);\n\n        // 2x M2 Mounting Screw Holes at +-14.0mm\n        for (sx = [-clamp_span_x/2, clamp_span_x/2]) {\n            translate([sx, 0, -eps])\n                cylinder(d = m2_thru_d, h = clamp_h + 2*eps);\n            translate([sx, 0, clamp_h - 1.5])\n                cylinder(d = m2_head_d, h = 1.6);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nmodule cable_clamp_pair() {\n    // Clamp A: Lid Switch 90-deg USB-C Plug Retainer\n    single_clamp(16.0, 2.2);\n\n    // Clamp B: Base Rear Coupler Retainer\n    translate([0, 16.0, 0])\n        single_clamp(14.5, 2.0);\n}\n\ncable_clamp_pair();\n",
  "config.scad": "// ============================================================================\n// ns-conv: Nintendo Switch v1 (Erista) -> Clamshell Cyberdeck Conversion\n// File: cad/config.scad\n// Purpose: Shared parametric configuration & single source of truth for all\n//          custom 3D-printed enclosure parts (JLC3DP SLA 8001 Translucent /\n//          PCBWay UTR-8100 Transparent).\n// Units: Millimeters (mm)\n// ============================================================================\n// NOTE: Every dimension marked with [USER_VERIFY] should be checked with\n// digital calipers against your physical hardware (see docs/teardown.md Part D)\n// before ordering the full enclosure print.\n// ============================================================================\n\n$fn = $preview ? 36 : 72;\neps = 0.02; // Boolean CSG overlap epsilon to guarantee 2-manifold meshes\n\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// 1. SLA MANUFACTURING & TOLERANCE PARAMETERS (JLC3DP SLA 8001 / PCBWay UTR-8100)\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nwall_thick        = 2.50;  // Nominal structural wall thickness (mm) for SLA rigidity & even lilac dye\nrib_thick         = 1.80;  // Internal stiffening rib thickness (~72% of wall_thick to prevent sink marks)\ncorner_r          = 5.00;  // Outer enclosure corner fillet radius (mm)\nchamfer_s         = 1.00;  // Edge break chamfer size (mm)\n\nsla_clear_slip    = 0.20;  // Per-side slip-fit clearance for drop-in PCBs and mating shell lips (mm)\nsla_clear_tight   = 0.10;  // Per-side snug locate clearance for bearings and switches (mm)\nsla_clear_insert  = 0.05;  // Per-side cold-press + CA glue clearance for knurled brass inserts in thermoset SLA\n\n// Metric Fasteners (M2, M2.5, M3, M4 \u2014 DIN 912 / ISO 7380 + DIN 934 Hex Nuts)\nm2_thru_d         = 2.30;  // M2 screw clearance hole diameter\nm2_head_d         = 4.20;  // M2 socket/button head counterbore diameter\nm2_nut_w          = 4.15;  // M2 DIN 934 hex nut flat-to-flat width (4.0mm nominal + 0.15mm SLA clearance)\nm2_nut_h          = 1.75;  // M2 hex nut trap depth\nm2_insert_d       = 3.15;  // M2x3x3.2mm knurled brass insert bore (cold-press + CA glue)\nm2_insert_h       = 3.50;  // M2 brass insert bore depth\n\nm3_thru_d         = 3.35;  // M3 screw clearance hole diameter\nm3_head_d         = 6.00;  // M3 socket/button head counterbore diameter\nm3_nut_w          = 5.65;  // M3 DIN 934 hex nut flat-to-flat width (5.5mm nominal + 0.15mm SLA clearance)\nm3_nut_h          = 2.55;  // M3 hex nut trap depth\nm3_insert_d       = 4.45;  // M3x4x4.5mm knurled brass insert bore (cold-press + CA glue)\nm3_insert_h       = 4.50;  // M3 brass insert bore depth\n\nm4_thru_d         = 4.35;  // M4 screw clearance hole for Southco E6 hinge leaves\n\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// 2. NINTENDO SWITCH v1 (MOD. HAC-001, 2017 ERISTA) CORE ASSEMBLY\n//    (Front Bezel + Digitizer + LCD + Magnesium Midframe + Mainboard + Fan +\n//     EMI Shield, with Rear Plastic Backplate & Joy-Con Side Rails Removed)\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nsw_core_w         = 166.50; // [USER_VERIFY] Width of Switch midframe/bezel without side Joy-Con rails (173.0mm w/ rails)\nsw_core_h         = 102.00; // [USER_VERIFY] Height of Switch tablet from bottom edge to top edge\nsw_core_thick     = 11.80;  // [USER_VERIFY] Thickness from front glass to rear aluminum EMI shield (13.9mm w/ plastic backplate)\n\nsw_screen_view_w  = 137.00; // Active 6.2\" LCD + touch margin opening width in lid bezel\nsw_screen_view_h  = 77.20;  // Active 6.2\" LCD + touch margin opening height in lid bezel\nsw_glass_w        = 161.20; // [USER_VERIFY] Front digitizer outer glass width\nsw_glass_h        = 94.20;  // [USER_VERIFY] Front digitizer outer glass height\n\n// 10x M2 Side-Rail Mounting Holes in Magnesium Midframe (5 Left, 5 Right)\n// Measured from bottom edge of Switch core (Y=0 at bottom edge of Switch)\nsw_rail_hole_y    = [12.00, 31.50, 51.00, 70.50, 90.00]; // [USER_VERIFY] 5x M2 hole Y positions (mm)\nsw_rail_hole_z    = 5.80;   // [USER_VERIFY] Z-distance from front glass surface to side M2 hole centers\n\n// Switch Bottom USB-C Port & 90-Degree Flat FPC Plug (CAB-01) Clearance\nsw_usbc_w         = 12.00;  // USB-C cutout width\nsw_usbc_plug_h    = 14.50;  // Vertical clearance below Switch bottom edge for 90-deg flat USB-C plug & strain clamp\nsw_usbc_plug_w    = 24.00;  // Width of 90-deg USB-C plug + clamp pocket\n\n// Switch Thermal Vents, Top Controls & Rear microSD Access\nsw_exhaust_x_off  = 11.00;  // [USER_VERIFY] Top radiator exhaust X offset from Switch centerline (+X = right)\nsw_exhaust_w      = 42.00;  // [USER_VERIFY] Top copper radiator exhaust width\nsw_exhaust_h      = 6.50;   // Top exhaust slot thickness\nsw_intake_x_span  = 74.00;  // [USER_VERIFY] Center-to-center span between the two lower-rear intake grilles\nsw_intake_y_off   = 18.00;  // [USER_VERIFY] Distance from Switch bottom edge to rear intake grilles\nsw_intake_w       = 20.00;  // Rear intake grille width each\nsw_intake_h       = 5.00;   // Rear intake grille height each\n\nsw_sd_x_off       = -51.00; // [USER_VERIFY] Rear microSDXC slot X offset from Switch center (-X = left when facing screen)\nsw_sd_y_off       = 26.00;  // [USER_VERIFY] Rear microSDXC slot Y height from Switch bottom edge\nsw_sd_win_w       = 20.00;  // Rear microSDXC access window width\nsw_sd_win_h       = 18.00;  // Rear microSDXC access window height\n\nsw_btn_pwr_x      = -58.00; // [USER_VERIFY] Top Power button X offset from Switch center\nsw_btn_vol_x      = -40.00; // [USER_VERIFY] Top Volume +/- rocker center X offset from Switch center\nsw_btn_vol_w      = 20.00;  // Volume rocker cutout width\nsw_audio_x        = 22.50;  // [USER_VERIFY] 3.5mm headphone jack X offset from Switch center\nsw_gamecard_x     = 44.00;  // [USER_VERIFY] Game Card slot X offset from Switch center\nsw_gamecard_w     = 31.00;  // Game Card slot cutout width\n\n// Recessed Momentary RCM Boot Tactile Button (RCM-01: 6x6x5mm switch)\nrcm_switch_w      = 6.30;   // Pocket width for 6x6mm tactile switch\nrcm_pinhole_d     = 3.20;   // Recessed actuator pinhole diameter (prevents accidental press)\n\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// 3. DROP x OLKB MIT PLANCK KEYBOARD (REV 6.x)\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nplanck_w          = 233.00; // [USER_VERIFY] Bare switch plate & PCB width (mm)\nplanck_d          = 81.00;  // [USER_VERIFY] Bare switch plate & PCB depth (mm)\nplanck_plate_t    = 1.50;   // [USER_VERIFY] Top metal switch plate thickness (mm)\nplanck_pcb_drop   = 10.50;  // [USER_VERIFY] Distance from underside of switch plate to lowest PCB component (hotswap/piezo)\nplanck_keycap_h   = 12.00;  // [USER_VERIFY] Keycap clearance height above switch plate when lid is closed\nplanck_lip_w      = 2.00;   // Perimeter shelf supporting the edges of the 233x81mm switch plate\n\n// OLKB Planck Rev 6 M2 Standoff Coordinates [x, y] measured from Front-Left corner of Planck\nplanck_mount_pts  = [\n    [21.50,  21.50],\n    [211.50, 21.50],\n    [21.50,  59.50],\n    [211.50, 59.50],\n    [116.50, 40.50]\n]; // [USER_VERIFY]\n\nplanck_usbc_x_off = 19.05;  // [USER_VERIFY] USB-C receptacle X offset from left edge of Planck PCB\n\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// 4. TRACKBALL SUBSYSTEM (PER-01: 38.0mm Ball + Ploopy Nano 2 / PMW3360 + MR63ZZ)\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\ntball_d           = 38.00;  // Standard 1.5-inch snooker/trackball diameter (mm)\ntball_cup_clear   = 0.65;   // Radial clearance between 38mm ball and socket cup wall\ntball_bearing_od  = 6.00;   // MR63ZZ bearing outer diameter (3x6x2.5mm)\ntball_bearing_id  = 3.00;   // MR63ZZ bearing bore diameter\ntball_bearing_w   = 2.50;   // MR63ZZ bearing width\ntball_bearing_ang = 35.0;   // Elevation angle of the 3 roller bearings from bottom pole (deg)\ntball_sensor_w    = 28.50;  // PMW3360 breakout / Ploopy Nano PCB pocket width\ntball_sensor_d    = 22.00;  // PMW3360 breakout pocket depth\ntball_lens_gap    = 2.40;   // PMW3360 optical lens working distance below bottom of 38mm ball\nmx_cutout_w       = 14.00;  // Standard 14.0 x 14.0mm Cherry MX switch cutout for thumb click buttons\n\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// 5. POWER BANK (PWR-01: INIU 45W SLIM) & USB-C PD HUB (HUB-01: UGREEN 105)\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Default Preset: INIU Carry P50-E1 / BI-B62 45W Slim (10,000 mAh, 15V/3A PD)\npbank_w           = 110.00; // [USER_VERIFY] Power bank length (mm) \u2014 Set to 134.0 for Baseus Blade HD\npbank_d           = 68.00;  // [USER_VERIFY] Power bank width (mm)  \u2014 Set to 134.0 for Baseus Blade HD\npbank_h           = 18.50;  // [USER_VERIFY] Power bank thickness (mm) \u2014 Set to 18.0 for Baseus Blade HD\npbank_foam_t      = 1.50;   // EVA/Poron shock & thermal isolation foam thickness\npbank_safe_gap    = 4.50;   // Mandatory safety clearance from battery wall to any M3 fastener boss\n\nhub_w             = 115.00; // [USER_VERIFY] UGREEN Revodok 105 / Baseus 5-in-1 100W PD Hub length (mm)\nhub_d             = 27.50;  // [USER_VERIFY] Hub width (mm)\nhub_h             = 12.20;  // [USER_VERIFY] Hub height (mm)\n\n// Rear Panel-Mount USB-C Socket (CAB-03)\npanel_usbc_hole_w = 9.40;   // USB-C receptacle nose cutout width\npanel_usbc_hole_h = 3.60;   // USB-C receptacle nose cutout height\npanel_usbc_span   = 16.00;  // M2/M3 mounting ear center-to-center pitch\n\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// 6. ADJUSTABLE FRICTION TORQUE HINGES (MEC-01: SOUTHCO E6-10-301-20 / CL226)\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nhinge_w           = 42.90;  // [USER_VERIFY] Hinge width along hinge axis (mm)\nhinge_d           = 36.50;  // [USER_VERIFY] Total open leaf span perpendicular to axis (mm)\nhinge_knuckle_d   = 12.70;  // [USER_VERIFY] Hinge barrel diameter / thickness (mm)\nhinge_leaf_t      = 3.20;   // Hinge leaf thickness (mm)\nhinge_hole_span_x = 25.40;  // [USER_VERIFY] Horizontal mounting hole pitch on each leaf (1.00 inch)\nhinge_hole_span_y = 19.10;  // [USER_VERIFY] Distance between base leaf holes and lid leaf holes (0.75 inch)\nhinge_x_offset    = 96.00;  // Distance from deck centerline (X=0) to Left (-96) and Right (+96) hinge centers\n\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// 7. OVERALL CLAMSHELL ENCLOSURE ENVELOPE (DERIVED AUTOMATICALLY)\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// X-Axis (Width): Left Margin (10) + Planck (233) + Divider (7) + Trackball Zone (48) + Right Margin (8) = 306.0 mm\ndeck_w            = 306.00;\n// Y-Axis (Depth): Front Wrist Bevel (16) + Planck (81) + Rear Deck/USB-C Zone (47) + Hinge Spine (18) = 162.0 mm\ndeck_d            = 162.00;\n\n// Layout Coordinates in Base Deck (Origin [0,0,0] = Center-X, Front-Y=0, Bottom-Z=0)\nplanck_x0         = -deck_w/2 + 10.00; // Left X edge of Planck cutout (-143.0 mm)\nplanck_y0         = 16.00;             // Front Y edge of Planck cutout (+16.0 mm from front edge)\n\ntball_cx          = planck_x0 + planck_w + 31.00; // Trackball X center (+121.0 mm)\ntball_cy          = planck_y0 + 52.00;            // Trackball Y center (+68.0 mm)\n\n// Z-Axis Heights\nbase_bottom_h     = 24.50;  // Lower base tub height (2.5mm floor + 20.0mm battery/hub cavity + 2.0mm lip)\nbase_top_h        = 4.00;   // Top deck plate visible flange thickness (total base height = 28.50 mm)\nbase_total_h      = base_bottom_h + base_top_h;\n\nlid_rear_h        = 15.00;  // Upper lid rear shell height (2.5mm back + 12.5mm Switch core & 90-deg USB-C cavity)\nlid_bezel_h       = 3.00;   // Upper lid front bezel retainer flange thickness (total lid height = 18.00 mm)\nlid_total_h       = lid_rear_h + lid_bezel_h;\n\n// Switch Core Placement in Upper Lid (Centered on X=0, Y positioned above 90-deg USB-C channel)\nsw_center_x       = 0.00;   // Switch centered horizontally in lid for balanced hinge torque\nsw_bottom_y       = 26.00;  // Distance from hinge-side bottom edge of lid to Switch bottom edge\n\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// 8. SHARED UTILITY MODULES\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n// Rounded rectangular prism centered in X, starting at Y=0, Z=0\nmodule rounded_box_xcenter(w, d, h, r) {\n    hull() {\n        for (sx = [-1, 1], sy = [0, 1]) {\n            translate([sx * (w/2 - r), r + sy * (d - 2*r), 0])\n                cylinder(r = r, h = h);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// Standard DIN 934 Hex Nut Trap (flat-to-flat width w, depth h)\nmodule hex_nut_trap(flat_w, depth) {\n    cylinder(d = flat_w / cos(30), h = depth, $fn = 6);\n}\n",
  "lid_bezel.scad": "// ============================================================================\n// ns-conv: Nintendo Switch v1 (Erista) -> Clamshell Cyberdeck Conversion\n// File: cad/lid_bezel.scad\n// Part: Upper Lid Front Bezel Retainer (Translucent Lilac SLA)\n// Features:\n//   - Full-width front bezel plate (306 x 162 x 3.0 mm) that frames the\n//     Nintendo Switch v1 6.2\" capacitive touchscreen & ambient light sensor\n//   - Captures the Switch front glass perimeter cleanly without adhesives\n//   - Includes dual speaker acoustic slots aligned with the Switch's front\n//     stereo speakers\n//   - 8x M3 counterbored perimeter mounting holes matching lid_rear.scad\n//   - 6x \u00d86.2 x 0.8mm shallow recesses for 6x1.5mm silicone closure bumpers\n//     so the lid rests gently on the base deck rim without touching keycaps\n// ============================================================================\n\ninclude <config.scad>\n\nlid_boss_pts = [\n    [-deck_w/2 + 6.5,  12.0],\n    [ deck_w/2 - 6.5,  12.0],\n    [-deck_w/2 + 6.5,  81.0],\n    [ deck_w/2 - 6.5,  81.0],\n    [-deck_w/2 + 6.5,  deck_d - 8.0],\n    [-80.0,            deck_d - 8.0],\n    [ 80.0,            deck_d - 8.0],\n    [ deck_w/2 - 6.5,  deck_d - 8.0]\n];\n\nbumper_pts = [\n    [-deck_w/2 + 16.0, 22.0],\n    [ deck_w/2 - 16.0, 22.0],\n    [-deck_w/2 + 16.0, deck_d - 16.0],\n    [ 0.0,             deck_d - 16.0],\n    [ deck_w/2 - 16.0, deck_d - 16.0],\n    [ 0.0,             14.0]\n];\n\nmodule lid_bezel() {\n    sw_center_y = sw_bottom_y + sw_core_h/2;\n\n    difference() {\n        union() {\n            // 1. Main Front Bezel Plate (306 x 162 x 3.0 mm)\n            rounded_box_xcenter(deck_w, deck_d, lid_bezel_h, corner_r);\n\n            // 2. Inner Engagement Rim around Switch Front Glass Perimeter (1.2mm lip)\n            translate([\n                sw_center_x - (sw_glass_w + 4.0)/2,\n                sw_center_y - (sw_glass_h + 4.0)/2,\n                -1.2\n            ])\n                difference() {\n                    cube([sw_glass_w + 4.0, sw_glass_h + 4.0, 1.2 + eps]);\n                    translate([2.2, 2.2, -eps])\n                        cube([sw_glass_w - 0.4, sw_glass_h - 0.4, 1.2 + 3*eps]);\n                }\n        }\n\n        // ====================================================================\n        // SUBTRACTIONS (Touchscreen Window, Speaker Slots, M3 Screws, Bumpers)\n        // ====================================================================\n\n        // A. Active 6.2\" Touchscreen + Bezel Viewing Window (144 x 83 mm with 45-deg bevel)\n        translate([\n            sw_center_x - (sw_screen_view_w + 6.0)/2,\n            sw_center_y - (sw_screen_view_h + 5.0)/2,\n            -2.0\n        ])\n            cube([sw_screen_view_w + 6.0, sw_screen_view_h + 5.0, lid_bezel_h + 4.0]);\n\n        // B. Front Stereo Speaker Acoustic Port Slots + Ambient Light Sensor Window\n        for (sx = [-1, 1]) {\n            translate([sw_center_x + sx * 52.0 - 7.0, sw_bottom_y + 4.5, -2.0])\n                cube([14.0, 3.0, lid_bezel_h + 4.0]);\n        }\n        // Ambient light sensor aperture (bottom-left of bezel)\n        translate([sw_center_x - 71.0, sw_bottom_y + 11.0, -2.0])\n            cylinder(d = 5.0, h = lid_bezel_h + 4.0);\n\n        // C. Hinge Leaf Clearance Cutouts at Bottom Spine (Y = 0..16mm)\n        for (hx = [-hinge_x_offset, hinge_x_offset]) {\n            translate([hx - (hinge_w + 1.0)/2, -eps, -2.0])\n                cube([hinge_w + 1.0, 16.5, lid_bezel_h + 4.0]);\n        }\n\n        // D. 8x M3 Counterbored Perimeter Mounting Screw Holes\n        for (pt = lid_boss_pts) {\n            translate([pt[0], pt[1], -2.0])\n                cylinder(d = m3_thru_d, h = lid_bezel_h + 4.0);\n            translate([pt[0], pt[1], lid_bezel_h - 1.6])\n                cylinder(d = m3_head_d, h = 1.6 + eps);\n        }\n\n        // E. 6x \u00d86.2 x 0.8mm Silicone Lid Bumper Seats on Front Face\n        for (bp = bumper_pts) {\n            translate([bp[0], bp[1], lid_bezel_h - 0.8])\n                cylinder(d = 6.3, h = 0.8 + eps);\n        }\n\n        // F. Trackball Parking Clearance Aperture in Right Wing (X = +tball_cx, Y = deck_d - tball_cy)\n        //    Allows the protruding top of the 38mm trackball to nest inside the right\n        //    wing of the lid when the clamshell is folded closed (0 deg)!\n        translate([tball_cx, deck_d - tball_cy, -2.0])\n            cylinder(d = tball_d + 4.0, h = lid_bezel_h + 4.0);\n    }\n}\n\nlid_bezel();\n",
  "lid_rear.scad": "// ============================================================================\n// ns-conv: Nintendo Switch v1 (Erista) -> Clamshell Cyberdeck Conversion\n// File: cad/lid_rear.scad\n// Part: Upper Lid Rear Shell (Translucent Lilac SLA)\n// Features:\n//   - Full-width clamshell lid (306 x 162 x 15.0 mm) with 2.5mm uniform walls\n//   - Precision central cradle for the intact Nintendo Switch v1 Core Assembly\n//     (166.5 x 102.0 x 11.8 mm \u2014 LCD + Digitizer + Magnesium Midframe +\n//     Mainboard + Fan + 4310mAh Battery)\n//   - 10x M2 Side-Rail Structural Mounting Holes (5 Left + 5 Right) aligned\n//     with the factory Joy-Con rail screw bosses on the Switch midframe\n//   - Diagonal X-truss stiffening ribs (1.8mm thick) linking the two Southco\n//     E6-10-301-20 hinge pads directly to the Switch core cradle\n//   - Unobstructed OEM Rear Fan Intake Louvers, Top Radiator Exhaust Channel,\n//     Rear microSDXC Access Window, Top Controls (Power, Vol+/-, Audio,\n//     Game Card), and Recessed Right-Side RCM Boot Tactile Switch Pocket\n//   - Bottom 90-Degree Flat USB-C (CAB-01) Strain-Relief Channel & Clamp Bosses\n// ============================================================================\n\ninclude <config.scad>\n\n// Coordinate system for lid_rear (printed flat on its outer back face Z=0):\n// X=0 at center, Y=0 at hinge edge (bottom of lid), Y=deck_d at top edge of lid,\n// Z=0 at outer rear surface of lid, Z=lid_rear_h (15.0mm) at inner bezel mating rim.\n\nlid_boss_pts = [\n    [-deck_w/2 + 6.5,  12.0],\n    [ deck_w/2 - 6.5,  12.0],\n    [-deck_w/2 + 6.5,  81.0],\n    [ deck_w/2 - 6.5,  81.0],\n    [-deck_w/2 + 6.5,  deck_d - 8.0],\n    [-80.0,            deck_d - 8.0],\n    [ 80.0,            deck_d - 8.0],\n    [ deck_w/2 - 6.5,  deck_d - 8.0]\n];\n\nmodule lid_rear() {\n    difference() {\n        union() {\n            // 1. Outer Lid Tub (306 x 162 x 15.0 mm)\n            difference() {\n                rounded_box_xcenter(deck_w, deck_d, lid_rear_h, corner_r);\n\n                // Exterior rear perimeter aesthetic bevel along top/left/right edges\n                // (Gives a sleek laptop profile while keeping uniform wall thickness)\n                translate([0, wall_thick, wall_thick])\n                    rounded_box_xcenter(\n                        deck_w - 2*wall_thick,\n                        deck_d - 2*wall_thick,\n                        lid_rear_h,\n                        corner_r - wall_thick\n                    );\n            }\n\n            // 2. Central Nintendo Switch v1 Core Cradle Walls (Left, Right, Bottom, Top)\n            //    Left & Right structural rail walls are 4.5mm thick to house the\n            //    10x M2 counterbored side bolts into the Switch magnesium midframe!\n            sw_pocket_w = sw_core_w + 2*sla_clear_slip; // 166.90 mm\n            sw_pocket_h = sw_core_h + 2*sla_clear_slip; // 102.40 mm\n            rail_wall_t = 4.50;\n\n            translate([\n                sw_center_x - sw_pocket_w/2 - rail_wall_t,\n                sw_bottom_y - wall_thick,\n                wall_thick - eps\n            ])\n                difference() {\n                    cube([\n                        sw_pocket_w + 2*rail_wall_t,\n                        sw_pocket_h + 2*wall_thick,\n                        lid_rear_h - wall_thick + eps\n                    ]);\n                    // Inner Switch core pocket\n                    translate([rail_wall_t, wall_thick, -eps])\n                        cube([sw_pocket_w, sw_pocket_h, lid_rear_h + 2*eps]);\n                }\n\n            // 3. Structural Load-Transfer Ribs from Hinge Pads to Switch Cradle\n            //    (1.8mm thick ribs transfer hinge torque smoothly across the SLA lid)\n            for (sx = [-1, 1]) {\n                // Hinge mounting block at Y=0..18mm\n                translate([sx * hinge_x_offset - (hinge_w + 6.0)/2, wall_thick - eps, wall_thick - eps])\n                    cube([hinge_w + 6.0, 16.0, lid_rear_h - wall_thick + eps]);\n\n                // Vertical and diagonal ribs into Switch side rail wall\n                hull() {\n                    translate([sx * hinge_x_offset - rib_thick/2, 16.0, wall_thick - eps])\n                        cylinder(d = rib_thick, h = lid_rear_h - wall_thick - 2.0 + eps);\n                    translate([sx * (sw_pocket_w/2 + rail_wall_t/2), sw_bottom_y + 15.0, wall_thick - eps])\n                        cylinder(d = rib_thick, h = lid_rear_h - wall_thick - 2.0 + eps);\n                }\n                hull() {\n                    translate([sx * (deck_w/2 - wall_thick - 2.0), 45.0, wall_thick - eps])\n                        cylinder(d = rib_thick, h = lid_rear_h - wall_thick - 2.0 + eps);\n                    translate([sx * (sw_pocket_w/2 + rail_wall_t/2), sw_bottom_y + 45.0, wall_thick - eps])\n                        cylinder(d = rib_thick, h = lid_rear_h - wall_thick - 2.0 + eps);\n                }\n                hull() {\n                    translate([sx * (deck_w/2 - wall_thick - 2.0), 105.0, wall_thick - eps])\n                        cylinder(d = rib_thick, h = lid_rear_h - wall_thick - 2.0 + eps);\n                    translate([sx * (sw_pocket_w/2 + rail_wall_t/2), sw_bottom_y + 85.0, wall_thick - eps])\n                        cylinder(d = rib_thick, h = lid_rear_h - wall_thick - 2.0 + eps);\n                }\n            }\n\n            // 4. 2x M2 Brass-Insert Standoffs for 90-Degree USB-C Strain-Relief Clamp (CAB-01)\n            for (sx = [-14.0, 14.0]) {\n                translate([sw_center_x + sx, sw_bottom_y - 11.0, wall_thick])\n                    cylinder(d = 6.5, h = 6.5);\n            }\n\n            // 5. Recessed Momentary RCM Boot Tactile Switch Holder (Right of Switch Cradle)\n            translate([sw_center_x + sw_pocket_w/2 + rail_wall_t - 0.5, sw_bottom_y + 78.0, wall_thick])\n                cube([10.0, 12.0, 9.0]);\n\n            // 6. 8x M3 Perimeter Bosses for Front Bezel Retainer (lid_bezel.scad)\n            for (pt = lid_boss_pts) {\n                translate([pt[0], pt[1], wall_thick])\n                    cylinder(d = 8.0, h = lid_rear_h - wall_thick);\n            }\n        }\n\n        // ====================================================================\n        // SUBTRACTIONS (10x Midframe Bolts, Vents, SD Window, USB-C, Hinges)\n        // ====================================================================\n        sw_pocket_w = sw_core_w + 2*sla_clear_slip;\n        sw_pocket_h = sw_core_h + 2*sla_clear_slip;\n        rail_wall_t = 4.50;\n\n        // A. 10x M2 Side-Rail Structural Mounting Holes (5 Left + 5 Right)\n        //    Screws pass horizontally through the cradle side walls into the\n        //    Switch's factory M2 Joy-Con rail threads!\n        //    Also includes outer side-access clearance holes for long M2 hex driver.\n        for (ry = sw_rail_hole_y) {\n            hole_y = sw_bottom_y + sla_clear_slip + ry;\n            hole_z = lid_rear_h - sw_rail_hole_z; // Measured down from front glass plane\n\n            // Left & Right Cradle Wall M2 Clearance Holes + Head Counterbores\n            for (sx = [-1, 1]) {\n                translate([sw_center_x + sx * (sw_pocket_w/2 - 1.0), hole_y, hole_z])\n                    rotate([0, sx * 90, 0]) {\n                        cylinder(d = m2_thru_d, h = rail_wall_t + 3.0);\n                        translate([0, 0, rail_wall_t - 1.2])\n                            cylinder(d = m2_head_d, h = 20.0);\n                    }\n            }\n        }\n\n        // B. Switch Bottom 90-Degree Flat USB-C Plug (CAB-01) Channel & Hinge Exit\n        translate([sw_center_x - sw_usbc_plug_w/2, -eps, wall_thick])\n            cube([sw_usbc_plug_w, sw_bottom_y + 4.0, lid_rear_h]);\n        // Hinge exit slot at bottom spine (Y = 0)\n        translate([sw_center_x - 11.0, -eps, wall_thick + 2.0])\n            cube([22.0, wall_thick + 4.0, lid_rear_h]);\n        // 2x M2 Brass Insert bores for USB-C Strain-Relief Clamp\n        for (sx = [-14.0, 14.0]) {\n            translate([sw_center_x + sx, sw_bottom_y - 11.0, wall_thick + 6.5 - m2_insert_h])\n                cylinder(d = m2_insert_d, h = m2_insert_h + eps);\n        }\n\n        // C. OEM-Aligned Rear Fan Intake Louvers (2x 20x5mm slotted grilles)\n        for (sx = [-1, 1]) {\n            gx = sw_center_x + sx * (sw_intake_x_span / 2);\n            gy = sw_bottom_y + sw_intake_y_off;\n            for (slot = [-2 : 2]) {\n                translate([gx + slot * 3.6 - 1.0, gy - sw_intake_h/2, -eps])\n                    cube([2.0, sw_intake_h, wall_thick + 2*eps]);\n            }\n        }\n\n        // D. Top Copper Radiator Active Fan Exhaust Channel & Top Edge Louver\n        //    Routes hot air from top of Switch core straight out the top edge of the lid!\n        ex_x = sw_center_x + sw_exhaust_x_off - sw_exhaust_w/2;\n        translate([ex_x, sw_bottom_y + sw_core_h - 2.0, wall_thick + 2.0])\n            cube([sw_exhaust_w, deck_d - (sw_bottom_y + sw_core_h) + 4.0, sw_exhaust_h + 2.0]);\n        // Rear exhaust relief slots directly above radiator\n        for (i = [0 : 7]) {\n            translate([ex_x + 3.0 + i * 5.0, sw_bottom_y + sw_core_h - 4.0, -eps])\n                cube([2.8, 12.0, wall_thick + 2*eps]);\n        }\n\n        // E. Rear microSDXC Card Access Window (Bevelled slot so card can be swapped anytime)\n        translate([\n            sw_center_x + sw_sd_x_off - sw_sd_win_w/2,\n            sw_bottom_y + sw_sd_y_off - sw_sd_win_h/2,\n            -eps\n        ])\n            cube([sw_sd_win_w, sw_sd_win_h, wall_thick + 2*eps]);\n\n        // F. Top Control Cutouts (Power, Volume +/-, 3.5mm Audio Jack, Game Card Slot)\n        //    Direct finger access channels from the top edge of the Switch core to top of lid\n        // 1. Power + Volume Rocker Access Recess\n        translate([sw_center_x + sw_btn_pwr_x - 8.0, sw_bottom_y + sw_core_h - 2.0, wall_thick])\n            cube([38.0, deck_d - (sw_bottom_y + sw_core_h) + 2.0, lid_rear_h]);\n        // 2. 3.5mm Headphone + Game Card Access Recess\n        translate([sw_center_x + sw_audio_x - 6.0, sw_bottom_y + sw_core_h - 2.0, wall_thick])\n            cube([46.0, deck_d - (sw_bottom_y + sw_core_h) + 2.0, lid_rear_h]);\n\n        // G. Recessed Momentary RCM Boot Tactile Switch Pocket (6.3 x 6.3mm + \u00d83.2mm Pinhole)\n        //    Located on the rear-right of the Switch cradle (Y = sw_bottom_y + 84mm)\n        translate([sw_center_x + sw_pocket_w/2 + rail_wall_t + 1.5, sw_bottom_y + 81.0, wall_thick + 1.5])\n            cube([rcm_switch_w, rcm_switch_w, 8.0]);\n        // Wire slot into Right Joy-Con rail channel\n        translate([sw_center_x + sw_pocket_w/2 - 1.0, sw_bottom_y + 82.5, wall_thick + 2.0])\n            cube([rail_wall_t + 4.0, 3.5, 6.0]);\n        // Recessed rear pinhole so you can hold RCM at boot without accidental bumps\n        translate([\n            sw_center_x + sw_pocket_w/2 + rail_wall_t + 1.5 + rcm_switch_w/2,\n            sw_bottom_y + 81.0 + rcm_switch_w/2,\n            -eps\n        ])\n            cylinder(d = rcm_pinhole_d, h = wall_thick + 2.0);\n\n        // H. Left & Right Southco E6-10-301-20 Hinge Leaf Seats & M3/M4 Mounting Bores\n        for (hx = [-hinge_x_offset, hinge_x_offset]) {\n            // Hinge leaf pocket on inner bottom spine (Y = 0..16mm)\n            translate([hx - (hinge_w + 0.5)/2, -eps, lid_rear_h - hinge_leaf_t])\n                cube([hinge_w + 0.5, 16.5, hinge_leaf_t + eps]);\n            // 2x M3/M4 Mounting Bores + Outer Rear Hex-Nut Traps\n            for (dx = [-hinge_hole_span_x/2, hinge_hole_span_x/2]) {\n                translate([hx + dx, 8.5, -eps]) {\n                    cylinder(d = m3_thru_d + 0.2, h = lid_rear_h + 2*eps);\n                    hex_nut_trap(m3_nut_w + 0.1, m3_nut_h + 0.5);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        // I. 8x M3 Perimeter Brass Insert Bores for Front Bezel Retainer (lid_bezel.scad)\n        for (pt = lid_boss_pts) {\n            translate([pt[0], pt[1], lid_rear_h - m3_insert_h])\n                cylinder(d = m3_insert_d, h = m3_insert_h + eps);\n            translate([pt[0], pt[1], wall_thick])\n                cylinder(d = m3_thru_d, h = lid_rear_h);\n        }\n\n        // J. Spherical Trackball Parking Pocket in Right Wing when Lid is Closed\n        //    Leaves a full 2.5mm solid outer rear wall (Z = 2.5mm)\n        translate([tball_cx, deck_d - tball_cy, lid_rear_h + 8.0])\n            sphere(d = tball_d + 3.0);\n    }\n}\n\nlid_rear();\n",
  "test_fit_jig.scad": "// ============================================================================\n// ns-conv: Nintendo Switch v1 (Erista) -> Clamshell Cyberdeck Conversion\n// File: cad/test_fit_jig.scad\n// Part: Pre-Order Calibration & Test-Fit Gauge Jig (Print First!)\n// Purpose:\n//   A compact (~18g, <3 EUR) test coupon that verifies all 5 critical\n//   mechanical interfaces before committing to the full 306x162mm shells:\n//     1. Switch v1 Side-Rail M2 Hole Pitch Gauge (12.0, 31.5, 51.0, 70.5, 90.0mm)\n//        and Switch Core Thickness Slot (11.80mm + 0.20mm clearance)\n//     2. Drop x MIT Planck Corner Ledge + M2 Standoff Offset (21.5 x 21.5mm)\n//     3. Southco E6-10-301-20 Hinge Leaf Footprint & Hole Pitch (25.4 x 19.1mm)\n//     4. 38.0mm Trackball + MR63ZZ Bearing Seat Fit Coupon\n//     5. Thermoset SLA Fastener Tolerance Ladder (M2/M3 Brass Insert & Hex Nut\n//        test bores at -0.05mm, 0.00mm nominal, and +0.05mm)\n// ============================================================================\n\ninclude <config.scad>\n\nmodule test_fit_jig() {\n    difference() {\n        union() {\n            // 1. Main L-Shaped Calibration Coupon Base (105 x 55 x 5.0 mm)\n            cube([105.0, 55.0, 5.0]);\n\n            // 2. Switch Core Thickness Caliper U-Jaw at Left End (Tests 11.8mm + 2*0.2mm = 12.2mm)\n            translate([0, 0, 5.0 - eps])\n                difference() {\n                    cube([18.0, 24.0, 12.0]);\n                    translate([3.0, -eps, -eps])\n                        cube([sw_core_thick + 2*sla_clear_slip, 24.0 + 2*eps, 12.5]);\n                }\n\n            // 3. Planck Corner Support Ledge Coupon (Top-Right of Jig)\n            translate([60.0, 20.0, 5.0 - eps])\n                difference() {\n                    cube([45.0, 35.0, 5.0]);\n                    // Planck switch plate corner recess\n                    translate([5.0, 5.0, 5.0 - (planck_plate_t + 0.5)])\n                        cube([40.0 + eps, 30.0 + eps, planck_plate_t + 1.0]);\n                    // Inner PCB drop clearance (leaving 2.0mm support shelf)\n                    translate([5.0 + planck_lip_w, 5.0 + planck_lip_w, -eps])\n                        cube([40.0, 30.0, 3.5]);\n                }\n            // Planck M2 Standoff Boss at exact (21.5, 21.5) offset from corner\n            translate([60.0 + 5.0 + 21.5, 20.0 + 5.0 + 21.5, 5.0 - eps])\n                cylinder(d = 7.0, h = 5.0 - (planck_plate_t + 0.5));\n        }\n\n        // A. 5x Switch v1 Side-Rail M2 Pitch Verification Holes along Y=8.0mm edge\n        //    (Positions: X = 12.0, 31.5, 51.0, 70.5, 90.0 mm)\n        for (rx = sw_rail_hole_y) {\n            translate([rx, 8.0, -eps])\n                cylinder(d = m2_thru_d, h = 10.0);\n        }\n\n        // B. Planck Corner M2 Through-Hole + Underside Hex Nut Trap at (86.5, 46.5)\n        translate([60.0 + 5.0 + 21.5, 20.0 + 5.0 + 21.5, -eps]) {\n            cylinder(d = m2_thru_d, h = 15.0);\n            hex_nut_trap(m2_nut_w, m2_nut_h + eps);\n        }\n\n        // C. Southco E6-10-301-20 Hinge Hole Pitch Test Pattern (25.4 x 19.1 mm)\n        for (dx = [0, hinge_hole_span_x], dy = [0, hinge_hole_span_y]) {\n            translate([24.0 + dx, 24.0 + dy, -eps]) {\n                cylinder(d = m3_thru_d + 0.2, h = 10.0);\n                hex_nut_trap(m3_nut_w, m3_nut_h + eps);\n            }\n        }\n\n        // D. Single MR63ZZ (3x6x2.5mm) Roller Bearing Test Seat at (52.0, 35.0)\n        translate([52.0, 35.0, 5.0]) {\n            rotate([0, 90, 0])\n                cylinder(d = tball_bearing_od + 0.5, h = tball_bearing_w + 0.5, center = true);\n            rotate([0, 90, 0])\n                cylinder(d = tball_bearing_id + 0.1, h = 10.0, center = true);\n        }\n\n        // E. SLA Thermoset Insert & Nut Tolerance Ladder (-0.05, 0.00, +0.05mm)\n        for (i = [-1, 0, 1]) {\n            delta = i * 0.05;\n            // M2 Brass Insert test bores\n            translate([30.0 + (i + 1) * 9.0, 15.0, 5.0 - m2_insert_h])\n                cylinder(d = m2_insert_d + delta, h = m2_insert_h + eps);\n            // M3 Brass Insert test bores\n            translate([62.0 + (i + 1) * 11.0, 13.0, 5.0 - m3_insert_h])\n                cylinder(d = m3_insert_d + delta, h = m3_insert_h + eps);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\ntest_fit_jig();\n"
};
